   "id": "cell-000",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# WILDSPEECH P01 — Literacy Signal Discovery\n",
    "\n",
    "Problem-oriented discovery of literacy-related signal in anonymised child speech, from data integrity to a validated feature-discovery and hypothesis registry.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Execution policy.** Nothing runs automatically. Every expensive step is guarded by a flag that defaults to `False`. Cloud processing stays disabled until you set `cloud_storage_authorized=True` after confirming that your environment complies with the competition data-use agreement. No data is sent to external APIs.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Order of use:** (1) write/locate the package, (2) optional installs, (3) configure, (4) initialise context, (5) run sections individually or the full pipeline at the end."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## A. Package bootstrap\n",
    "\n",
    "The cells in this section write the `wildspeech` package to `CODE_ROOT`. If you already copied the repository (zip or Git), set `CODE_ROOT` to it and **skip the `%%writefile` cells** (they only overwrite source files; they never touch data)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-002",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "ename": "",
     "evalue": "",
     "output_type": "error",
     "traceback": [
      "\u001b[1;31mRunning cells with 'casmi (Python 3.10.21)' requires the ipykernel package.\n",
      "\u001b[1;31m<a href='command:jupyter.createPythonEnvAndSelectController'>Create a Python Environment</a> with the required packages.\n",
      "\u001b[1;31mOr install 'ipykernel' using the command: 'conda install -n casmi ipykernel --update-deps --force-reinstall'"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import os, sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "CODE_ROOT = Path(\"/content/WildSpeech_code\") if \"google.colab\" in sys.modules else Path.cwd() / \"WildSpeech_code\"\n",
    "for sub in (\"src/wildspeech\", \"configs\", \"tests\", \"tools\"):\n",
    "    (CODE_ROOT / sub).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "if str(CODE_ROOT / \"src\") not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(CODE_ROOT / \"src\"))\n",
    "print(\"CODE_ROOT =\", CODE_ROOT)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-003",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/__init__.py\n",
    "\"\"\"WildSpeech P01: problem-oriented literacy speech signal discovery.\n",
    "\n",
    "The package is organised as reusable modules, one per scientific section, plus\n",
    "infrastructure (configuration, paths, logging, artifact storage and a\n",
    "dependency-aware stage orchestrator). Importing the package never triggers\n",
    "data access, downloads, extraction, model training or any other expensive\n",
    "operation; work only happens when a stage is executed explicitly.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n",
    "PACKAGE_NAME = \"wildspeech\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-004",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/ablation.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 20 - predictive feature-family ablation.\n",
    "\n",
    "A controlled experiment matrix (A00-A23) evaluated with student-disjoint CV\n",
    "(repeated student K-fold and school-grouped K-fold), conservative model\n",
    "settings, nested supervised selection inside the model pipeline and paired\n",
    "bootstrap comparisons. Unavailable modalities are reported as skipped and\n",
    "never replaced with invented data.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "from .baseline_models import ModelUnavailable, make_fit_predict, model_available\n",
    "from .families import AUDIO_FAMILIES, TABULAR_FAMILIES, modeling_columns\n",
    "from .validation import available_schemes, paired_bootstrap_delta, pooled_predictions, run_cv\n",
    "\n",
    "TAB = list(TABULAR_FAMILIES)\n",
    "AUDIO_CORE = [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\", \"PHONETIC\", \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\",\n",
    "              \"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\", \"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\", \"CROSS_TASK\", \"EMBEDDINGS\"]\n",
    "EXPERIMENTS = {\n",
    "    \"A00_TARGET_MEAN\": [],\n",
    "    \"A01_THETA_ONLY\": [\"SCREENING\"],\n",
    "    \"A02_THETA_CORRECTNESS\": [\"SCREENING\", \"CORRECTNESS\"],\n",
    "    \"A03_THETA_ITEM_DIFFICULTY\": [\"SCREENING\", \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\"],\n",
    "    \"A04_THETA_ADAPTIVE_BEHAVIOR\": [\"SCREENING\", \"ADAPTIVE\"],\n",
    "    \"A05_COMPLETE_TABULAR\": TAB,\n",
    "    \"A06_TABULAR_TEMPORAL\": TAB + [\"TEMPORAL\"],\n",
    "    \"A07_TABULAR_SPECTRAL\": TAB + [\"SPECTRAL\"],\n",
    "    \"A08_TABULAR_MFCC\": TAB + [\"MFCC\"],\n",
    "    \"A09_TABULAR_WAVELETS\": TAB + [\"WAVELETS\"],\n",
    "    \"A10_TABULAR_PROSODY\": TAB + [\"PROSODY\"],\n",
    "    \"A11_TABULAR_PHONETIC\": TAB + [\"PHONETIC\"],\n",
    "    \"A12_TABULAR_ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\": TAB + [\"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\", \"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\", \"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\"],\n",
    "    \"A13_TABULAR_MULTIMODAL\": TAB + AUDIO_CORE,\n",
    "    \"A14_TABULAR_LITERACY_INDICES\": TAB + [\"LITERACY_INDICES\"],\n",
    "    \"A15_TABULAR_CLUSTER_FEATURES\": TAB + [\"CLUSTER\"],\n",
    "    \"A16_AUDIO_ONLY\": [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\", \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\", \"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\",\n",
    "                       \"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\", \"CROSS_TASK\"],\n",
    "    \"A17_PHONETIC_ONLY\": [\"PHONETIC\"],\n",
    "    \"A18_TEMPORAL_ONLY\": [\"TEMPORAL\"],\n",
    "    \"A19_SPECTRAL_ONLY\": [\"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\"],\n",
    "    \"A20_WAVELETS_ONLY\": [\"WAVELETS\"],\n",
    "    \"A21_BACKGROUND_ONLY\": [\"BACKGROUND\"],\n",
    "    \"A22_ALL_VALIDATED_FEATURES\": TAB + AUDIO_CORE + [\"LITERACY_INDICES\"],\n",
    "    \"A23_RESIDUAL_MULTIMODAL\": TAB + AUDIO_CORE,\n",
    "}\n",
    "# Families an experiment is about; a single-purpose experiment is skipped when any is unavailable,\n",
    "# a composite experiment only when all are unavailable.\n",
    "KEY_FAMILIES = {name: [f for f in fams if f not in ([\"SCREENING\"] if name[:3] in {\"A02\", \"A03\", \"A04\"} else TAB)]\n",
    "                for name, fams in EXPERIMENTS.items()}\n",
    "KEY_FAMILIES[\"A05_COMPLETE_TABULAR\"] = [\"CORRECTNESS\", \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\", \"ADAPTIVE\", \"LINGUISTIC\"]\n",
    "for _single in (\"A17_PHONETIC_ONLY\", \"A18_TEMPORAL_ONLY\", \"A19_SPECTRAL_ONLY\", \"A20_WAVELETS_ONLY\", \"A21_BACKGROUND_ONLY\", \"A16_AUDIO_ONLY\"):\n",
    "    KEY_FAMILIES[_single] = list(EXPERIMENTS[_single])\n",
    "COMPOSITE_EXPERIMENTS = {\"A05_COMPLETE_TABULAR\", \"A13_TABULAR_MULTIMODAL\", \"A16_AUDIO_ONLY\", \"A19_SPECTRAL_ONLY\",\n",
    "                         \"A22_ALL_VALIDATED_FEATURES\", \"A23_RESIDUAL_MULTIMODAL\"}\n",
    "MULTI_MODEL_EXPERIMENTS = [\"A01_THETA_ONLY\", \"A05_COMPLETE_TABULAR\", \"A13_TABULAR_MULTIMODAL\", \"A22_ALL_VALIDATED_FEATURES\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class ColumnSetBuilder:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Builder over a fixed numeric table (no fold-fitted features).\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, base: pd.DataFrame, columns: list):\n",
    "        self.base = base\n",
    "        self.columns = [c for c in columns if c in base.columns]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def build(self, train_ids, val_ids, families=None, key=None):\n",
    "        X = self.base[self.columns]\n",
    "        X = X.loc[:, X.loc[list(train_ids)].notna().any()]\n",
    "        return X.loc[list(train_ids)], X.loc[list(val_ids)]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def columns_for(self, families):\n",
    "        return self.columns\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def family_available(fam: str, builder, ctx) -> bool:\n",
    "    if fam in {\"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\"}:\n",
    "        cm = da.clips(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "        return bool(ctx.config.get(\"enable_irt\")) and \"correct\" in cm.columns and cm[\"correct\"].notna().any()\n",
    "    if fam == \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\":\n",
    "        return ctx.stage_available(\"06\") or bool(modeling_columns(builder.base.columns, [fam]))\n",
    "    if fam == \"LITERACY_INDICES\":\n",
    "        from .literacy_indices import compute_indices\n",
    "\n",
    "        idx, _ = compute_indices(builder.base, list(builder.base.index), ctx.config)\n",
    "        return idx.shape[1] > 0\n",
    "    if fam == \"CLUSTER\":\n",
    "        from .clustering import prepare_space\n",
    "\n",
    "        Z, _ = prepare_space(builder.base, \"C09_SCREENING_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\")\n",
    "        return Z is not None\n",
    "    return bool(builder.columns_for({fam}))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def cv_evaluate(builder, families, y: pd.Series, assign: pd.DataFrame, scheme: str, cfg: dict, model: str = \"RIDGE\",\n",
    "                repeats=None, groups=None, label: str = \"\"):\n",
    "    fp = make_fit_predict(builder, set(families or []), model, cfg, y)\n",
    "    return run_cv(y, assign, scheme, fp, cfg, repeats=repeats, groups=groups, label=label)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _record(rows, oofs, name, model, scheme, res, families):\n",
    "    rows.append({\"experiment\": name, \"model\": model, \"scheme\": scheme, \"families\": \"+\".join(families), **res.summary})\n",
    "    oofs.append(res.oof.assign(experiment=name, model=model, scheme=scheme))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_predictive_ablation(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    from .fold_features import FoldFeatureBuilder\n",
    "    from .residual_models import nested_two_stage_cv\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    meta = da.student_meta(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    y = meta[\"target\"].dropna().astype(float)\n",
    "    assign = ctx.load_df(\"cv_assignments\")\n",
    "    builder = FoldFeatureBuilder(ctx)\n",
    "    builder.base = builder.base.reindex(y.index)\n",
    "    schemes = [s for s in (\"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\", \"CV_B_SCHOOL_GROUP_KFOLD\") if s in available_schemes(assign)]\n",
    "    groups = meta[\"school_id\"] if meta[\"school_id\"].notna().any() else None\n",
    "    primary = cfg[\"ablation_primary_model\"]\n",
    "    avail_cache: dict = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "    def avail(fam):\n",
    "        if fam not in avail_cache:\n",
    "            avail_cache[fam] = family_available(fam, builder, ctx)\n",
    "        return avail_cache[fam]\n",
    "\n",
    "    rows, oofs, status = [], [], []\n",
    "    for name, fams in EXPERIMENTS.items():\n",
    "        if name == \"A23_RESIDUAL_MULTIMODAL\":\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        present = [f for f in fams if avail(f)]\n",
    "        keys = KEY_FAMILIES.get(name, [])\n",
    "        missing = [f for f in keys if not avail(f)]\n",
    "        if name in COMPOSITE_EXPERIMENTS:\n",
    "            skip = bool(keys) and len(missing) == len(keys)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            skip = bool(missing)\n",
    "        if name != \"A00_TARGET_MEAN\" and (skip or not present):\n",
    "            status.append({\"experiment\": name, \"status\": \"SKIPPED_UNAVAILABLE\", \"missing_families\": \",\".join(missing)})\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        model = \"MEAN\" if name == \"A00_TARGET_MEAN\" else primary\n",
    "        for scheme in schemes:\n",
    "            res = cv_evaluate(builder, present, y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, groups=groups, label=name)\n",
    "            _record(rows, oofs, name, model, scheme, res, present)\n",
    "        status.append({\"experiment\": name, \"status\": \"COMPLETE\", \"families_used\": \"+\".join(present),\n",
    "                       \"missing_families\": \",\".join(missing)})\n",
    "        ctx.logger.info(\"Ablation %s complete\", name)\n",
    "    for name in MULTI_MODEL_EXPERIMENTS:\n",
    "        done = [s for s in status if s[\"experiment\"] == name and s[\"status\"] == \"COMPLETE\"]\n",
    "        if not done:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        fams = done[0][\"families_used\"].split(\"+\")\n",
    "        for m in cfg[\"ablation_models\"]:\n",
    "            if m == primary:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            ok, reason = model_available(m, cfg)\n",
    "            if not ok:\n",
    "                status.append({\"experiment\": name, \"model\": m, \"status\": \"MODEL_UNAVAILABLE\", \"reason\": reason})\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            res = cv_evaluate(builder, fams, y, assign, schemes[0], cfg, m, repeats=[0], groups=groups, label=name)\n",
    "            _record(rows, oofs, name, m, schemes[0], res, fams)\n",
    "    a23 = [f for f in EXPERIMENTS[\"A23_RESIDUAL_MULTIMODAL\"] if avail(f)]\n",
    "    if any(f in a23 for f in AUDIO_CORE):\n",
    "        for scheme in schemes:\n",
    "            res = nested_two_stage_cv(builder, y, assign, scheme, cfg, stage1_families=[\"SCREENING\"] + [f for f in TAB if avail(f) and f != \"SCREENING\"],\n",
    "                                      stage2_families=[f for f in AUDIO_CORE if avail(f)], groups=groups)\n",
    "            _record(rows, oofs, \"A23_RESIDUAL_MULTIMODAL\", f\"TWO_STAGE_{primary}\", scheme, res, a23)\n",
    "        status.append({\"experiment\": \"A23_RESIDUAL_MULTIMODAL\", \"status\": \"COMPLETE\"})\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        status.append({\"experiment\": \"A23_RESIDUAL_MULTIMODAL\", \"status\": \"SKIPPED_UNAVAILABLE\", \"missing_families\": \"audio\"})\n",
    "    results = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    oof = pd.concat(oofs, ignore_index=True) if oofs else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    results = add_comparisons(results, oof, cfg)\n",
    "    loo = leave_one_family_out(builder, y, assign, schemes[0], cfg, primary, avail, groups)\n",
    "    pair = pairwise_families(builder, y, assign, schemes[0], cfg, primary, avail, groups) if cfg.get(\"ablation_pairwise_families\") else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    fwd = nested_forward_selection(builder, y, assign, schemes[0], cfg, primary, avail)\n",
    "    red = redundancy_analysis(oof, results)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(results, \"ablation_results\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(oof, \"ablation_oof_predictions\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.DataFrame(status), \"ablation_status\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(loo, \"ablation_leave_one_family_out\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pair, \"ablation_pairwise_families\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(fwd, \"ablation_forward_selection\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(red, \"ablation_redundancy\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    _ablation_figures(ctx, results, loo, pair)\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": [\"ablation_results\", \"ablation_oof_predictions\", \"ablation_status\", \"ablation_leave_one_family_out\",\n",
    "                        \"ablation_pairwise_families\", \"ablation_forward_selection\", \"ablation_redundancy\"],\n",
    "            \"summary\": results[(results[\"model\"] == primary) & (results[\"scheme\"] == schemes[0])][\n",
    "                [\"experiment\", \"pooled_r2\", \"delta_r2_vs_screening\", \"delta_r2_vs_full_tabular\"]].to_dict(\"records\")\n",
    "            if len(results) else {}}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def add_comparisons(results: pd.DataFrame, oof: pd.DataFrame, cfg: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    if results.empty:\n",
    "        return results\n",
    "    out = results.copy()\n",
    "    for col in (\"delta_r2_vs_screening\", \"delta_r2_vs_screening_ci_lower\", \"delta_r2_vs_screening_ci_upper\",\n",
    "                \"delta_r2_vs_full_tabular\", \"delta_r2_vs_full_tabular_ci_lower\", \"delta_r2_vs_full_tabular_ci_upper\",\n",
    "                \"school_generalization_gap\", \"confidence_interval_lower\", \"confidence_interval_upper\", \"fold_std\"):\n",
    "        out[col] = np.nan\n",
    "    pooled = {k: pooled_predictions(g) for k, g in oof.groupby([\"experiment\", \"model\", \"scheme\"])}\n",
    "    primary = cfg[\"ablation_primary_model\"]\n",
    "    for i, r in out.iterrows():\n",
    "        key = (r[\"experiment\"], r[\"model\"], r[\"scheme\"])\n",
    "        if key not in pooled:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        p = pooled[key]\n",
    "        for ref, label in ((\"A01_THETA_ONLY\", \"screening\"), (\"A05_COMPLETE_TABULAR\", \"full_tabular\")):\n",
    "            rk = (ref, primary, r[\"scheme\"])\n",
    "            if rk in pooled and ref != r[\"experiment\"]:\n",
    "                common = p.index.intersection(pooled[rk].index)\n",
    "                d = paired_bootstrap_delta(p.loc[common, \"y\"], p.loc[common, \"pred\"], pooled[rk].loc[common, \"pred\"], cfg, \"r2\")\n",
    "                out.loc[i, f\"delta_r2_vs_{label}\"] = d[\"delta\"]\n",
    "                out.loc[i, f\"delta_r2_vs_{label}_ci_lower\"] = d[\"ci_lower\"]\n",
    "                out.loc[i, f\"delta_r2_vs_{label}_ci_upper\"] = d[\"ci_upper\"]\n",
    "        out.loc[i, \"confidence_interval_lower\"] = r.get(\"pooled_r2_ci_lower\")\n",
    "        out.loc[i, \"confidence_interval_upper\"] = r.get(\"pooled_r2_ci_upper\")\n",
    "        out.loc[i, \"fold_std\"] = r.get(\"std_fold_r2\")\n",
    "    for (exp, model), g in out.groupby([\"experiment\", \"model\"]):\n",
    "        a = g[g[\"scheme\"] == \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\"][\"pooled_r2\"]\n",
    "        b = g[g[\"scheme\"] == \"CV_B_SCHOOL_GROUP_KFOLD\"][\"pooled_r2\"]\n",
    "        if len(a) and len(b):\n",
    "            out.loc[g.index, \"school_generalization_gap\"] = float(a.iloc[0] - b.iloc[0])\n",
    "    out = out.rename(columns={\"pooled_r2\": \"r2\", \"pooled_rmse\": \"rmse\", \"pooled_mae\": \"mae\"})\n",
    "    out[\"pooled_r2\"] = out[\"r2\"]\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def leave_one_family_out(builder, y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, avail, groups) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    fams = [f for f in EXPERIMENTS[\"A13_TABULAR_MULTIMODAL\"] if avail(f)]\n",
    "    if len(fams) < 2:\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    full = cv_evaluate(builder, fams, y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, repeats=[0], groups=groups)\n",
    "    pf = pooled_predictions(full.oof)\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for f in fams:\n",
    "        sub = [x for x in fams if x != f]\n",
    "        res = cv_evaluate(builder, sub, y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, repeats=[0], groups=groups)\n",
    "        ps = pooled_predictions(res.oof)\n",
    "        d = paired_bootstrap_delta(pf[\"y\"], pf[\"pred\"], ps.reindex(pf.index)[\"pred\"], cfg, \"r2\")\n",
    "        rows.append({\"dropped_family\": f, \"r2_without\": res.summary.get(\"pooled_r2\"), \"r2_full\": full.summary.get(\"pooled_r2\"),\n",
    "                     \"loss_when_dropped\": d[\"delta\"], \"ci_lower\": d[\"ci_lower\"], \"ci_upper\": d[\"ci_upper\"]})\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def pairwise_families(builder, y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, avail, groups) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    audio = [f for f in (\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\", \"PHONETIC\", \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\") if avail(f)]\n",
    "    tab = [f for f in TAB if avail(f)]\n",
    "    base = cv_evaluate(builder, tab, y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, repeats=[0], groups=groups)\n",
    "    r_base = base.summary.get(\"pooled_r2\", np.nan)\n",
    "    single = {}\n",
    "    for f in audio:\n",
    "        single[f] = cv_evaluate(builder, tab + [f], y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, repeats=[0], groups=groups).summary.get(\"pooled_r2\", np.nan) - r_base\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for i, a in enumerate(audio):\n",
    "        for b in audio[i + 1:]:\n",
    "            r = cv_evaluate(builder, tab + [a, b], y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, repeats=[0], groups=groups).summary.get(\"pooled_r2\", np.nan)\n",
    "            gain = r - r_base\n",
    "            rows.append({\"family_a\": a, \"family_b\": b, \"delta_r2_pair\": gain, \"delta_r2_a\": single[a], \"delta_r2_b\": single[b],\n",
    "                         \"complementarity\": gain - single[a] - single[b]})\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def nested_forward_selection(builder, y, assign, scheme, cfg, model, avail) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Greedy family selection chosen on inner folds of each outer training set (nested).\"\"\"\n",
    "    from sklearn.model_selection import KFold\n",
    "\n",
    "    from .validation import iter_folds, regression_metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "    candidates = [f for f in (\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\", \"PHONETIC\", \"CROSS_TASK\",\n",
    "                              \"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\", \"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\") if avail(f)]\n",
    "    tab = [f for f in TAB if avail(f) and f not in {\"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\"}]\n",
    "    cols_base = builder.columns_for(set(tab))\n",
    "    simple = ColumnSetBuilder(builder.base, cols_base)\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for rep, fold, tr, va in iter_folds(assign, scheme, repeats=[0]):\n",
    "        tr = np.array([s for s in tr if s in y.index])\n",
    "        va = np.array([s for s in va if s in y.index])\n",
    "        chosen = []\n",
    "        inner = KFold(int(cfg[\"inner_cv_folds\"]), shuffle=True, random_state=int(cfg[\"seed\"]) + fold)\n",
    "\n",
    "        def inner_score(fams):\n",
    "            cols = cols_base + builder.columns_for(set(fams))\n",
    "            sb = ColumnSetBuilder(builder.base, cols)\n",
    "            fp = make_fit_predict(sb, None, model, cfg, y)\n",
    "            preds = pd.Series(np.nan, index=tr)\n",
    "            for itr, iva in inner.split(tr):\n",
    "                preds.iloc[iva] = fp(tr[itr], tr[iva], None)\n",
    "            return regression_metrics(y.loc[tr], preds)[\"r2\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "        current = inner_score([])\n",
    "        for step in range(int(cfg[\"ablation_forward_max_steps\"])):\n",
    "            scores = {f: inner_score(chosen + [f]) for f in candidates if f not in chosen}\n",
    "            if not scores:\n",
    "                break\n",
    "            best = max(scores, key=scores.get)\n",
    "            if scores[best] <= current + 0.002:\n",
    "                break\n",
    "            chosen.append(best)\n",
    "            current = scores[best]\n",
    "        sb = ColumnSetBuilder(builder.base, cols_base + builder.columns_for(set(chosen)))\n",
    "        pred = make_fit_predict(sb, None, model, cfg, y)(tr, va, None)\n",
    "        outer = regression_metrics(y.loc[va], pred)\n",
    "        base_pred = make_fit_predict(simple, None, model, cfg, y)(tr, va, None)\n",
    "        rows.append({\"repeat\": rep, \"fold\": fold, \"selected_families\": \"+\".join(chosen), \"inner_r2\": current,\n",
    "                     \"outer_r2\": outer[\"r2\"], \"outer_r2_tabular_only\": regression_metrics(y.loc[va], base_pred)[\"r2\"]})\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def redundancy_analysis(oof: pd.DataFrame, results: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    if oof.empty:\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    single = [\"A17_PHONETIC_ONLY\", \"A18_TEMPORAL_ONLY\", \"A19_SPECTRAL_ONLY\", \"A20_WAVELETS_ONLY\", \"A21_BACKGROUND_ONLY\",\n",
    "              \"A16_AUDIO_ONLY\", \"A01_THETA_ONLY\"]\n",
    "    sub = oof[oof[\"experiment\"].isin(single) & (oof[\"scheme\"] == \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\")]\n",
    "    if sub.empty:\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    P = sub.groupby([\"student_id\", \"experiment\"])[\"pred\"].mean().unstack()\n",
    "    C = P.corr(method=\"spearman\")\n",
    "    return C.reset_index().rename(columns={\"experiment\": \"experiment_a\"})\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _ablation_figures(ctx, results: pd.DataFrame, loo: pd.DataFrame, pair: pd.DataFrame) -> None:\n",
    "    if results.empty:\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    primary = ctx.config[\"ablation_primary_model\"]\n",
    "    for scheme, g in results[results[\"model\"].isin([primary, \"MEAN\", f\"TWO_STAGE_{primary}\"])].groupby(\"scheme\"):\n",
    "        g = g.sort_values(\"experiment\")\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 2, (7, 0.3 * len(g) + 2))\n",
    "        ax = axes[0, 0]\n",
    "        lo = (g[\"r2\"] - g[\"confidence_interval_lower\"]).clip(lower=0).fillna(0)\n",
    "        hi = (g[\"confidence_interval_upper\"] - g[\"r2\"]).clip(lower=0).fillna(0)\n",
    "        ax.errorbar(g[\"r2\"], g[\"experiment\"], xerr=[lo, hi], fmt=\"o\", capsize=2)\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(ax, f\"Pooled OOF R² ({scheme})\", \"R² (95% CI)\", \"\", int(g[\"n_students\"].max()))\n",
    "        ax = axes[0, 1]\n",
    "        d = g.dropna(subset=[\"delta_r2_vs_screening\"])\n",
    "        ax.errorbar(d[\"delta_r2_vs_screening\"], d[\"experiment\"],\n",
    "                    xerr=[(d[\"delta_r2_vs_screening\"] - d[\"delta_r2_vs_screening_ci_lower\"]).clip(lower=0).fillna(0),\n",
    "                          (d[\"delta_r2_vs_screening_ci_upper\"] - d[\"delta_r2_vs_screening\"]).clip(lower=0).fillna(0)], fmt=\"o\", capsize=2)\n",
    "        ax.axvline(0, color=\"grey\")\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(ax, \"Incremental R² vs screening (paired bootstrap)\", \"delta R²\", \"\", int(g[\"n_students\"].max()))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, f\"ablation_{scheme}\", f\"Feature-family ablation ({scheme})\", \"Which modalities add predictive value?\",\n",
    "                   \"ablation_results\", int(g[\"n_students\"].max()),\n",
    "                   f\"Best experiment: {g.loc[g['r2'].idxmax(), 'experiment']} (R²={g['r2'].max():.3f}).\")\n",
    "    if len(loo):\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1)\n",
    "        l = loo.sort_values(\"loss_when_dropped\")\n",
    "        viz.forest(axes[0, 0], l, \"dropped_family\", \"loss_when_dropped\", \"ci_lower\", \"ci_upper\",\n",
    "                   \"Leave-one-family-out: R² lost when dropping a family\", \"delta R²\")\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"ablation_leave_one_out\", \"Leave-one-family-out ablation\", \"Which families are indispensable?\",\n",
    "                   \"ablation_leave_one_family_out\", None, \"Positive values: the family contributes uniquely.\")\n",
    "    if len(pair):\n",
    "        fams = sorted(set(pair[\"family_a\"]) | set(pair[\"family_b\"]))\n",
    "        M = pd.DataFrame(np.nan, index=fams, columns=fams)\n",
    "        for _, r in pair.iterrows():\n",
    "            M.loc[r[\"family_a\"], r[\"family_b\"]] = M.loc[r[\"family_b\"], r[\"family_a\"]] = r[\"complementarity\"]\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (6, 5))\n",
    "        viz.heatmap(axes[0, 0], M, \"Family complementarity (pair gain - single gains)\", annotate=True, cbar_label=\"delta R²\")\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"ablation_complementarity\", \"Feature-family complementarity\", \"Do families add complementary information?\",\n",
    "                   \"ablation_pairwise_families\", None, \"Positive: synergy; negative: redundancy.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-005",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/adaptive_behavior.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 05 - adaptive assessment and behavioural trajectories.\n",
    "\n",
    "Scientific question: does the pattern of item responses provide information\n",
    "beyond the final screening score?\n",
    "\n",
    "Sequential analysis requires a reliable presentation order (a resolved\n",
    "order/position column or a timestamp). Dataframe row order is never used. If\n",
    "no valid order exists the stage reports why and produces no trajectory\n",
    "features.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "from .stats_utils import linear_slope, safe_corr\n",
    "\n",
    "TRAJECTORY_FEATURES = [\"n_attempted\", \"longest_correct_streak\", \"longest_error_streak\", \"error_recovery_rate\",\n",
    "                       \"accuracy_early\", \"accuracy_late\", \"accuracy_decay\", \"difficulty_progression_slope\",\n",
    "                       \"duration_progression_slope\", \"duration_difficulty_slope\", \"response_sequence_entropy\",\n",
    "                       \"response_volatility\", \"response_autocorr_lag1\", \"difficulty_at_stop\", \"accuracy_last3\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def order_validity(clips: pd.DataFrame) -> dict:\n",
    "    report: dict = {\"valid\": False, \"source\": None, \"reason\": \"\"}\n",
    "    if \"order\" in clips.columns and clips[\"order\"].notna().mean() > 0.9:\n",
    "        dup = clips.dropna(subset=[\"order\"]).duplicated([\"student_id\", \"task_family\", \"order\"]).mean()\n",
    "        report.update({\"source\": \"order\", \"duplicate_rate_within_student_task\": float(dup)})\n",
    "        if dup <= 0.05:\n",
    "            report.update(valid=True, reason=\"resolved order column with <=5% within-student-task duplicates\")\n",
    "            return report\n",
    "        report[\"reason\"] = f\"order column has {dup:.1%} duplicated positions within student-task\"\n",
    "    if \"timestamp\" in clips.columns and clips[\"timestamp\"].notna().mean() > 0.9:\n",
    "        dup = clips.dropna(subset=[\"timestamp\"]).duplicated([\"student_id\", \"timestamp\"]).mean()\n",
    "        report.update({\"source\": \"timestamp\", \"duplicate_rate_within_student\": float(dup)})\n",
    "        if dup <= 0.05:\n",
    "            report.update(valid=True, reason=\"timestamp column with <=5% duplicates\")\n",
    "            return report\n",
    "        report[\"reason\"] = f\"timestamps have {dup:.1%} duplicates\"\n",
    "    if not report[\"reason\"]:\n",
    "        report[\"reason\"] = \"no resolved order or timestamp column; dataframe order is not a valid substitute\"\n",
    "    return report\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _longest_run(seq: np.ndarray, value: float) -> int:\n",
    "    best = cur = 0\n",
    "    for v in seq:\n",
    "        cur = cur + 1 if v == value else 0\n",
    "        best = max(best, cur)\n",
    "    return best\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def sequence_features(seq: np.ndarray, diff: np.ndarray | None, dur: np.ndarray | None) -> dict:\n",
    "    n = len(seq)\n",
    "    out = {k: np.nan for k in TRAJECTORY_FEATURES}\n",
    "    out[\"n_attempted\"] = float(n)\n",
    "    if n == 0:\n",
    "        return out\n",
    "    out[\"longest_correct_streak\"] = float(_longest_run(seq, 1.0))\n",
    "    out[\"longest_error_streak\"] = float(_longest_run(seq, 0.0))\n",
    "    if n >= 2:\n",
    "        prev, nxt = seq[:-1], seq[1:]\n",
    "        err = prev == 0\n",
    "        out[\"error_recovery_rate\"] = float(nxt[err].mean()) if err.any() else np.nan\n",
    "        out[\"response_volatility\"] = float((prev != nxt).mean())\n",
    "        trans = pd.crosstab(prev, nxt, normalize=\"index\")\n",
    "        p_prev = pd.Series(prev).value_counts(normalize=True)\n",
    "        h = 0.0\n",
    "        for a in trans.index:\n",
    "            row = trans.loc[a].to_numpy()\n",
    "            row = row[row > 0]\n",
    "            h += p_prev.get(a, 0) * -(row * np.log2(row)).sum()\n",
    "        out[\"response_sequence_entropy\"] = float(h)\n",
    "        if np.std(seq) > 0 and n >= 4:\n",
    "            out[\"response_autocorr_lag1\"] = float(np.corrcoef(prev, nxt)[0, 1])\n",
    "    half = n // 2\n",
    "    if n >= 4:\n",
    "        out[\"accuracy_early\"] = float(seq[:half].mean())\n",
    "        out[\"accuracy_late\"] = float(seq[half:].mean())\n",
    "        out[\"accuracy_decay\"] = out[\"accuracy_early\"] - out[\"accuracy_late\"]\n",
    "    out[\"accuracy_last3\"] = float(seq[-3:].mean())\n",
    "    pos = np.arange(n, dtype=float)\n",
    "    if diff is not None:\n",
    "        out[\"difficulty_progression_slope\"] = linear_slope(pos, diff)\n",
    "        out[\"difficulty_at_stop\"] = float(diff[-1]) if np.isfinite(diff[-1]) else np.nan\n",
    "    if dur is not None:\n",
    "        out[\"duration_progression_slope\"] = linear_slope(pos, dur)\n",
    "        if diff is not None:\n",
    "            out[\"duration_difficulty_slope\"] = linear_slope(diff, dur)\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_adaptive_testing(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    clips = da.clips(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    validity = order_validity(clips)\n",
    "    ctx.save_json(validity, \"order_validity\")\n",
    "    if not validity[\"valid\"]:\n",
    "        ctx.logger.warning(\"Sequential analysis disabled: %s\", validity[\"reason\"])\n",
    "        return {\"outputs\": [\"order_validity\"], \"summary\": validity}\n",
    "    if \"correct\" not in clips.columns or clips[\"correct\"].notna().sum() == 0:\n",
    "        validity[\"reason\"] += \"; no binary correctness\"\n",
    "        ctx.save_json(validity, \"order_validity\")\n",
    "        return {\"outputs\": [\"order_validity\"], \"summary\": validity}\n",
    "    key = validity[\"source\"]\n",
    "    d = clips.dropna(subset=[key, \"correct\"]).copy()\n",
    "    diff = da.item_difficulty(ctx)\n",
    "    if diff is not None:\n",
    "        d = d.merge(diff[[\"item_key\", \"b\"]], on=\"item_key\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        p = d.groupby(\"item_key\")[\"correct\"].transform(\"mean\").clip(0.02, 0.98)\n",
    "        d[\"b\"] = -np.log(p / (1 - p))\n",
    "    dur_col = None\n",
    "    if ctx.stage_available(\"06\"):\n",
    "        cf = da.clip_features(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "        if cf is not None and \"t_active_dur\" in cf.columns:\n",
    "            d = d.merge(cf[[\"clip_id\", \"t_active_dur\"]], on=\"clip_id\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "            dur_col = \"t_active_dur\"\n",
    "    if dur_col is None and \"response_duration\" in d.columns:\n",
    "        dur_col = \"response_duration\"\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    seq_rows = []\n",
    "    for (sid, task), g in d.sort_values(key).groupby([\"student_id\", \"task_family\"], sort=False):\n",
    "        seq = g[\"correct\"].to_numpy(dtype=float)\n",
    "        feats = sequence_features(seq, g[\"b\"].to_numpy(dtype=float), g[dur_col].to_numpy(dtype=float) if dur_col else None)\n",
    "        feats.update({\"student_id\": sid, \"task_family\": task})\n",
    "        rows.append(feats)\n",
    "        for pos, (c, b) in enumerate(zip(seq, g[\"b\"].to_numpy(dtype=float))):\n",
    "            seq_rows.append({\"student_id\": sid, \"task_family\": task, \"position\": pos, \"correct\": c, \"b\": b})\n",
    "    long = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    wide = long.pivot(index=\"student_id\", columns=\"task_family\", values=TRAJECTORY_FEATURES)\n",
    "    wide.columns = [f\"traj_{task}_{feat}\" for feat, task in wide.columns]\n",
    "    for feat in TRAJECTORY_FEATURES:\n",
    "        cols = [c for c in wide.columns if c.endswith(f\"_{feat}\")]\n",
    "        wide[f\"traj_all_{feat}\"] = wide[cols].mean(axis=1)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(wide.reset_index(), \"trajectory_features\")\n",
    "    seqs = pd.DataFrame(seq_rows)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(seqs, \"response_sequences\")\n",
    "    trans = []\n",
    "    for task, g in seqs.sort_values([\"student_id\", \"position\"]).groupby(\"task_family\"):\n",
    "        prev = g.groupby(\"student_id\")[\"correct\"].shift(1)\n",
    "        t = pd.crosstab(prev.dropna(), g.loc[prev.notna(), \"correct\"], normalize=\"index\")\n",
    "        for a in t.index:\n",
    "            for b in t.columns:\n",
    "                trans.append({\"task_family\": task, \"from\": a, \"to\": b, \"probability\": float(t.loc[a, b])})\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.DataFrame(trans), \"transition_matrix\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    y = da.target(ctx)\n",
    "    assoc = []\n",
    "    for c in wide.columns:\n",
    "        r, p, n = safe_corr(wide[c], y.reindex(wide.index), \"spearman\", int(cfg[\"min_n_correlation\"]))\n",
    "        assoc.append({\"feature\": c, \"target_rho\": r, \"p\": p, \"n\": n})\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.DataFrame(assoc), \"trajectory_target_associations\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    _trajectory_figures(ctx, seqs, pd.DataFrame(trans), wide, y)\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": [\"order_validity\", \"trajectory_features\", \"response_sequences\", \"transition_matrix\",\n",
    "                        \"trajectory_target_associations\"],\n",
    "            \"summary\": {\"order_source\": key, \"n_students\": int(len(wide)), \"duration_source\": dur_col}}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _trajectory_figures(ctx, seqs: pd.DataFrame, trans: pd.DataFrame, wide: pd.DataFrame, y: pd.Series) -> None:\n",
    "    scr = da.screening(ctx)\n",
    "    for task, g in seqs.groupby(\"task_family\"):\n",
    "        M = g.pivot_table(index=\"student_id\", columns=\"position\", values=\"correct\")\n",
    "        if scr is not None and \"theta_mean\" in scr.columns:\n",
    "            M = M.loc[scr[\"theta_mean\"].reindex(M.index).sort_values().index]\n",
    "        M = M.iloc[:, :60]\n",
    "        sample = M if len(M) <= 400 else M.iloc[np.linspace(0, len(M) - 1, 400).astype(int)]\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 2, (6, 5))\n",
    "        axes[0, 0].imshow(sample.to_numpy(), aspect=\"auto\", cmap=\"RdYlGn\", vmin=0, vmax=1, interpolation=\"nearest\")\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], f\"{task}: student x position correctness (white = not attempted)\", \"position\",\n",
    "                          \"students (sorted by screening)\", len(M))\n",
    "        prof = g.groupby(\"position\")[\"b\"].agg([\"mean\", \"std\", \"count\"])\n",
    "        prof = prof[prof[\"count\"] >= 5]\n",
    "        axes[0, 1].errorbar(prof.index, prof[\"mean\"], yerr=1.96 * prof[\"std\"] / np.sqrt(prof[\"count\"]), fmt=\"-o\", ms=2)\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 1], f\"{task}: difficulty trajectory\", \"position\", \"mean item difficulty (95% CI)\", len(M))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, f\"sequence_heatmap_{task}\", f\"Response sequences and difficulty trajectory: {task}\",\n",
    "                   \"How do students progress through adaptive items?\", \"response_sequences\", len(M),\n",
    "                   f\"Median sequence length {g.groupby('student_id').size().median():.0f}.\")\n",
    "    if len(trans):\n",
    "        tasks = trans[\"task_family\"].unique()\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, len(tasks), (3.5, 3.2))\n",
    "        for ax, task in zip(axes.ravel(), tasks):\n",
    "            t = trans[trans[\"task_family\"] == task].pivot(index=\"from\", columns=\"to\", values=\"probability\")\n",
    "            viz.heatmap(ax, t, f\"{task}: P(next | previous)\", cmap=\"viridis\", vmin=0, vmax=1, annotate=True)\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"correctness_transitions\", \"Correctness transition matrices\", \"Do errors cluster?\",\n",
    "                   \"transition_matrix\", int(seqs[\"student_id\"].nunique()), \"Rows: previous response; columns: next response.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-006",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/audio_manifest.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Safe TAR inspection, audio inventory and safe extraction.\n",
    "\n",
    "Archives are never extracted before their members have been inspected and the\n",
    "available disk space has been checked. Only regular files with safe relative\n",
    "paths are ever written; symlinks, hard links, devices, absolute paths and\n",
    "path traversal are rejected.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import hashlib\n",
    "import io\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import tarfile\n",
    "from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from .io_utils import atomic_write_json, read_json\n",
    "\n",
    "AUDIO_EXTENSIONS = {\".wav\", \".flac\", \".mp3\", \".ogg\", \".opus\", \".m4a\", \".aac\", \".webm\", \".aiff\", \".aif\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class UnsafeArchiveError(RuntimeError):\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def member_safety(member: tarfile.TarInfo) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n",
    "    name = member.name\n",
    "    if member.issym():\n",
    "        return False, \"symlink\"\n",
    "    if member.islnk():\n",
    "        return False, \"hardlink\"\n",
    "    if member.isdir():\n",
    "        return False, \"directory\"\n",
    "    if not member.isreg():\n",
    "        return False, \"not_regular_file\"\n",
    "    if not name or \"\\x00\" in name:\n",
    "        return False, \"invalid_name\"\n",
    "    normalized = name.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")\n",
    "    p = PurePosixPath(normalized)\n",
    "    if p.is_absolute() or normalized.startswith(\"/\"):\n",
    "        return False, \"absolute_path\"\n",
    "    if len(normalized) >= 2 and normalized[1] == \":\":\n",
    "        return False, \"drive_letter\"\n",
    "    if any(part == \"..\" for part in p.parts):\n",
    "        return False, \"path_traversal\"\n",
    "    if member.size < 0:\n",
    "        return False, \"negative_size\"\n",
    "    return True, \"ok\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def inspect_archive(tar_path: Path) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"List archive members without extracting anything.\"\"\"\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    with tarfile.open(tar_path, mode=\"r:*\") as tf:\n",
    "        for m in tf:\n",
    "            safe, reason = member_safety(m)\n",
    "            if m.isdir():\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            name = m.name.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")\n",
    "            rows.append({\n",
    "                \"archive\": tar_path.name, \"member\": name, \"basename\": PurePosixPath(name).name,\n",
    "                \"stem\": PurePosixPath(name).stem, \"extension\": PurePosixPath(name).suffix.lower(),\n",
    "                \"size_bytes\": int(m.size), \"offset_data\": int(getattr(m, \"offset_data\", -1)),\n",
    "                \"safe\": safe, \"safety_reason\": reason,\n",
    "            })\n",
    "    df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    if df.empty:\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"archive\", \"member\", \"basename\", \"stem\", \"extension\", \"size_bytes\",\n",
    "                                     \"offset_data\", \"safe\", \"safety_reason\", \"is_audio_ext\"])\n",
    "    df[\"is_audio_ext\"] = df[\"extension\"].isin(AUDIO_EXTENSIONS)\n",
    "    return df\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _audio_info_from_bytes(data: bytes) -> dict:\n",
    "    info = {\"decode_status\": \"OK\", \"sample_rate\": np.nan, \"channels\": np.nan, \"frames\": np.nan,\n",
    "            \"duration_s\": np.nan, \"format\": None, \"subtype\": None, \"decode_backend\": None}\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import soundfile as sf  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "        with sf.SoundFile(io.BytesIO(data)) as f:\n",
    "            info.update(sample_rate=float(f.samplerate), channels=float(f.channels), frames=float(f.frames),\n",
    "                        duration_s=float(f.frames) / float(f.samplerate) if f.samplerate else np.nan,\n",
    "                        format=f.format, subtype=f.subtype, decode_backend=\"soundfile\")\n",
    "            probe = f.read(frames=min(int(f.frames), 2048), dtype=\"float32\", always_2d=True)\n",
    "            if probe.size and not np.all(np.isfinite(probe)):\n",
    "                info[\"decode_status\"] = \"INVALID_VALUES\"\n",
    "        if info[\"frames\"] == 0:\n",
    "            info[\"decode_status\"] = \"EMPTY\"\n",
    "        return info\n",
    "    except Exception as exc:\n",
    "        first_error = f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\"\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import tempfile\n",
    "\n",
    "        import librosa  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "        with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".audio\", delete=False) as tmp:\n",
    "            tmp.write(data)\n",
    "            tmp_path = tmp.name\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            y, sr = librosa.load(tmp_path, sr=None, mono=False)\n",
    "        finally:\n",
    "            os.unlink(tmp_path)\n",
    "        channels = 1 if y.ndim == 1 else y.shape[0]\n",
    "        frames = y.shape[-1]\n",
    "        info.update(sample_rate=float(sr), channels=float(channels), frames=float(frames),\n",
    "                    duration_s=frames / sr if sr else np.nan, decode_backend=\"librosa\")\n",
    "        if frames == 0:\n",
    "            info[\"decode_status\"] = \"EMPTY\"\n",
    "        return info\n",
    "    except Exception as exc:\n",
    "        info[\"decode_status\"] = \"CORRUPT\"\n",
    "        info[\"decode_error\"] = f\"{first_error} | {type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\"\n",
    "        return info\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def audio_inventory(tar_path: Path, members: pd.DataFrame, decode: bool = True, hash_bytes: bool = True,\n",
    "                    allowed_members: set | None = None, logger=None) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Read each safe audio member once (sequentially) to collect metadata and hashes.\"\"\"\n",
    "    from .logging_utils import progress\n",
    "\n",
    "    wanted = members[members[\"safe\"] & members[\"is_audio_ext\"]]\n",
    "    if allowed_members is not None:\n",
    "        wanted = wanted[wanted[\"member\"].isin(allowed_members)]\n",
    "    wanted_set = set(wanted[\"member\"])\n",
    "    records = []\n",
    "    with tarfile.open(tar_path, mode=\"r:*\") as tf:\n",
    "        iterator = progress(tf, total=len(members), desc=f\"inventory {tar_path.name}\")\n",
    "        for m in iterator:\n",
    "            name = m.name.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")\n",
    "            if name not in wanted_set:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            fh = tf.extractfile(m)\n",
    "            data = fh.read() if fh is not None else b\"\"\n",
    "            rec = {\"member\": name}\n",
    "            if hash_bytes:\n",
    "                rec[\"sha1\"] = hashlib.sha1(data).hexdigest()\n",
    "            if decode:\n",
    "                rec.update(_audio_info_from_bytes(data))\n",
    "            records.append(rec)\n",
    "    inv = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
    "    if inv.empty:\n",
    "        return members.assign(sha1=np.nan, decode_status=\"NOT_INSPECTED\")\n",
    "    out = members.merge(inv, on=\"member\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "    if \"decode_status\" not in out.columns:\n",
    "        out[\"decode_status\"] = np.where(out[\"member\"].isin(wanted_set), \"HEADER_NOT_DECODED\", None)\n",
    "    out.loc[out[\"decode_status\"].isna(), \"decode_status\"] = np.where(\n",
    "        out.loc[out[\"decode_status\"].isna(), \"safe\"], \"NOT_INSPECTED\", \"UNSAFE_MEMBER\")\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def match_clips_to_members(clips: pd.DataFrame, members: pd.DataFrame, split: str) -> tuple[pd.DataFrame, dict]:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Map clip rows to archive members via the resolved audio file or clip id.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Matching keys tried (in order): exact member path, basename, stem. A key that\n",
    "    maps to more than one member is reported as ambiguous and left unmatched.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    report: dict = {\"split\": split, \"n_clips\": int(len(clips))}\n",
    "    m = members[members[\"safe\"] & members[\"is_audio_ext\"]].copy()\n",
    "    clips = clips.copy()\n",
    "    clips[\"audio_member\"] = np.nan\n",
    "    clips[\"audio_match_key\"] = np.nan\n",
    "    lookups = {\n",
    "        \"member\": m.groupby(\"member\")[\"member\"].agg(list).to_dict(),\n",
    "        \"basename\": m.groupby(\"basename\")[\"member\"].agg(list).to_dict(),\n",
    "        \"stem\": m.groupby(\"stem\")[\"member\"].agg(list).to_dict(),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    candidates = []\n",
    "    if \"audio_file\" in clips.columns:\n",
    "        af = clips[\"audio_file\"].astype(str).str.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\", regex=False)\n",
    "        candidates += [(\"audio_file\", \"member\", af), (\"audio_file\", \"basename\", af.map(lambda s: PurePosixPath(s).name)),\n",
    "                       (\"audio_file\", \"stem\", af.map(lambda s: PurePosixPath(s).stem))]\n",
    "    candidates += [(\"clip_id\", \"stem\", clips[\"clip_id\"].astype(str)), (\"clip_id\", \"basename\", clips[\"clip_id\"].astype(str))]\n",
    "    ambiguous = 0\n",
    "    for source, kind, keys in candidates:\n",
    "        todo = clips[\"audio_member\"].isna()\n",
    "        if not todo.any():\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        found = keys[todo].map(lambda k: lookups[kind].get(k))\n",
    "        single = found.map(lambda v: isinstance(v, list) and len(v) == 1)\n",
    "        multi = found.map(lambda v: isinstance(v, list) and len(v) > 1)\n",
    "        ambiguous += int(multi.sum())\n",
    "        idx = found[single].index\n",
    "        clips.loc[idx, \"audio_member\"] = found[single].map(lambda v: v[0])\n",
    "        clips.loc[idx, \"audio_match_key\"] = f\"{source}->{kind}\"\n",
    "    matched = clips[\"audio_member\"].notna()\n",
    "    dup_members = clips.loc[matched, \"audio_member\"].duplicated(keep=False)\n",
    "    report.update({\n",
    "        \"n_matched\": int(matched.sum()),\n",
    "        \"n_missing_audio\": int((~matched).sum()),\n",
    "        \"n_ambiguous_keys\": ambiguous,\n",
    "        \"n_members_shared_by_several_clips\": int(dup_members.sum()),\n",
    "        \"match_methods\": clips[\"audio_match_key\"].value_counts(dropna=False).to_dict(),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    used = set(clips.loc[matched, \"audio_member\"])\n",
    "    orphans = sorted(set(m[\"member\"]) - used)\n",
    "    report[\"n_orphaned_recordings\"] = len(orphans)\n",
    "    report[\"orphan_examples\"] = orphans[:20]\n",
    "    return clips, report\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def required_extraction_bytes(members: pd.DataFrame, factor: float) -> int:\n",
    "    return int(members[\"size_bytes\"].sum() * factor)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def safe_extract(tar_path: Path, dest: Path, members: list, free_bytes: int, factor: float = 1.15,\n",
    "                 min_free_gb: float = 2.0, logger=None) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Extract only the listed members after safety and disk-space checks.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Resumable: a member already present with the expected size is skipped. A\n",
    "    completion marker records the extracted set.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    dest = Path(dest).resolve()\n",
    "    dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    marker = dest / \".extraction_complete.json\"\n",
    "    wanted = set(members)\n",
    "    done = read_json(marker, default={}) or {}\n",
    "    if done.get(\"archive\") == tar_path.name and set(done.get(\"members\", [])) >= wanted:\n",
    "        return {\"status\": \"ALREADY_EXTRACTED\", \"n\": len(wanted), \"dest\": str(dest)}\n",
    "    with tarfile.open(tar_path, mode=\"r:*\") as tf:\n",
    "        infos = [m for m in tf.getmembers() if m.name.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\") in wanted]\n",
    "        unsafe = [(m.name, member_safety(m)[1]) for m in infos if not member_safety(m)[0]]\n",
    "        if unsafe:\n",
    "            raise UnsafeArchiveError(f\"unsafe members requested for extraction: {unsafe[:5]}\")\n",
    "        need = int(sum(m.size for m in infos) * factor) + int(min_free_gb * 1e9)\n",
    "        if need > free_bytes:\n",
    "            raise OSError(f\"insufficient disk space: need {need / 1e9:.2f} GB, have {free_bytes / 1e9:.2f} GB\")\n",
    "        from .logging_utils import progress\n",
    "\n",
    "        written = skipped = 0\n",
    "        for m in progress(sorted(infos, key=lambda i: getattr(i, \"offset_data\", 0)), total=len(infos),\n",
    "                          desc=f\"extract {tar_path.name}\"):\n",
    "            rel = PurePosixPath(m.name.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\"))\n",
    "            target = (dest / Path(*rel.parts)).resolve()\n",
    "            if dest not in target.parents:\n",
    "                raise UnsafeArchiveError(f\"member escapes destination: {m.name}\")\n",
    "            if target.exists() and target.stat().st_size == m.size:\n",
    "                skipped += 1\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "            src = tf.extractfile(m)\n",
    "            if src is None:\n",
    "                raise UnsafeArchiveError(f\"cannot read member {m.name}\")\n",
    "            tmp = target.with_name(target.name + \".part\")\n",
    "            with open(tmp, \"wb\") as out:\n",
    "                while True:\n",
    "                    chunk = src.read(1 << 20)\n",
    "                    if not chunk:\n",
    "                        break\n",
    "                    out.write(chunk)\n",
    "            os.replace(tmp, target)\n",
    "            written += 1\n",
    "    atomic_write_json(marker, {\"archive\": tar_path.name, \"members\": sorted(wanted | set(done.get(\"members\", [])))})\n",
    "    return {\"status\": \"EXTRACTED\", \"written\": written, \"skipped_existing\": skipped, \"dest\": str(dest)}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def read_member_bytes(tar_path: Path, members: list) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Read selected members (ordered by archive offset) into memory.\"\"\"\n",
    "    wanted = set(members)\n",
    "    out = {}\n",
    "    with tarfile.open(tar_path, mode=\"r:*\") as tf:\n",
    "        infos = [m for m in tf.getmembers() if m.name.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\") in wanted]\n",
    "        for m in sorted(infos, key=lambda i: getattr(i, \"offset_data\", 0)):\n",
    "            if not member_safety(m)[0]:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            fh = tf.extractfile(m)\n",
    "            if fh is not None:\n",
    "                out[m.name.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")] = fh.read()\n",
    "    return out\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-007",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/audio_processing.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 06 - acoustic quality, signal atlas and the unified extraction pipeline.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each recording is decoded exactly once. A shared ``SignalBundle`` (STFT,\n",
    "power, mel, log-mel, MFCC, RMS envelope and voice-activity mask) feeds the\n",
    "quality, temporal, spectral, cepstral, wavelet and prosody extractors.\n",
    "Extraction runs in parallel chunks, writes each chunk atomically and resumes\n",
    "after interruption. Failed recordings keep their row with an explicit status.\n",
    "\n",
    "Voice activity detection marks speech-like regions only. It is not speaker\n",
    "identification: speech-active frames may contain other voices.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import gc\n",
    "import hashlib\n",
    "import io\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import tempfile\n",
    "import time\n",
    "from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from .config import extraction_config, subset_hash, EXTRACTION_KEYS\n",
    "from .io_utils import atomic_write_parquet\n",
    "\n",
    "EPS = 1e-10\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "@dataclass\n",
    "class SignalBundle:\n",
    "    y: np.ndarray\n",
    "    sr: int\n",
    "    n_fft: int\n",
    "    hop: int\n",
    "    win: int\n",
    "    duration: float\n",
    "    S: np.ndarray\n",
    "    power: np.ndarray\n",
    "    freqs: np.ndarray\n",
    "    mel: np.ndarray\n",
    "    logmel: np.ndarray\n",
    "    mfcc: np.ndarray\n",
    "    rms: np.ndarray\n",
    "    rms_db: np.ndarray\n",
    "    vad_mask: np.ndarray\n",
    "    segments: list = field(default_factory=list)\n",
    "    vad_info: dict = field(default_factory=dict)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- decode\n",
    "def decode_audio(source, target_sr: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, dict]:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Decode a path or raw bytes to mono float32 at ``target_sr``.\"\"\"\n",
    "    meta: dict = {\"decode_backend\": None}\n",
    "    data = None\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import soundfile as sf\n",
    "\n",
    "        handle = io.BytesIO(source) if isinstance(source, (bytes, bytearray)) else str(source)\n",
    "        data, sr = sf.read(handle, dtype=\"float32\", always_2d=True)\n",
    "        meta[\"decode_backend\"] = \"soundfile\"\n",
    "    except Exception as first:\n",
    "        import librosa\n",
    "\n",
    "        path, tmp = source, None\n",
    "        if isinstance(source, (bytes, bytearray)):\n",
    "            fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(suffix=\".audio\")\n",
    "            with os.fdopen(fd, \"wb\") as fh:\n",
    "                fh.write(source)\n",
    "            path = tmp\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            y, sr = librosa.load(str(path), sr=None, mono=False)\n",
    "            data = (y[:, None] if y.ndim == 1 else y.T).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "            meta[\"decode_backend\"] = \"librosa\"\n",
    "            meta[\"soundfile_error\"] = f\"{type(first).__name__}\"\n",
    "        finally:\n",
    "            if tmp:\n",
    "                os.unlink(tmp)\n",
    "    meta[\"orig_sr\"] = int(sr)\n",
    "    meta[\"channels\"] = int(data.shape[1])\n",
    "    meta[\"n_samples_orig\"] = int(data.shape[0])\n",
    "    y = data.mean(axis=1) if data.shape[1] > 1 else data[:, 0]\n",
    "    bad = ~np.isfinite(y)\n",
    "    meta[\"n_invalid_values\"] = int(bad.sum())\n",
    "    if bad.any():\n",
    "        y = np.where(bad, 0.0, y).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "    if int(sr) != int(target_sr) and len(y) > 0:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            import librosa\n",
    "\n",
    "            y = librosa.resample(y, orig_sr=int(sr), target_sr=int(target_sr), res_type=\"soxr_hq\")\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            from scipy.signal import resample_poly\n",
    "\n",
    "            g = np.gcd(int(sr), int(target_sr))\n",
    "            y = resample_poly(y, int(target_sr) // g, int(sr) // g).astype(np.float32)\n",
    "    meta[\"resampled\"] = int(sr) != int(target_sr)\n",
    "    return np.ascontiguousarray(y, dtype=np.float32), meta\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- VAD\n",
    "def _hysteresis(values: np.ndarray, on: float, off: float) -> np.ndarray:\n",
    "    mask = np.zeros(len(values), dtype=bool)\n",
    "    state = False\n",
    "    for i, v in enumerate(values):\n",
    "        if not state and v >= on:\n",
    "            state = True\n",
    "        elif state and v < off:\n",
    "            state = False\n",
    "        mask[i] = state\n",
    "    return mask\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _clean_mask(mask: np.ndarray, hop_s: float, min_speech_s: float, min_silence_s: float) -> np.ndarray:\n",
    "    mask = mask.copy()\n",
    "    def runs(m, value):\n",
    "        out, start = [], None\n",
    "        for i, v in enumerate(np.append(m, not value)):\n",
    "            if v == value and start is None:\n",
    "                start = i\n",
    "            elif v != value and start is not None:\n",
    "                out.append((start, i))\n",
    "                start = None\n",
    "        return out\n",
    "    for s, e in runs(mask, False):\n",
    "        if s > 0 and e < len(mask) and (e - s) * hop_s < min_silence_s:\n",
    "            mask[s:e] = True\n",
    "    for s, e in runs(mask, True):\n",
    "        if (e - s) * hop_s < min_speech_s:\n",
    "            mask[s:e] = False\n",
    "    return mask\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def energy_vad(rms_db: np.ndarray, hop_s: float, cfg: dict) -> tuple[np.ndarray, dict]:\n",
    "    finite = rms_db[np.isfinite(rms_db)]\n",
    "    if len(finite) == 0:\n",
    "        return np.zeros(len(rms_db), bool), {\"vad_status\": \"NO_FRAMES\"}\n",
    "    floor = float(np.percentile(finite, 10))\n",
    "    peak = float(np.percentile(finite, 99))\n",
    "    info = {\"vad_backend\": \"energy\", \"vad_noise_floor_db\": floor, \"vad_peak_db\": peak}\n",
    "    if peak - floor < float(cfg[\"vad_min_dynamic_range_db\"]):\n",
    "        info[\"vad_status\"] = \"LOW_DYNAMIC_RANGE\"\n",
    "        return np.zeros(len(rms_db), bool), info\n",
    "    on = max(floor + float(cfg[\"vad_energy_offset_db\"]), peak - float(cfg[\"vad_max_below_peak_db\"]))\n",
    "    mask = _hysteresis(rms_db, on, on - 3.0)\n",
    "    mask = _clean_mask(mask, hop_s, float(cfg[\"vad_min_speech_s\"]), float(cfg[\"vad_min_silence_s\"]))\n",
    "    info.update({\"vad_status\": \"OK\", \"vad_threshold_db\": on})\n",
    "    return mask, info\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def webrtc_vad(y: np.ndarray, sr: int, n_frames: int, hop: int, cfg: dict) -> tuple[np.ndarray, dict]:\n",
    "    import webrtcvad  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "    if sr not in (8000, 16000, 32000, 48000):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"webrtcvad requires 8/16/32/48 kHz audio\")\n",
    "    vad = webrtcvad.Vad(int(cfg[\"vad_webrtc_aggressiveness\"]))\n",
    "    frame = int(0.03 * sr)\n",
    "    pcm = (np.clip(y, -1, 1) * 32767).astype(np.int16)\n",
    "    flags = []\n",
    "    for start in range(0, len(pcm) - frame + 1, frame):\n",
    "        flags.append(vad.is_speech(pcm[start:start + frame].tobytes(), sr))\n",
    "    flags = np.array(flags, dtype=bool)\n",
    "    times = (np.arange(n_frames) * hop) // frame\n",
    "    mask = flags[np.clip(times, 0, max(len(flags) - 1, 0))] if len(flags) else np.zeros(n_frames, bool)\n",
    "    mask = _clean_mask(mask, hop / sr, float(cfg[\"vad_min_speech_s\"]), float(cfg[\"vad_min_silence_s\"]))\n",
    "    return mask, {\"vad_backend\": \"webrtc\", \"vad_status\": \"OK\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "_SILERO = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def silero_local_vad(y: np.ndarray, sr: int, n_frames: int, hop: int, cfg: dict) -> tuple[np.ndarray, dict]:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Silero VAD from a user-supplied local TorchScript file (license verified by the user).\"\"\"\n",
    "    import torch  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "    if not cfg.get(\"vad_model_path\"):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"vad_model_path required for silero_local\")\n",
    "    path = str(cfg[\"vad_model_path\"])\n",
    "    if path not in _SILERO:\n",
    "        _SILERO[path] = torch.jit.load(path, map_location=\"cpu\").eval()\n",
    "    model = _SILERO[path]\n",
    "    window = 512 if sr == 16000 else 256\n",
    "    probs = []\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        if hasattr(model, \"reset_states\"):\n",
    "            model.reset_states()\n",
    "        for start in range(0, len(y) - window + 1, window):\n",
    "            chunk = torch.from_numpy(y[start:start + window].copy())\n",
    "            probs.append(float(model(chunk, sr).item()))\n",
    "    probs = np.array(probs)\n",
    "    times = (np.arange(n_frames) * hop) // window\n",
    "    mask = probs[np.clip(times, 0, max(len(probs) - 1, 0))] >= 0.5 if len(probs) else np.zeros(n_frames, bool)\n",
    "    mask = _clean_mask(mask, hop / sr, float(cfg[\"vad_min_speech_s\"]), float(cfg[\"vad_min_silence_s\"]))\n",
    "    return mask, {\"vad_backend\": \"silero_local\", \"vad_status\": \"OK\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def mask_to_segments(mask: np.ndarray, hop_s: float, duration: float) -> list:\n",
    "    segs, start = [], None\n",
    "    for i, v in enumerate(np.append(mask, False)):\n",
    "        if v and start is None:\n",
    "            start = i\n",
    "        elif not v and start is not None:\n",
    "            segs.append((start * hop_s, min(i * hop_s, duration)))\n",
    "            start = None\n",
    "    return [(float(s), float(e)) for s, e in segs if e > s]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------- bundle\n",
    "def compute_bundle(y: np.ndarray, sr: int, cfg: dict) -> SignalBundle:\n",
    "    import librosa\n",
    "\n",
    "    n_fft, hop, win = int(cfg[\"n_fft\"]), int(cfg[\"hop_length\"]), int(cfg[\"win_length\"])\n",
    "    duration = len(y) / sr\n",
    "    yy = y if len(y) >= n_fft else np.pad(y, (0, n_fft - len(y)))\n",
    "    S = np.abs(librosa.stft(yy, n_fft=n_fft, hop_length=hop, win_length=win, center=True))\n",
    "    power = S ** 2\n",
    "    freqs = librosa.fft_frequencies(sr=sr, n_fft=n_fft)\n",
    "    mel = librosa.feature.melspectrogram(S=power, sr=sr, n_mels=int(cfg[\"n_mels\"]), fmax=sr / 2)\n",
    "    logmel = librosa.power_to_db(mel, ref=1.0, amin=1e-10, top_db=None)\n",
    "    mfcc = librosa.feature.mfcc(S=logmel, n_mfcc=int(cfg[\"n_mfcc\"]))\n",
    "    rms = librosa.feature.rms(y=yy, frame_length=n_fft, hop_length=hop, center=True)[0]\n",
    "    T = S.shape[1]\n",
    "    rms = np.resize(rms, T) if len(rms) != T else rms\n",
    "    rms_db = 20 * np.log10(np.maximum(rms, EPS))\n",
    "    hop_s = hop / sr\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"enable_vad\", True):\n",
    "        backend = cfg.get(\"vad_backend\", \"energy\")\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            if backend == \"webrtc\":\n",
    "                mask, info = webrtc_vad(yy, sr, T, hop, cfg)\n",
    "            elif backend == \"silero_local\":\n",
    "                mask, info = silero_local_vad(yy, sr, T, hop, cfg)\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                mask, info = energy_vad(rms_db, hop_s, cfg)\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:\n",
    "            mask, info = energy_vad(rms_db, hop_s, cfg)\n",
    "            info[\"vad_fallback_reason\"] = f\"{backend}: {type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\"\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        mask, info = np.ones(T, bool), {\"vad_backend\": \"disabled\", \"vad_status\": \"DISABLED\"}\n",
    "    segments = mask_to_segments(mask, hop_s, duration)\n",
    "    return SignalBundle(y=yy.astype(np.float32), sr=sr, n_fft=n_fft, hop=hop, win=win, duration=duration, S=S,\n",
    "                        power=power, freqs=freqs, mel=mel, logmel=logmel, mfcc=mfcc, rms=rms, rms_db=rms_db,\n",
    "                        vad_mask=mask, segments=segments, vad_info=info)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def quality_features(y: np.ndarray, b: SignalBundle, cfg: dict) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Signal-quality descriptors. SNR and noise floor are explicitly approximate.\"\"\"\n",
    "    out: dict = {}\n",
    "    dur = len(y) / b.sr\n",
    "    peak = float(np.max(np.abs(y))) if len(y) else 0.0\n",
    "    rms = float(np.sqrt(np.mean(y ** 2))) if len(y) else 0.0\n",
    "    out[\"q_duration_s\"] = dur\n",
    "    out[\"q_peak\"] = peak\n",
    "    out[\"q_rms\"] = rms\n",
    "    out[\"q_rms_db\"] = float(20 * np.log10(max(rms, EPS)))\n",
    "    out[\"q_dc_offset\"] = float(np.mean(y)) if len(y) else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_crest_factor\"] = float(peak / rms) if rms > 0 else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_clip_ratio\"] = float(np.mean(np.abs(y) >= float(cfg[\"clip_level_threshold\"]))) if len(y) else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_near_zero_ratio\"] = float(np.mean(np.abs(y) < 1e-4)) if len(y) else np.nan\n",
    "    finite = b.rms_db[np.isfinite(b.rms_db)]\n",
    "    out[\"q_dynamic_range_db\"] = float(np.percentile(finite, 99) - np.percentile(finite, 5)) if len(finite) else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_noise_floor_db_approx\"] = float(np.percentile(finite, 10)) if len(finite) else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_noise_floor_db\"] = out[\"q_noise_floor_db_approx\"]\n",
    "    speech = b.rms_db[b.vad_mask[:len(b.rms_db)]]\n",
    "    out[\"q_speech_level_db_approx\"] = float(np.median(speech)) if len(speech) else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_snr_db_approx\"] = (out[\"q_speech_level_db_approx\"] - out[\"q_noise_floor_db_approx\"]) if len(speech) else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_silence_ratio\"] = float(1 - b.vad_mask.mean()) if len(b.vad_mask) else np.nan\n",
    "    mean_spec = b.power.mean(axis=1) + EPS\n",
    "    total = mean_spec.sum()\n",
    "    for name, lo, hi in ((\"low\", 0, 300), (\"mid\", 300, 3400), (\"high\", 3400, b.sr / 2 + 1)):\n",
    "        out[f\"q_band_energy_{name}_rel\"] = float(mean_spec[(b.freqs >= lo) & (b.freqs < hi)].sum() / total)\n",
    "    out[\"q_spectral_flatness\"] = float(np.exp(np.mean(np.log(mean_spec))) / np.mean(mean_spec))\n",
    "    cum = np.cumsum(mean_spec) / total\n",
    "    out[\"q_eff_bandwidth_hz\"] = float(b.freqs[np.argmax(cum >= 0.99)])\n",
    "    out[\"q_flag_short\"] = float(dur < 0.3)\n",
    "    out[\"q_flag_silent\"] = float(peak < 1e-4)\n",
    "    out[\"q_flag_clipping\"] = float(out[\"q_clip_ratio\"] > 0.001) if np.isfinite(out[\"q_clip_ratio\"]) else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_flag_low_snr\"] = float(out[\"q_snr_db_approx\"] < 10) if np.isfinite(out[\"q_snr_db_approx\"]) else 1.0\n",
    "    out[\"q_flag_dc\"] = float(abs(out[\"q_dc_offset\"]) > 0.01) if np.isfinite(out[\"q_dc_offset\"]) else np.nan\n",
    "    out[\"q_flag_narrowband\"] = float(out[\"q_eff_bandwidth_hz\"] < 0.45 * b.sr / 2)\n",
    "    out[\"q_flag_no_speech\"] = float(len(b.segments) == 0)\n",
    "    flags = [v for k, v in out.items() if k.startswith(\"q_flag_\") and np.isfinite(v)]\n",
    "    out[\"q_n_flags\"] = float(np.sum(flags))\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def process_clip(task: dict, cfg: dict) -> tuple[dict, list]:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Decode one recording and compute all enabled feature families.\"\"\"\n",
    "    from .prosody_features import prosody_features\n",
    "    from .spectral_features import mfcc_features, spectral_features\n",
    "    from .temporal_features import temporal_features\n",
    "    from .wavelet_features import wavelet_features\n",
    "\n",
    "    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "    rec: dict = {\"clip_id\": task[\"clip_id\"], \"proc_status\": \"OK\", \"proc_error\": \"\"}\n",
    "    segs: list = []\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        source = task.get(\"bytes\") if task.get(\"bytes\") is not None else task[\"path\"]\n",
    "        y, meta = decode_audio(source, int(cfg[\"sample_rate\"]))\n",
    "        rec.update({f\"meta_{k}\": v for k, v in meta.items() if isinstance(v, (int, float, bool))})\n",
    "        rec[\"meta_decode_backend\"] = meta.get(\"decode_backend\")\n",
    "        if meta[\"n_invalid_values\"]:\n",
    "            rec[\"proc_status\"] = \"INVALID_VALUES_REPLACED\"\n",
    "        if len(y) == 0:\n",
    "            rec[\"proc_status\"] = \"EMPTY\"\n",
    "            return rec, segs\n",
    "        dur = len(y) / int(cfg[\"sample_rate\"])\n",
    "        if dur < float(cfg[\"min_audio_duration_s\"]):\n",
    "            rec[\"proc_status\"] = \"TOO_SHORT\"\n",
    "            rec[\"q_duration_s\"] = dur\n",
    "            return rec, segs\n",
    "        if np.ptp(y) == 0:\n",
    "            rec[\"proc_status\"] = \"CONSTANT\"\n",
    "            rec[\"q_duration_s\"] = dur\n",
    "            return rec, segs\n",
    "        if dur > float(cfg[\"max_audio_duration_s\"]):\n",
    "            y = y[: int(float(cfg[\"max_audio_duration_s\"]) * int(cfg[\"sample_rate\"]))]\n",
    "            rec[\"proc_status\"] = \"TRUNCATED_LONG\"\n",
    "        with np.errstate(all=\"ignore\"):\n",
    "            b = compute_bundle(y, int(cfg[\"sample_rate\"]), cfg)\n",
    "            segs = b.segments\n",
    "            rec.update({f\"vad_{k}\" if not k.startswith(\"vad_\") else k: v for k, v in b.vad_info.items()})\n",
    "            rec.update(quality_features(y, b, cfg))\n",
    "            if np.max(np.abs(y)) < 1e-5:\n",
    "                rec[\"proc_status\"] = \"SILENT\"\n",
    "            rec.update(temporal_features(b, cfg))\n",
    "            rec.update(spectral_features(b, cfg))\n",
    "            rec.update(mfcc_features(b, cfg))\n",
    "            if cfg.get(\"enable_wavelets\"):\n",
    "                rec.update(wavelet_features(b, cfg))\n",
    "            if cfg.get(\"enable_prosody\"):\n",
    "                rec.update(prosody_features(b, cfg))\n",
    "    except Exception as exc:\n",
    "        rec[\"proc_status\"] = \"FAILED\"\n",
    "        rec[\"proc_error\"] = f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {str(exc)[:300]}\"\n",
    "    rec[\"proc_seconds\"] = time.perf_counter() - t0\n",
    "    for k, v in list(rec.items()):\n",
    "        if isinstance(v, (np.floating, np.integer)):\n",
    "            rec[k] = v.item()\n",
    "    return rec, segs\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# --------------------------------------------------------------- unified extraction\n",
    "def feature_version_hash(cfg: dict) -> str:\n",
    "    return subset_hash(cfg, list(EXTRACTION_KEYS))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _audio_sources(ctx, clips: pd.DataFrame, split: str) -> tuple[pd.DataFrame, str]:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return clip rows with a file path (extracted) or the archive for streaming.\"\"\"\n",
    "    from . import audio_manifest as am\n",
    "    from .environment import disk_free_bytes\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    archive = ctx.data_root() / (\"train_audio.tar\" if split == \"train\" else \"test_audio.tar\")\n",
    "    dest = ctx.paths.extracted_train if split == \"train\" else ctx.paths.extracted_test\n",
    "    extract = cfg[\"extract_train_audio\"] if split == \"train\" else cfg[\"extract_test_audio\"]\n",
    "    members = clips[\"audio_member\"].dropna().unique().tolist()\n",
    "    if extract:\n",
    "        manifest = ctx.load_df(\"audio_manifest\")\n",
    "        sizes = manifest[(manifest[\"archive\"] == archive.name) & manifest[\"member\"].isin(members)]\n",
    "        report = am.safe_extract(archive, dest, members, disk_free_bytes(dest), float(cfg[\"disk_safety_factor\"]),\n",
    "                                 float(cfg[\"min_free_disk_gb\"]), ctx.logger)\n",
    "        ctx.logger.info(\"Extraction %s: %s (members %d, %.2f GB)\", split, report[\"status\"], len(members),\n",
    "                        sizes[\"size_bytes\"].sum() / 1e9)\n",
    "        clips = clips.assign(path=clips[\"audio_member\"].map(lambda m: str(dest / Path(*str(m).split(\"/\"))) if pd.notna(m) else None))\n",
    "        return clips, \"file\"\n",
    "    return clips.assign(path=None), \"stream\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_unified_extraction(ctx, split: str = \"train\") -> tuple[pd.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame]:\n",
    "    from joblib import Parallel, delayed\n",
    "\n",
    "    from . import audio_manifest as am\n",
    "    from .environment import resolve_n_jobs\n",
    "    from .logging_utils import progress\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    clips = ctx.load_df(\"clip_master\")\n",
    "    clips = clips[(clips[\"split\"] == split) & clips[\"audio_member\"].notna()].copy()\n",
    "    fhash = feature_version_hash(cfg)\n",
    "    cache_dir = ctx.paths.cache_dir(\"acoustic\") / f\"{split}_{fhash}\"\n",
    "    seg_dir = ctx.paths.cache_dir(\"vad\") / f\"{split}_{fhash}\"\n",
    "    cache_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    seg_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"overwrite_cache\"):\n",
    "        for p in list(cache_dir.glob(\"chunk_*.parquet\")) + list(seg_dir.glob(\"chunk_*.parquet\")):\n",
    "            p.unlink()\n",
    "    done: set = set()\n",
    "    for p in sorted(cache_dir.glob(\"chunk_*.parquet\")):\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            done |= set(pd.read_parquet(p, columns=[\"clip_id\"])[\"clip_id\"])\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            ctx.logger.warning(\"Removing unreadable cache chunk %s\", p)\n",
    "            p.unlink()\n",
    "    todo = clips[~clips[\"clip_id\"].isin(done)]\n",
    "    ctx.logger.info(\"Unified extraction %s: %d clips cached, %d to process\", split, len(done), len(todo))\n",
    "    if len(todo):\n",
    "        todo, mode = _audio_sources(ctx, todo, split)\n",
    "        # duration-aware scheduling: interleave long and short recordings across chunks\n",
    "        if \"audio_duration_s\" in todo.columns:\n",
    "            todo = todo.sort_values(\"audio_duration_s\", ascending=False, na_position=\"last\")\n",
    "            order = np.argsort(np.arange(len(todo)) % max(1, int(np.ceil(len(todo) / int(cfg[\"extraction_chunk_size\"])))), kind=\"stable\")\n",
    "            todo = todo.iloc[order]\n",
    "        archive = ctx.data_root() / (\"train_audio.tar\" if split == \"train\" else \"test_audio.tar\")\n",
    "        fcfg = extraction_config(cfg)\n",
    "        n_jobs = resolve_n_jobs(int(cfg[\"n_jobs\"]))\n",
    "        size = int(cfg[\"extraction_chunk_size\"])\n",
    "        start_idx = len(list(cache_dir.glob(\"chunk_*.parquet\")))\n",
    "        for ci, start in enumerate(progress(range(0, len(todo), size), total=int(np.ceil(len(todo) / size)),\n",
    "                                            desc=f\"extract {split}\")):\n",
    "            chunk = todo.iloc[start:start + size]\n",
    "            tasks = []\n",
    "            if mode == \"stream\":\n",
    "                blobs = am.read_member_bytes(archive, chunk[\"audio_member\"].tolist())\n",
    "                for _, r in chunk.iterrows():\n",
    "                    tasks.append({\"clip_id\": r[\"clip_id\"], \"bytes\": blobs.get(r[\"audio_member\"]), \"path\": None})\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                tasks = [{\"clip_id\": r[\"clip_id\"], \"path\": r[\"path\"], \"bytes\": None} for _, r in chunk.iterrows()]\n",
    "            tasks = [t for t in tasks if t[\"bytes\"] is not None or t[\"path\"]]\n",
    "            results = Parallel(n_jobs=n_jobs, backend=\"loky\", batch_size=\"auto\")(\n",
    "                delayed(process_clip)(t, fcfg) for t in tasks)\n",
    "            feats = pd.DataFrame([r for r, _ in results])\n",
    "            seg_rows = [{\"clip_id\": r[\"clip_id\"], \"seg_index\": i, \"start_s\": s, \"end_s\": e}\n",
    "                        for (r, segs) in results for i, (s, e) in enumerate(segs)]\n",
    "            idx = start_idx + ci\n",
    "            atomic_write_parquet(pd.DataFrame(seg_rows, columns=[\"clip_id\", \"seg_index\", \"start_s\", \"end_s\"]),\n",
    "                                 seg_dir / f\"chunk_{idx:05d}.parquet\")\n",
    "            atomic_write_parquet(feats, cache_dir / f\"chunk_{idx:05d}.parquet\")\n",
    "            del results, feats, tasks\n",
    "            gc.collect()\n",
    "    parts = [pd.read_parquet(p) for p in sorted(cache_dir.glob(\"chunk_*.parquet\"))]\n",
    "    features = pd.concat(parts, ignore_index=True, sort=False) if parts else pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"clip_id\"])\n",
    "    features = features.drop_duplicates(\"clip_id\", keep=\"last\")\n",
    "    features = features[features[\"clip_id\"].isin(set(clips[\"clip_id\"]))]\n",
    "    id_cols = [\"clip_id\", \"proc_status\", \"proc_error\", \"proc_seconds\"]\n",
    "    other = sorted(c for c in features.columns if c not in id_cols)\n",
    "    features = features[[c for c in id_cols if c in features.columns] + other]\n",
    "    sparts = [pd.read_parquet(p) for p in sorted(seg_dir.glob(\"chunk_*.parquet\"))]\n",
    "    segments = pd.concat(sparts, ignore_index=True) if sparts else pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"clip_id\", \"seg_index\", \"start_s\", \"end_s\"])\n",
    "    segments = segments[segments[\"clip_id\"].isin(set(features[\"clip_id\"]))].drop_duplicates([\"clip_id\", \"seg_index\"], keep=\"last\")\n",
    "    return features, segments\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- atlas\n",
    "def _anon(clip_id: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return hashlib.sha256(str(clip_id).encode()).hexdigest()[:10]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def select_atlas_examples(ctx, clips: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Systematic selection across task, correctness, ability, difficulty, target, quality, residual.\"\"\"\n",
    "    from . import data_access as da\n",
    "    from .stats_utils import quantile_bins\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "    df = clips[clips[\"proc_status\"].isin([\"OK\", \"INVALID_VALUES_REPLACED\", \"TRUNCATED_LONG\"])].copy()\n",
    "    if df.empty:\n",
    "        return df\n",
    "    sm = da.student_meta(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    df = df.merge(sm[[\"target\"]], left_on=\"student_id\", right_index=True, how=\"left\")\n",
    "    scr = da.screening(ctx) if ctx.stage_available(\"03\") else None\n",
    "    if scr is not None and \"theta_mean\" in scr.columns:\n",
    "        df = df.merge(scr[[\"theta_mean\"]], left_on=\"student_id\", right_index=True, how=\"left\")\n",
    "        df[\"stratum_ability\"] = quantile_bins(df[\"theta_mean\"], 3, 1, \"A\")\n",
    "    if \"item_b\" in df.columns:\n",
    "        df[\"stratum_difficulty\"] = quantile_bins(df[\"item_b\"], 3, 1, \"D\")\n",
    "    df[\"stratum_target\"] = quantile_bins(df[\"target\"], 5, 1, \"T\")\n",
    "    if \"q_snr_db_approx\" in df.columns:\n",
    "        df[\"stratum_quality\"] = quantile_bins(df[\"q_snr_db_approx\"], 3, 1, \"SNR\")\n",
    "    res = da.residuals(ctx)\n",
    "    if res is not None:\n",
    "        df[\"stratum_residual\"] = quantile_bins(df[\"student_id\"].map(res), 5, 1, \"R\")\n",
    "    dims = [\"task_family\", \"correct\"] + [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith(\"stratum_\")]\n",
    "    chosen = []\n",
    "    per = int(cfg[\"atlas_examples_per_stratum\"])\n",
    "    for dim in dims:\n",
    "        if dim not in df.columns:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        for level, g in df.dropna(subset=[dim]).groupby(dim):\n",
    "            pick = g.iloc[rng.choice(len(g), min(per, len(g)), replace=False)]\n",
    "            chosen.append(pick.assign(atlas_dimension=dim, atlas_level=str(level)))\n",
    "    if not chosen:\n",
    "        return df.head(0)\n",
    "    sel = pd.concat(chosen).drop_duplicates(\"clip_id\")\n",
    "    return sel.head(int(cfg[\"atlas_max_examples\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def render_atlas_example(ctx, row: pd.Series, source) -> None:\n",
    "    import librosa\n",
    "    import librosa.display  # noqa: F401\n",
    "\n",
    "    from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    y, _ = decode_audio(source, int(cfg[\"sample_rate\"]))\n",
    "    b = compute_bundle(y, int(cfg[\"sample_rate\"]), cfg)\n",
    "    sr, hop = b.sr, b.hop\n",
    "    t = np.arange(len(b.y)) / sr\n",
    "    tf = np.arange(b.S.shape[1]) * hop / sr\n",
    "    fig, axes = viz.new_figure(5, 2, (7, 2.4))\n",
    "    ax = axes.ravel()\n",
    "    ax[0].plot(t, b.y, lw=0.4)\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(ax[0], \"Waveform\", \"time [s]\", \"amplitude\")\n",
    "    ax[1].plot(tf, b.rms_db, lw=0.8)\n",
    "    ax[1].fill_between(tf, b.rms_db.min(), b.rms_db.max(), where=b.vad_mask, alpha=0.2, color=\"green\", label=\"speech-active (VAD)\")\n",
    "    ax[1].legend(fontsize=6)\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(ax[1], \"Energy envelope and VAD mask\", \"time [s]\", \"RMS [dB]\")\n",
    "    for a, data, title, unit in ((ax[2], 20 * np.log10(b.S + EPS), \"STFT magnitude\", \"dB\"),\n",
    "                                 (ax[3], np.sqrt(b.mel), \"Mel spectrogram (sqrt power)\", \"a.u.\"),\n",
    "                                 (ax[4], b.logmel, \"Log-Mel spectrogram\", \"dB\"),\n",
    "                                 (ax[5], b.mfcc, \"MFCC\", \"coef\")):\n",
    "        im = a.imshow(data, origin=\"lower\", aspect=\"auto\", extent=[0, tf[-1] if len(tf) else 1, 0, data.shape[0]])\n",
    "        fig.colorbar(im, ax=a, fraction=0.04).set_label(unit)\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(a, title, \"time [s]\", \"bin\")\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        f0, voiced, _ = librosa.pyin(b.y, fmin=float(cfg[\"f0_min_hz\"]), fmax=float(cfg[\"f0_max_hz\"]), sr=sr,\n",
    "                                     frame_length=1024, hop_length=hop)\n",
    "        ax[6].plot(np.arange(len(f0)) * hop / sr, f0, \".\", ms=2)\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        ax[6].text(0.5, 0.5, \"pitch unavailable\", ha=\"center\", transform=ax[6].transAxes)\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(ax[6], \"Pitch contour (anonymised voice)\", \"time [s]\", \"F0 [Hz]\")\n",
    "    flux = np.concatenate([[0], np.sqrt((np.clip(np.diff(np.log1p(b.S), axis=1), 0, None) ** 2).sum(axis=0))])\n",
    "    ax[7].plot(tf, flux, lw=0.7)\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(ax[7], \"Spectral flux\", \"time [s]\", \"flux\")\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import pywt\n",
    "        from scipy.signal import resample_poly\n",
    "\n",
    "        xd = resample_poly(b.y, 1, max(1, sr // int(cfg[\"cwt_sr\"])))[: int(float(cfg[\"cwt_max_seconds\"]) * int(cfg[\"cwt_sr\"]))]\n",
    "        freqs = np.geomspace(40, int(cfg[\"cwt_sr\"]) / 2 * 0.95, 48)\n",
    "        scales = pywt.central_frequency(\"morl\") * int(cfg[\"cwt_sr\"]) / freqs\n",
    "        coefs, pf = pywt.cwt(xd, scales, \"morl\", sampling_period=1 / int(cfg[\"cwt_sr\"]))\n",
    "        ax[8].imshow(np.log10(np.abs(coefs) ** 2 + EPS), aspect=\"auto\", origin=\"upper\",\n",
    "                     extent=[0, len(xd) / int(cfg[\"cwt_sr\"]), pf[-1], pf[0]])\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        ax[8].text(0.5, 0.5, \"scalogram unavailable\", ha=\"center\", transform=ax[8].transAxes)\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(ax[8], \"Morlet wavelet scalogram\", \"time [s]\", \"frequency [Hz]\")\n",
    "    ax[9].axis(\"off\")\n",
    "    ax[9].text(0.0, 0.9, \"\\n\".join([\n",
    "        f\"anonymous id: {_anon(row['clip_id'])}\", f\"task: {row.get('task_family')}\",\n",
    "        f\"correct: {row.get('correct')}\", f\"stratum: {row.get('atlas_dimension')}={row.get('atlas_level')}\",\n",
    "        f\"duration: {b.duration:.2f}s  segments: {len(b.segments)}\",\n",
    "        f\"SNR(approx): {row.get('q_snr_db_approx', np.nan):.1f} dB\"]), va=\"top\", fontsize=8)\n",
    "    ctx.figure(fig, f\"atlas_{row['atlas_dimension']}_{row['atlas_level']}_{_anon(row['clip_id'])}\",\n",
    "               \"Acoustic atlas example (training data, anonymous id)\",\n",
    "               \"What information is available in an anonymised recording?\", \"clip_features\", 1,\n",
    "               f\"Representative example for {row['atlas_dimension']}={row['atlas_level']}. Local use only.\", sub=\"atlas\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_acoustic_atlas(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    from . import audio_manifest as am\n",
    "    from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    outputs = []\n",
    "    feats, segs = run_unified_extraction(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(feats, \"clip_features\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(segs, \"vad_segments\")\n",
    "    outputs += [\"clip_features\", \"vad_segments\"]\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"allow_test_inference\") and cfg.get(\"extract_test_audio\"):\n",
    "        tf, tsegs = run_unified_extraction(ctx, \"test\")\n",
    "        ctx.save_df(tf, \"clip_features_test\")\n",
    "        ctx.save_df(tsegs, \"vad_segments_test\")\n",
    "        outputs += [\"clip_features_test\", \"vad_segments_test\"]\n",
    "    status = feats[\"proc_status\"].value_counts().rename_axis(\"proc_status\").reset_index(name=\"n\")\n",
    "    qcols = [c for c in feats.columns if c.startswith(\"q_\")]\n",
    "    summary = feats[qcols].describe(percentiles=[0.05, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 0.95]).T.reset_index().rename(columns={\"index\": \"feature\"})\n",
    "    flag_rates = feats[[c for c in qcols if c.startswith(\"q_flag_\")]].mean().rename(\"rate\").reset_index().rename(columns={\"index\": \"flag\"})\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(status, \"audio_processing_status\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(summary, \"audio_quality_summary\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(flag_rates, \"audio_quality_flag_rates\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    outputs += [\"audio_processing_status\", \"audio_quality_summary\", \"audio_quality_flag_rates\"]\n",
    "    show = [c for c in (\"q_duration_s\", \"q_snr_db_approx\", \"q_noise_floor_db_approx\", \"q_clip_ratio\",\n",
    "                        \"q_silence_ratio\", \"q_eff_bandwidth_hz\") if c in feats.columns]\n",
    "    if show:\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(2, 3, (4.5, 3.2))\n",
    "        for ax, c in zip(axes.ravel(), show):\n",
    "            viz.hist_kde(ax, feats[c], c)\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"audio_quality_distributions\", \"Audio quality distributions (training)\",\n",
    "                   \"How reliable is the acoustic information?\", \"clip_features\", int(len(feats)),\n",
    "                   \"; \".join(f\"{r.flag}={r.rate:.1%}\" for r in flag_rates.itertuples()))\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"atlas_enabled\"):\n",
    "        cm = ctx.load_df(\"clip_master\")\n",
    "        cm = cm[cm[\"split\"] == \"train\"]\n",
    "        merged = cm.merge(feats, on=\"clip_id\", how=\"inner\")\n",
    "        from . import data_access as da\n",
    "\n",
    "        diff = da.item_difficulty(ctx)\n",
    "        if diff is not None:\n",
    "            merged = merged.merge(diff.rename(columns={\"b\": \"item_b\"})[[\"item_key\", \"item_b\"]], on=\"item_key\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "        examples = select_atlas_examples(ctx, merged)\n",
    "        ctx.save_df(examples.assign(anonymous_id=examples[\"clip_id\"].map(_anon))[\n",
    "            [\"anonymous_id\", \"atlas_dimension\", \"atlas_level\", \"task_family\"]], \"atlas_examples\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "        outputs.append(\"atlas_examples\")\n",
    "        archive = ctx.data_root() / \"train_audio.tar\"\n",
    "        blobs = am.read_member_bytes(archive, examples[\"audio_member\"].tolist()) if not cfg[\"extract_train_audio\"] else {}\n",
    "        for _, row in examples.iterrows():\n",
    "            src = blobs.get(row[\"audio_member\"]) if blobs else str(ctx.paths.extracted_train / Path(*str(row[\"audio_member\"]).split(\"/\")))\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                render_atlas_example(ctx, row, src)\n",
    "            except Exception as exc:\n",
    "                ctx.logger.warning(\"Atlas example failed: %s\", exc)\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": outputs, \"summary\": {\"n_clips\": int(len(feats)), \"status\": status.set_index(\"proc_status\")[\"n\"].to_dict(),\n",
    "                                            \"feature_version\": feature_version_hash(cfg), \"n_features\": int(feats.shape[1])}}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-008",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/baseline_models.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 14 - cross-validation partitions and screening-only baselines.\n",
    "\n",
    "Models: M00_MEAN, M01_RIDGE, M02_ELASTIC_NET, M03_GAM_OR_SPLINE_RIDGE,\n",
    "M04_CATBOOST, M05_SHALLOW_XGBOOST, M06_PLS. Optional libraries that are not\n",
    "installed are reported as MODEL_UNAVAILABLE (never silently substituted).\n",
    "All preprocessing (imputation, scaling, spline bases, PLS components,\n",
    "supervised feature selection) is inside the model pipeline, i.e. fitted on\n",
    "training folds only. Hyper-parameters are tuned by internal CV within the\n",
    "training fold (RidgeCV / ElasticNetCV / GridSearchCV).\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.base import BaseEstimator, TransformerMixin\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "from .validation import (SCHEMES, available_schemes, group_performance, make_cv_assignments, pooled_predictions,\n",
    "                         quantile_performance, run_cv)\n",
    "\n",
    "BASELINE_MODELS = {\"M00_MEAN\": \"MEAN\", \"M01_RIDGE\": \"RIDGE\", \"M02_ELASTIC_NET\": \"ELASTIC_NET\",\n",
    "                   \"M03_GAM_OR_SPLINE_RIDGE\": \"SPLINE_RIDGE\", \"M04_CATBOOST\": \"CATBOOST\",\n",
    "                   \"M05_SHALLOW_XGBOOST\": \"XGBOOST\", \"M06_PLS\": \"PLS\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class ModelUnavailable(ImportError):\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class NanSafeKBest(BaseEstimator, TransformerMixin):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Keep the k columns with the largest |Spearman| with y (training fold only).\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, k: int = 300):\n",
    "        self.k = k\n",
    "\n",
    "    def fit(self, X, y):\n",
    "        X = np.asarray(X, dtype=float)\n",
    "        y = np.asarray(y, dtype=float)\n",
    "        if X.shape[1] <= self.k:\n",
    "            self.support_ = np.arange(X.shape[1])\n",
    "            return self\n",
    "        Xr = pd.DataFrame(X).rank().to_numpy()\n",
    "        yr = pd.Series(y).rank().to_numpy()\n",
    "        scores = np.zeros(X.shape[1])\n",
    "        for j in range(X.shape[1]):\n",
    "            m = np.isfinite(Xr[:, j])\n",
    "            if m.sum() > 10 and np.std(Xr[m, j]) > 0:\n",
    "                scores[j] = abs(np.corrcoef(Xr[m, j], yr[m])[0, 1])\n",
    "        self.support_ = np.sort(np.argsort(-np.nan_to_num(scores))[: self.k])\n",
    "        return self\n",
    "\n",
    "    def transform(self, X):\n",
    "        return np.asarray(X, dtype=float)[:, self.support_]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class PLS1D(BaseEstimator):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, n_components: int = 2):\n",
    "        self.n_components = n_components\n",
    "\n",
    "    def fit(self, X, y):\n",
    "        from sklearn.cross_decomposition import PLSRegression\n",
    "\n",
    "        self.model_ = PLSRegression(n_components=max(1, min(self.n_components, X.shape[1], X.shape[0] - 1)))\n",
    "        self.model_.fit(X, y)\n",
    "        return self\n",
    "\n",
    "    def predict(self, X):\n",
    "        return np.asarray(self.model_.predict(X)).ravel()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_model(kind: str, cfg: dict, n_features: int = 1, n_samples: int = 100):\n",
    "    from sklearn.dummy import DummyRegressor\n",
    "    from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "    from sklearn.linear_model import ElasticNetCV, RidgeCV\n",
    "    from sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV, KFold\n",
    "    from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "    from sklearn.preprocessing import SplineTransformer, StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "    seed = int(cfg[\"seed\"])\n",
    "    k = int(cfg.get(\"ablation_max_features\", 300))\n",
    "    inner = KFold(int(cfg[\"inner_cv_folds\"]), shuffle=True, random_state=seed)\n",
    "    impute = (\"impute\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\", add_indicator=True, keep_empty_features=False))\n",
    "    select = [(\"select\", NanSafeKBest(k))] if n_features > k else []\n",
    "    kind = kind.upper()\n",
    "    if kind == \"MEAN\":\n",
    "        return DummyRegressor(strategy=\"mean\")\n",
    "    if kind == \"RIDGE\":\n",
    "        return Pipeline(select + [impute, (\"scale\", StandardScaler()), (\"model\", RidgeCV(alphas=np.logspace(-3, 4, 30)))])\n",
    "    if kind == \"ELASTIC_NET\":\n",
    "        return Pipeline(select + [impute, (\"scale\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "                                  (\"model\", ElasticNetCV(l1_ratio=[0.1, 0.5, 0.9], n_alphas=30, cv=inner, max_iter=5000,\n",
    "                                                         random_state=seed))])\n",
    "    if kind == \"SPLINE_RIDGE\":\n",
    "        return Pipeline(select + [impute, (\"scale\", StandardScaler()), (\"spline\", SplineTransformer(n_knots=5, degree=3)),\n",
    "                                  (\"model\", RidgeCV(alphas=np.logspace(-2, 5, 30)))])\n",
    "    if kind == \"PLS\":\n",
    "        grid = [c for c in (1, 2, 3, 5, 8) if c <= max(1, min(n_features, 8))]\n",
    "        return Pipeline(select + [impute, (\"scale\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "                                  (\"model\", GridSearchCV(PLS1D(), {\"n_components\": grid}, cv=inner, scoring=\"neg_mean_squared_error\"))])\n",
    "    if kind == \"CATBOOST\":\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            from catboost import CatBoostRegressor  # type: ignore\n",
    "        except ImportError as exc:\n",
    "            raise ModelUnavailable(\"catboost not installed\") from exc\n",
    "        return Pipeline(select + [(\"model\", CatBoostRegressor(depth=4, iterations=600, learning_rate=0.03, l2_leaf_reg=6,\n",
    "                                                               loss_function=\"RMSE\", random_seed=seed, verbose=False,\n",
    "                                                               thread_count=max(1, int(cfg.get(\"n_jobs_model\", 4)))))])\n",
    "    if kind == \"XGBOOST\":\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            from xgboost import XGBRegressor  # type: ignore\n",
    "        except ImportError as exc:\n",
    "            raise ModelUnavailable(\"xgboost not installed\") from exc\n",
    "        return Pipeline(select + [(\"model\", XGBRegressor(max_depth=2, n_estimators=400, learning_rate=0.03, subsample=0.8,\n",
    "                                                          colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_lambda=5.0, min_child_weight=5,\n",
    "                                                          tree_method=\"hist\", random_state=seed, n_jobs=4))])\n",
    "    if kind == \"LIGHTGBM\":\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            from lightgbm import LGBMRegressor  # type: ignore\n",
    "        except ImportError as exc:\n",
    "            raise ModelUnavailable(\"lightgbm not installed\") from exc\n",
    "        return Pipeline(select + [(\"model\", LGBMRegressor(num_leaves=7, max_depth=3, n_estimators=400, learning_rate=0.03,\n",
    "                                                           min_child_samples=20, subsample=0.8, subsample_freq=1,\n",
    "                                                           colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_lambda=5.0, random_state=seed,\n",
    "                                                           verbose=-1, n_jobs=4))])\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"unknown model kind {kind}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def model_available(kind: str, cfg: dict) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        make_model(kind, cfg)\n",
    "        return True, \"\"\n",
    "    except ModelUnavailable as exc:\n",
    "        return False, str(exc)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_fit_predict(builder, families, kind: str, cfg: dict, y: pd.Series):\n",
    "    def fit_predict(train_ids, val_ids, key):\n",
    "        Xtr, Xva = builder.build(train_ids, val_ids, families, key)\n",
    "        model = make_model(kind, cfg, n_features=Xtr.shape[1], n_samples=len(Xtr))\n",
    "        if Xtr.shape[1] == 0:\n",
    "            return np.full(len(Xva), float(y.loc[train_ids].mean()))\n",
    "        model.fit(Xtr, y.loc[train_ids].to_numpy())\n",
    "        return model.predict(Xva)\n",
    "    return fit_predict\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def residual_groups(res: pd.Series, quantiles) -> pd.Series:\n",
    "    lo, hi = res.quantile(quantiles[0]), res.quantile(quantiles[1])\n",
    "    return pd.Series(np.where(res <= lo, \"NEGATIVE_RESIDUAL\", np.where(res >= hi, \"POSITIVE_RESIDUAL\", \"EXPECTED_OUTCOME\")),\n",
    "                     index=res.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_validation_and_baseline(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    from .fold_features import FoldFeatureBuilder\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    meta = da.student_meta(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    meta = meta[meta[\"target\"].notna()]\n",
    "    y = meta[\"target\"].astype(float)\n",
    "    assign, status = make_cv_assignments(meta, cfg)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(assign, \"cv_assignments\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_json(status, \"cv_scheme_status\")\n",
    "    scr = da.screening(ctx)\n",
    "    base = scr.loc[scr.index.intersection(y.index)]\n",
    "    builder = FoldFeatureBuilder(ctx, base=base)\n",
    "    schools = meta[\"school_id\"] if meta[\"school_id\"].notna().any() else None\n",
    "    results, oofs, registry = [], [], []\n",
    "    primary = cfg[\"primary_baseline\"]\n",
    "    primary_res = None\n",
    "    for name, kind in BASELINE_MODELS.items():\n",
    "        ok, reason = model_available(kind, cfg)\n",
    "        registry.append({\"model_id\": name, \"kind\": kind, \"available\": ok, \"reason\": reason, \"families\": \"SCREENING\",\n",
    "                         \"features\": \",\".join(builder.columns_for({\"SCREENING\"}) + [\"theta_common_factor (fold-fitted)\"])})\n",
    "        if not ok:\n",
    "            results.append({\"model_id\": name, \"scheme\": \"ALL\", \"status\": \"MODEL_UNAVAILABLE\", \"reason\": reason})\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        fp = make_fit_predict(builder, {\"SCREENING\"}, kind, cfg, y)\n",
    "        for scheme in available_schemes(assign):\n",
    "            res = run_cv(y, assign, scheme, fp, cfg, groups=schools, label=name)\n",
    "            results.append({\"model_id\": name, \"scheme\": scheme, **res.summary})\n",
    "            oofs.append(res.oof.assign(model_id=name, scheme=scheme))\n",
    "            if name == primary and scheme == cfg[\"primary_cv_scheme\"]:\n",
    "                primary_res = res\n",
    "        ctx.logger.info(\"Baseline %s done\", name)\n",
    "    results_df = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
    "    oof_df = pd.concat(oofs, ignore_index=True) if oofs else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(results_df, \"baseline_results\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(oof_df, \"baseline_oof_predictions\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.DataFrame(registry), \"baseline_model_registry\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    if primary_res is None:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(f\"primary baseline {primary} under {cfg['primary_cv_scheme']} unavailable\")\n",
    "    pooled = pooled_predictions(primary_res.oof)\n",
    "    residual = (pooled[\"y\"] - pooled[\"pred\"]).rename(\"residual\")\n",
    "    res_df = pd.DataFrame({\"student_id\": pooled.index, \"y\": pooled[\"y\"].to_numpy(), \"oof_prediction\": pooled[\"pred\"].to_numpy(),\n",
    "                           \"residual\": residual.to_numpy(), \"n_oof_predictions\": pooled[\"n_preds\"].to_numpy(),\n",
    "                           \"residual_group\": residual_groups(residual, cfg[\"residual_group_quantiles\"]).to_numpy(),\n",
    "                           \"model_id\": primary, \"scheme\": cfg[\"primary_cv_scheme\"]})\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(res_df, \"baseline_residuals\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    qp = quantile_performance(pooled)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(qp, \"baseline_quantile_performance\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    outputs = [\"cv_assignments\", \"cv_scheme_status\", \"baseline_results\", \"baseline_oof_predictions\",\n",
    "               \"baseline_model_registry\", \"baseline_residuals\", \"baseline_quantile_performance\"]\n",
    "    if schools is not None:\n",
    "        gp = group_performance(pooled, schools, int(cfg[\"min_group_size\"]))\n",
    "        ctx.save_df(gp, \"baseline_school_performance\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "        outputs.append(\"baseline_school_performance\")\n",
    "    _baseline_figures(ctx, results_df, pooled, residual, qp)\n",
    "    best = results_df[results_df[\"scheme\"] == cfg[\"primary_cv_scheme\"]].sort_values(\"pooled_official\", ascending=False).head(3) \\\n",
    "        if \"pooled_official\" in results_df.columns else results_df.head(0)\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": outputs,\n",
    "            \"summary\": {\"primary_pooled_r2\": primary_res.summary.get(\"pooled_r2\"),\n",
    "                        \"primary_mean_fold_r2\": primary_res.summary.get(\"mean_fold_r2\"),\n",
    "                        \"scheme_status\": {k: v[\"status\"] for k, v in status.items()},\n",
    "                        \"best_models\": best[[\"model_id\", \"pooled_official\"]].to_dict(\"records\") if len(best) else []}}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _baseline_figures(ctx, results: pd.DataFrame, pooled: pd.DataFrame, residual: pd.Series, qp: pd.DataFrame) -> None:\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    r = results[results.get(\"status\", \"OK\") == \"OK\"] if \"status\" in results.columns else results\n",
    "    if \"pooled_r2\" in r.columns and len(r):\n",
    "        for scheme, g in r.groupby(\"scheme\"):\n",
    "            g = g.sort_values(\"pooled_r2\")\n",
    "            fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (7, 0.4 * len(g) + 2))\n",
    "            ax = axes[0, 0]\n",
    "            lo = (g[\"pooled_r2\"] - g[\"pooled_r2_ci_lower\"]).clip(lower=0).fillna(0)\n",
    "            hi = (g[\"pooled_r2_ci_upper\"] - g[\"pooled_r2\"]).clip(lower=0).fillna(0)\n",
    "            ax.errorbar(g[\"pooled_r2\"], g[\"model_id\"], xerr=[lo, hi], fmt=\"o\", capsize=3, label=\"pooled OOF R² (95% CI)\")\n",
    "            ax.scatter(g[\"mean_fold_r2\"], g[\"model_id\"], marker=\"x\", color=\"#C44E52\", label=\"mean fold R²\")\n",
    "            ax.legend(fontsize=7)\n",
    "            viz.finalize_axis(ax, f\"Screening-only baselines: {scheme}\", \"R²\", \"\", int(g[\"n_students\"].max()))\n",
    "            ctx.figure(fig, f\"baseline_comparison_{scheme}\", f\"Baseline comparison ({scheme})\",\n",
    "                       \"How much variation does conventional screening explain?\", \"baseline_results\",\n",
    "                       int(g[\"n_students\"].max()), f\"Best pooled R²={g['pooled_r2'].max():.3f}; pooled and mean-fold R² differ by design.\")\n",
    "    fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 3, (4.8, 4))\n",
    "    viz.scatter_fit(axes[0, 0], pooled[\"pred\"], pooled[\"y\"], \"OOF prediction\", \"observed outcome\", \"actual vs predicted\")\n",
    "    lim = [np.nanmin([pooled[\"pred\"].min(), pooled[\"y\"].min()]), np.nanmax([pooled[\"pred\"].max(), pooled[\"y\"].max()])]\n",
    "    axes[0, 0].plot(lim, lim, \"--\", color=\"grey\")\n",
    "    viz.hist_kde(axes[0, 1], residual, \"OOF residual\")\n",
    "    bins = pd.qcut(pooled[\"pred\"].rank(method=\"first\"), 10, labels=False)\n",
    "    cal = pooled.groupby(bins).agg(pred=(\"pred\", \"mean\"), y=(\"y\", \"mean\"), n=(\"y\", \"size\"))\n",
    "    axes[0, 2].plot(cal[\"pred\"], cal[\"y\"], \"o-\")\n",
    "    axes[0, 2].plot(lim, lim, \"--\", color=\"grey\")\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 2], \"Calibration (prediction deciles)\", \"mean prediction\", \"mean observed\", int(len(pooled)))\n",
    "    ctx.figure(fig, \"baseline_primary_diagnostics\", f\"Primary baseline {cfg['primary_baseline']} diagnostics\",\n",
    "               \"Is the screening baseline well calibrated?\", \"baseline_residuals\", int(len(pooled)),\n",
    "               f\"Residual SD={residual.std():.3g}; quantile RMSE range {qp['rmse'].min():.3g}-{qp['rmse'].max():.3g}.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-009",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/clustering.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 15 - student phenotype and clustering atlas.\n",
    "\n",
    "Scientific question: are there distinct multimodal student profiles that\n",
    "conventional screening does not describe adequately?\n",
    "\n",
    "Clusters are fitted in PCA space (never only in a 2-D visualisation\n",
    "embedding) and never use the target. Discovered clusters are characterised\n",
    "afterwards; no predefined educational or cognitive labels are imposed.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "from .families import columns_by_family, modeling_columns\n",
    "from .stats_utils import cramers_v, smd\n",
    "\n",
    "SPACES = {\n",
    "    \"C01_SCREENING\": [\"SCREENING\"],\n",
    "    \"C02_ITEM_BEHAVIOR\": [\"CORRECTNESS\", \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\", \"ADAPTIVE\"],\n",
    "    \"C03_TEMPORAL\": [\"TEMPORAL\"],\n",
    "    \"C04_SPECTRAL\": [\"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\"],\n",
    "    \"C05_WAVELETS\": [\"WAVELETS\"],\n",
    "    \"C06_PHONETIC\": [\"PHONETIC\"],\n",
    "    \"C07_PROSODY\": [\"PROSODY\"],\n",
    "    \"C08_MULTIMODAL\": [\"SCREENING\", \"CORRECTNESS\", \"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\", \"PHONETIC\"],\n",
    "    \"C09_SCREENING_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\": [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\"],\n",
    "    \"C10_TASK_SPECIFIC\": [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"CORRECTNESS\"],\n",
    "}\n",
    "AUDIO_CLUSTER_FAMILIES = [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\", \"PHONETIC\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def prepare_space(S: pd.DataFrame, space: str, fit_index=None, max_components: int = 20, seed: int = 0):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Median-impute, robust-scale, optionally residualise on screening, then PCA (fit on fit_index).\"\"\"\n",
    "    from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "\n",
    "    fams = SPACES[space]\n",
    "    cols = [c for c in S.columns if c in set(modeling_columns(S.columns, fams))\n",
    "            and pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(S[c]) and not c.startswith(\"meta_\")]\n",
    "    if space == \"C10_TASK_SPECIFIC\":\n",
    "        cols = [c for c in cols if \"__task=\" in c]\n",
    "    X = S[cols]\n",
    "    X = X.loc[:, X.notna().mean() >= 0.5]\n",
    "    fit_index = X.index if fit_index is None else fit_index\n",
    "    Xf = X.loc[fit_index]\n",
    "    med = Xf.median()\n",
    "    iqr = (Xf.quantile(0.75) - Xf.quantile(0.25)).replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "    keep = iqr.notna()\n",
    "    X = ((X.loc[:, keep] - med[keep]) / iqr[keep]).fillna(0.0).clip(-10, 10)\n",
    "    if X.shape[1] < 2:\n",
    "        return None, {\"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT_FEATURES\", \"n_features\": int(X.shape[1])}\n",
    "    if space == \"C09_SCREENING_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\":\n",
    "        theta = [c for c in da.raw_theta_columns(S)]\n",
    "        if theta:\n",
    "            T = S[theta].fillna(S.loc[fit_index, theta].median())\n",
    "            T1 = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(T)), T.reindex(X.index).to_numpy()])\n",
    "            mask = X.index.isin(fit_index)\n",
    "            beta, *_ = np.linalg.lstsq(T1[mask], X.to_numpy()[mask], rcond=None)\n",
    "            X = pd.DataFrame(X.to_numpy() - T1 @ beta, index=X.index, columns=X.columns)\n",
    "    n_comp = int(min(max_components, X.shape[1], len(fit_index) - 1))\n",
    "    pca = PCA(n_components=n_comp, random_state=seed).fit(X.loc[fit_index])\n",
    "    cum = np.cumsum(pca.explained_variance_ratio_)\n",
    "    k = int(min(n_comp, np.searchsorted(cum, 0.9) + 1))\n",
    "    Z = pd.DataFrame(pca.transform(X)[:, :k], index=X.index, columns=[f\"PC{i + 1}\" for i in range(k)])\n",
    "    return Z, {\"status\": \"OK\", \"n_features\": int(X.shape[1]), \"n_components\": k, \"explained\": float(cum[k - 1])}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _fit_method(method: str, Z: np.ndarray, k: int, seed: int, cfg: dict):\n",
    "    from sklearn.cluster import AgglomerativeClustering, KMeans, SpectralClustering\n",
    "    from sklearn.mixture import GaussianMixture\n",
    "\n",
    "    if method == \"kmeans\":\n",
    "        m = KMeans(k, random_state=seed, n_init=10).fit(Z)\n",
    "        return m.labels_, None\n",
    "    if method == \"gmm\":\n",
    "        m = GaussianMixture(k, random_state=seed, n_init=3, covariance_type=\"diag\").fit(Z)\n",
    "        post = m.predict_proba(Z)\n",
    "        return post.argmax(1), post\n",
    "    if method == \"hierarchical\":\n",
    "        return AgglomerativeClustering(n_clusters=k, linkage=\"ward\").fit_predict(Z), None\n",
    "    if method == \"spectral\":\n",
    "        return SpectralClustering(n_clusters=k, random_state=seed, affinity=\"nearest_neighbors\",\n",
    "                                  n_neighbors=min(15, len(Z) - 1)).fit_predict(Z), None\n",
    "    raise ValueError(method)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _hdbscan(Z: np.ndarray, cfg: dict):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        from sklearn.cluster import HDBSCAN\n",
    "\n",
    "        return HDBSCAN(min_cluster_size=int(cfg[\"hdbscan_min_cluster_size\"])).fit_predict(Z)\n",
    "    except ImportError:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            import hdbscan  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "            return hdbscan.HDBSCAN(min_cluster_size=int(cfg[\"hdbscan_min_cluster_size\"])).fit_predict(Z)\n",
    "        except ImportError:\n",
    "            return None\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def bootstrap_stability(Z: np.ndarray, labels: np.ndarray, method: str, k: int, n_boot: int, seed: int, cfg: dict) -> float:\n",
    "    from sklearn.metrics import adjusted_rand_score\n",
    "\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "    aris = []\n",
    "    n = len(Z)\n",
    "    for b in range(n_boot):\n",
    "        idx = np.sort(rng.choice(n, int(0.8 * n), replace=False))\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            lb, _ = _fit_method(method, Z[idx], k, seed + b + 1, cfg)\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        aris.append(adjusted_rand_score(labels[idx], lb))\n",
    "    return float(np.mean(aris)) if aris else np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def evaluate_space(Z: pd.DataFrame, cfg: dict, meta: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple[pd.DataFrame, dict]:\n",
    "    from sklearn.metrics import calinski_harabasz_score, davies_bouldin_score, silhouette_score\n",
    "\n",
    "    seed = int(cfg[\"seed\"])\n",
    "    lo, hi = cfg[\"cluster_k_range\"]\n",
    "    hi = int(min(hi, max(2, len(Z) // 20)))\n",
    "    methods = [\"kmeans\", \"gmm\", \"hierarchical\"] + ([\"spectral\"] if len(Z) <= int(cfg[\"spectral_clustering_max_n\"]) else [])\n",
    "    rows, labels_store = [], {}\n",
    "    A = Z.to_numpy()\n",
    "    for method in methods:\n",
    "        for k in range(int(lo), hi + 1):\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                lab, post = _fit_method(method, A, k, seed, cfg)\n",
    "            except Exception as exc:\n",
    "                rows.append({\"method\": method, \"k\": k, \"status\": f\"FAILED: {exc}\"})\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            if len(np.unique(lab)) < 2:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            sizes = np.bincount(lab)\n",
    "            row = {\"method\": method, \"k\": k, \"status\": \"OK\", \"silhouette\": float(silhouette_score(A, lab)),\n",
    "                   \"davies_bouldin\": float(davies_bouldin_score(A, lab)), \"calinski_harabasz\": float(calinski_harabasz_score(A, lab)),\n",
    "                   \"min_size\": int(sizes.min()), \"size_balance\": float(sizes.min() / sizes.max()),\n",
    "                   \"assignment_uncertainty\": float(1 - post.max(1).mean()) if post is not None else np.nan}\n",
    "            if method != \"spectral\":\n",
    "                row[\"bootstrap_ari\"] = bootstrap_stability(A, lab, method, k, int(cfg[\"cluster_bootstrap\"]), seed, cfg)\n",
    "            for col in (\"school_id\", \"instrument\"):\n",
    "                if col in meta.columns and meta[col].nunique() > 1:\n",
    "                    row[f\"cramers_v_{col}\"] = cramers_v(lab, meta.reindex(Z.index)[col].astype(str).to_numpy())\n",
    "            rows.append(row)\n",
    "            labels_store[(method, k)] = lab\n",
    "    hdb = _hdbscan(A, cfg)\n",
    "    if hdb is not None and len(set(hdb) - {-1}) >= 2:\n",
    "        mask = hdb >= 0\n",
    "        rows.append({\"method\": \"hdbscan\", \"k\": int(len(set(hdb) - {-1})), \"status\": \"OK\",\n",
    "                     \"silhouette\": float(silhouette_score(A[mask], hdb[mask])), \"noise_fraction\": float((~mask).mean())})\n",
    "        labels_store[(\"hdbscan\", int(len(set(hdb) - {-1})))] = hdb\n",
    "    ev = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    ok = ev[(ev.get(\"status\") == \"OK\") & (ev[\"method\"] != \"hdbscan\")] if len(ev) else ev\n",
    "    if len(ok):\n",
    "        stable = ok[(ok.get(\"bootstrap_ari\", pd.Series(1.0, index=ok.index)).fillna(0) >= 0.6) & (ok[\"min_size\"] >= int(cfg[\"min_group_size\"]))]\n",
    "        cand = stable if len(stable) else ok\n",
    "        best = cand.sort_values(\"silhouette\", ascending=False).iloc[0]\n",
    "        chosen = {\"method\": best[\"method\"], \"k\": int(best[\"k\"]), \"silhouette\": float(best[\"silhouette\"]),\n",
    "                  \"stable\": bool(len(stable) > 0), \"labels\": labels_store[(best[\"method\"], int(best[\"k\"]))]}\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        chosen = {\"method\": None}\n",
    "    return ev, chosen\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_student_phenotypes(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    from sklearn.metrics import adjusted_rand_score\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    S = da.student_features(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    meta = da.student_meta(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    res = da.residuals(ctx)\n",
    "    evals, assignments, profiles, space_info = [], {}, [], {}\n",
    "    for space in SPACES:\n",
    "        Z, info = prepare_space(S, space, max_components=int(cfg[\"cluster_max_pca_components\"]), seed=int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "        space_info[space] = info\n",
    "        if Z is None or len(Z) < 30:\n",
    "            space_info[space][\"status\"] = info.get(\"status\", \"INSUFFICIENT_STUDENTS\")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        ev, chosen = evaluate_space(Z, cfg, meta)\n",
    "        evals.append(ev.assign(space=space))\n",
    "        if chosen.get(\"method\") is None:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        lab = pd.Series(chosen[\"labels\"], index=Z.index, name=space)\n",
    "        assignments[space] = lab\n",
    "        space_info[space].update({k: v for k, v in chosen.items() if k != \"labels\"})\n",
    "        _characterise(ctx, S, meta, res, lab, space, Z, profiles)\n",
    "    if not assignments:\n",
    "        ctx.save_json(space_info, \"cluster_space_info\")\n",
    "        return {\"outputs\": [\"cluster_space_info\"], \"summary\": {\"status\": \"NO_CLUSTERABLE_SPACE\"}}\n",
    "    A = pd.DataFrame(assignments)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(A.reset_index(), \"cluster_assignments\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.concat(evals, ignore_index=True), \"cluster_evaluation\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.DataFrame(profiles), \"cluster_profiles\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    sens = pd.DataFrame(index=A.columns, columns=A.columns, dtype=float)\n",
    "    for a in A.columns:\n",
    "        for b in A.columns:\n",
    "            m = A[a].notna() & A[b].notna()\n",
    "            sens.loc[a, b] = adjusted_rand_score(A.loc[m, a], A.loc[m, b]) if m.sum() > 10 else np.nan\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(sens.reset_index().rename(columns={\"index\": \"space\"}), \"cluster_space_sensitivity\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_json(space_info, \"cluster_space_info\")\n",
    "    fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (7, 6))\n",
    "    viz.heatmap(axes[0, 0], sens, \"Feature-space sensitivity (ARI between chosen clusterings)\", cmap=\"viridis\", vmin=0, vmax=1, annotate=True)\n",
    "    ctx.figure(fig, \"cluster_space_sensitivity\", \"Cluster stability across feature spaces\",\n",
    "               \"Do different modalities produce the same phenotypes?\", \"cluster_space_sensitivity\", int(len(A)),\n",
    "               \"ARI near 0 means the spaces induce unrelated partitions.\")\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": [\"cluster_assignments\", \"cluster_evaluation\", \"cluster_profiles\", \"cluster_space_sensitivity\",\n",
    "                        \"cluster_space_info\"],\n",
    "            \"summary\": {s: {k: v for k, v in i.items() if k in (\"method\", \"k\", \"silhouette\", \"stable\", \"status\")}\n",
    "                        for s, i in space_info.items()}}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _characterise(ctx, S, meta, res, lab: pd.Series, space: str, Z: pd.DataFrame, profiles: list) -> None:\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    d = pd.DataFrame({\"cluster\": lab}).join(meta).join(S)\n",
    "    if res is not None:\n",
    "        d[\"residual\"] = res\n",
    "    feat_cols = [c for c in modeling_columns(S.columns, SPACES[space]) if c in d.columns][:2000]\n",
    "    for c, g in d.groupby(\"cluster\"):\n",
    "        rest = d[d[\"cluster\"] != c]\n",
    "        diffs = {f: smd(g[f], rest[f]) for f in feat_cols}\n",
    "        top = sorted(((f, v) for f, v in diffs.items() if np.isfinite(v)), key=lambda t: -abs(t[1]))[:10]\n",
    "        prof = {\"space\": space, \"cluster\": int(c), \"n\": int(len(g)), \"target_mean\": float(g[\"target\"].mean()),\n",
    "                \"target_sd\": float(g[\"target\"].std()), \"top_distinguishing_features\": \"; \".join(f\"{f}:{v:+.2f}\" for f, v in top)}\n",
    "        for col in (\"theta_mean\", \"acc_all\", \"q_snr_db_approx__mean\", \"residual\"):\n",
    "            if col in g.columns:\n",
    "                prof[f\"{col}_mean\"] = float(g[col].mean())\n",
    "        profiles.append(prof)\n",
    "    tag = space.lower()\n",
    "    fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 3, (5, 4.3))\n",
    "    ax = axes[0, 0]\n",
    "    ax.scatter(Z.iloc[:, 0], Z.iloc[:, 1] if Z.shape[1] > 1 else np.zeros(len(Z)), c=lab.reindex(Z.index), s=6, cmap=\"tab10\")\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(ax, f\"{space}: PCA map (clusters fitted in {Z.shape[1]}-D PCA)\", \"PC1\", \"PC2\", len(Z))\n",
    "    emb = None\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"umap_enabled\"):\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            import umap  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "            emb = umap.UMAP(random_state=int(cfg[\"seed\"])).fit_transform(Z.to_numpy())\n",
    "            title = \"UMAP (visualisation only)\"\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            emb = None\n",
    "    if emb is None and cfg.get(\"tsne_enabled\") and len(Z) >= 10:\n",
    "        from sklearn.manifold import TSNE\n",
    "\n",
    "        emb = TSNE(n_components=2, random_state=int(cfg[\"seed\"]), perplexity=min(30, max(5, len(Z) // 10))).fit_transform(Z.to_numpy())\n",
    "        title = \"t-SNE (visualisation only)\"\n",
    "    if emb is not None:\n",
    "        axes[0, 1].scatter(emb[:, 0], emb[:, 1], c=lab.reindex(Z.index), s=6, cmap=\"tab10\")\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 1], title, \"dim 1\", \"dim 2\", len(Z))\n",
    "    viz.grouped_box(axes[0, 2], d.assign(cluster=d[\"cluster\"].astype(str)), \"target\", \"cluster\", \"outcome\")\n",
    "    ctx.figure(fig, f\"{tag}_maps\", f\"{space}: phenotype maps and outcome by cluster\",\n",
    "               \"Do multimodal profiles differ in outcome?\", \"cluster_assignments\", int(len(lab)),\n",
    "               f\"{lab.nunique()} clusters; target used only for characterisation.\")\n",
    "    top_feats = []\n",
    "    for p in profiles:\n",
    "        if p[\"space\"] == space:\n",
    "            top_feats += [t.split(\":\")[0] for t in p[\"top_distinguishing_features\"].split(\"; \") if t]\n",
    "    top_feats = list(dict.fromkeys(top_feats))[:40]\n",
    "    if top_feats:\n",
    "        zf = d[top_feats].apply(lambda s: (s - s.mean()) / s.std() if s.std() > 0 else s * 0)\n",
    "        M = zf.groupby(d[\"cluster\"]).mean().T\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (max(5, M.shape[1] * 0.8 + 3), 0.22 * len(M) + 2))\n",
    "        viz.heatmap(axes[0, 0], M, f\"{space}: standardised cluster means of distinguishing features\", cbar_label=\"z\")\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, f\"{tag}_feature_heatmap\", f\"{space}: cluster feature profiles\", \"What characterises each cluster?\",\n",
    "                   \"cluster_profiles\", int(len(lab)), \"Features ranked by |SMD| versus all other students.\")\n",
    "        radar_cols = top_feats[:8]\n",
    "        if len(radar_cols) >= 3:\n",
    "            fig = viz._plt().figure(figsize=(6, 6))\n",
    "            ax = fig.add_subplot(111, polar=True)\n",
    "            viz.radar(ax, radar_cols, {f\"cluster {c}\": M.loc[radar_cols, c].tolist() for c in M.columns}, f\"{space}: radar profiles\")\n",
    "            ctx.figure(fig, f\"{tag}_radar\", f\"{space}: radar profiles\", \"How do clusters differ?\", \"cluster_profiles\",\n",
    "                       int(len(lab)), \"Standardised means.\")\n",
    "    if len(Z) >= 10:\n",
    "        from scipy.cluster.hierarchy import dendrogram, linkage\n",
    "\n",
    "        sub = Z.iloc[np.linspace(0, len(Z) - 1, min(len(Z), 400)).astype(int)]\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (9, 4))\n",
    "        dendrogram(linkage(sub.to_numpy(), \"ward\"), ax=axes[0, 0], no_labels=True, color_threshold=None)\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], f\"{space}: Ward dendrogram (subsample)\", \"students\", \"distance\", len(sub))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, f\"{tag}_dendrogram\", f\"{space}: dendrogram\", \"Is there hierarchical structure?\", \"cluster_assignments\",\n",
    "                   len(sub), \"Evenly spaced subsample of at most 400 students.\")\n",
    "    for col in (\"school_id\", \"instrument\"):\n",
    "        if col in d.columns and d[col].nunique() > 1:\n",
    "            comp = pd.crosstab(d[\"cluster\"], d[col], normalize=\"index\")\n",
    "            comp = comp.loc[:, comp.sum().sort_values(ascending=False).index[:15]]\n",
    "            fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1)\n",
    "            comp.plot(kind=\"bar\", stacked=True, ax=axes[0, 0], legend=False)\n",
    "            viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], f\"{space}: {col} composition per cluster\", \"cluster\", \"proportion\", int(len(d)))\n",
    "            ctx.figure(fig, f\"{tag}_{col}_composition\", f\"{space}: {col} composition\", f\"Are clusters confounded with {col}?\",\n",
    "                       \"cluster_assignments\", int(len(d)), f\"Cramer's V={cramers_v(d['cluster'], d[col].astype(str)):.3f}.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fold_cluster_features(base: pd.DataFrame, train_ids, cfg: dict, k: int = 4) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Fold-fitted cluster distances on the multimodal audio space (for predictive use).\"\"\"\n",
    "    from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "\n",
    "    S = base.copy()\n",
    "    Z, info = prepare_space(S, \"C09_SCREENING_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\", fit_index=pd.Index(train_ids),\n",
    "                            max_components=int(cfg[\"cluster_max_pca_components\"]), seed=int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "    if Z is None:\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame(index=base.index)\n",
    "    km = KMeans(k, random_state=int(cfg[\"seed\"]), n_init=10).fit(Z.loc[train_ids])\n",
    "    dist = km.transform(Z)\n",
    "    out = pd.DataFrame(dist, index=Z.index, columns=[f\"clu_dist_{i}\" for i in range(k)])\n",
    "    out[\"clu_min_dist\"] = dist.min(axis=1)\n",
    "    return out\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-010",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/config.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Central configuration, execution profiles and configuration hashing.\n",
    "\n",
    "Configuration precedence (lowest to highest):\n",
    "\n",
    "1. ``BASE_CONFIG`` (the notebook configuration cell defaults)\n",
    "2. ``EXTENDED_DEFAULTS`` (advanced parameters)\n",
    "3. optional YAML file (``configs/p01_config.yaml``)\n",
    "4. user overrides (the notebook ``CONFIG`` dict)\n",
    "5. execution-profile overrides, except keys listed in ``profile_exempt_keys``\n",
    "\n",
    "The ``RESUME`` profile reloads the semantic configuration of the last run and\n",
    "only switches on resumption, so cached artifacts remain valid.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import copy\n",
    "import hashlib\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from typing import Any, Mapping, MutableMapping\n",
    "\n",
    "BASE_CONFIG: dict = {\n",
    "    \"project_name\": \"WildSpeech\",\n",
    "    \"experiment_name\": \"P01_LITERACY_SIGNAL_DISCOVERY\",\n",
    "    \"drive_folder_id\": \"10hOoRyDO2VwZ9rgU1grTe0tb97_MQjnf\",\n",
    "    \"drive_folder_url\": (\n",
    "        \"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/\"\n",
    "        \"10hOoRyDO2VwZ9rgU1grTe0tb97_MQjnf\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"environment\": \"COLAB\",\n",
    "    \"cloud_storage_authorized\": False,\n",
    "    \"drive_root\": None,\n",
    "    \"data_root\": None,\n",
    "    \"local_root\": None,\n",
    "    \"output_root\": None,\n",
    "    \"run_mode\": \"FULL\",\n",
    "    \"seed\": 42,\n",
    "    \"use_gpu\": True,\n",
    "    \"n_jobs\": -1,\n",
    "    \"sample_rate\": 16000,\n",
    "    \"audio_batch_size\": 64,\n",
    "    \"debug_max_students\": 30,\n",
    "    \"debug_max_clips\": 300,\n",
    "    \"extract_train_audio\": True,\n",
    "    \"extract_test_audio\": False,\n",
    "    \"train_only_eda\": True,\n",
    "    \"allow_test_inference\": False,\n",
    "    \"allow_external_apis\": False,\n",
    "    \"enable_tabular_eda\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_item_analysis\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_irt\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_acoustic_features\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_vad\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_wavelets\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_prosody\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_phonetic_analysis\": False,\n",
    "    \"enable_asr\": False,\n",
    "    \"enable_embeddings\": False,\n",
    "    \"enable_student_clustering\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_residual_analysis\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_confound_analysis\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_feature_interactions\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_baseline_models\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_failure_analysis\": True,\n",
    "    \"enable_submission\": False,\n",
    "    \"cv_folds\": 5,\n",
    "    \"cv_repeats\": 3,\n",
    "    \"bootstrap_iterations\": 1000,\n",
    "    \"fdr_alpha\": 0.05,\n",
    "    \"resume\": True,\n",
    "    \"overwrite_cache\": False,\n",
    "    \"save_figures\": True,\n",
    "    \"save_tables\": True,\n",
    "    \"save_html_report\": True,\n",
    "    \"figure_dpi\": 160,\n",
    "    \"max_features_for_heatmap\": 60,\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "EXTENDED_DEFAULTS: dict = {\n",
    "    # --- environment / storage -------------------------------------------\n",
    "    \"mount_drive\": True,\n",
    "    \"drive_mount_point\": \"/content/drive\",\n",
    "    \"persist_root\": None,            # Colab: defaults to <MyDrive>/WildSpeech\n",
    "    \"data_search_roots\": None,       # explicit list of directories to search\n",
    "    \"data_search_max_depth\": 7,\n",
    "    \"required_files\": [\n",
    "        \"pandas_read_csv_kwargs.json\",\n",
    "        \"submission_format.csv\",\n",
    "        \"train_audio.tar\",\n",
    "        \"test_audio.tar\",\n",
    "        \"train_clip_metadata.csv\",\n",
    "        \"test_clip_metadata.csv\",\n",
    "        \"train_student_metadata.csv\",\n",
    "        \"test_student_metadata.csv\",\n",
    "        \"train_labels.csv\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"min_free_disk_gb\": 2.0,\n",
    "    \"disk_safety_factor\": 1.15,\n",
    "    \"install_optional_dependencies\": False,\n",
    "    # --- evaluation --------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    \"official_metric\": \"r2\",            # must be verified on the competition page\n",
    "    \"official_metric_verified\": False,\n",
    "    \"primary_baseline\": \"M01_RIDGE\",\n",
    "    \"primary_cv_scheme\": \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\",\n",
    "    \"target_bins_for_stratification\": 5,\n",
    "    \"max_schools_for_loso\": 60,\n",
    "    \"min_group_size\": 10,\n",
    "    \"inner_cv_folds\": 4,\n",
    "    # --- schema -------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    # {\"student\": {\"student_id\": \"colname\"}, \"clip\": {...}, \"labels\": {...}}\n",
    "    \"schema_overrides\": {},\n",
    "    # {\"raw task value\": \"blending\" | \"deletion\" | \"repetition\" | \"other\"}\n",
    "    \"task_family_overrides\": {},\n",
    "    # --- audio --------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    \"audio_inventory_decode\": True,\n",
    "    \"audio_inventory_hash\": True,\n",
    "    \"min_audio_duration_s\": 0.05,\n",
    "    \"max_audio_duration_s\": 180.0,\n",
    "    \"n_fft\": 512,\n",
    "    \"hop_length\": 160,\n",
    "    \"win_length\": 400,\n",
    "    \"n_mels\": 64,\n",
    "    \"n_mfcc\": 13,\n",
    "    \"clip_level_threshold\": 0.99,\n",
    "    \"vad_backend\": \"energy\",          # energy | webrtc | silero_local\n",
    "    \"vad_model_path\": None,           # local TorchScript Silero file (license verified by user)\n",
    "    \"vad_model_license_verified\": False,\n",
    "    \"vad_webrtc_aggressiveness\": 2,\n",
    "    \"vad_energy_offset_db\": 12.0,\n",
    "    \"vad_max_below_peak_db\": 40.0,\n",
    "    \"vad_min_dynamic_range_db\": 6.0,\n",
    "    \"vad_min_speech_s\": 0.08,\n",
    "    \"vad_min_silence_s\": 0.15,\n",
    "    \"short_pause_s\": 0.15,\n",
    "    \"long_pause_s\": 0.5,\n",
    "    \"spectral_robust_stats\": [\n",
    "        \"mean\", \"std\", \"median\", \"mad\", \"min\", \"max\", \"p05\", \"p10\", \"p25\",\n",
    "        \"p75\", \"p90\", \"p95\", \"iqr\", \"skewness\", \"kurtosis\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"spectral_min_frames\": 5,\n",
    "    \"enable_hpss\": False,\n",
    "    \"enable_chroma\": False,\n",
    "    \"wavelet_families_dwt\": [\"haar\", \"db4\", \"sym8\"],\n",
    "    \"wavelet_families_all\": [\n",
    "        \"haar\", \"db2\", \"db4\", \"db6\", \"db8\", \"sym4\", \"sym8\", \"coif3\",\n",
    "        \"morl\", \"mexh\", \"cmor1.5-1.0\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"wavelet_primary_family\": \"db4\",\n",
    "    \"wavelet_max_level\": 8,\n",
    "    \"wavelet_packet_family\": \"db4\",\n",
    "    \"wavelet_packet_level\": 4,\n",
    "    \"enable_cwt\": True,\n",
    "    \"cwt_wavelets\": [\"morl\"],\n",
    "    \"cwt_sr\": 4000,\n",
    "    \"cwt_n_scales\": 24,\n",
    "    \"cwt_max_seconds\": 4.0,\n",
    "    \"prosody_f0_method\": \"pyin\",      # pyin | yin\n",
    "    \"f0_min_hz\": 75.0,\n",
    "    \"f0_max_hz\": 600.0,\n",
    "    \"formant_max_frames\": 60,\n",
    "    \"extraction_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n",
    "    \"extraction_chunk_size\": 400,\n",
    "    \"atlas_enabled\": True,\n",
    "    \"atlas_examples_per_stratum\": 1,\n",
    "    \"atlas_max_examples\": 24,\n",
    "    # --- aggregation --------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    \"aggregation_core_features\": None,  # None -> curated default list\n",
    "    \"aggregation_global_stats\": [\"mean\", \"std\", \"median\"],\n",
    "    \"aggregation_core_stats\": [\n",
    "        \"mean\", \"median\", \"std\", \"mad\", \"min\", \"max\", \"p10\", \"p25\", \"p75\",\n",
    "        \"p90\", \"iqr\", \"cv\", \"count\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"aggregation_min_obs\": 3,\n",
    "    \"slope_shrinkage_k\": 5.0,\n",
    "    \"item_shrinkage_k\": 10.0,\n",
    "    \"quality_good_snr_db\": 15.0,\n",
    "    \"length_bins_s\": [0.0, 1.5, 3.0, 1e9],\n",
    "    \"activity_bins\": [0.0, 0.3, 0.6, 1.0001],\n",
    "    \"phonetic_confidence_bins\": [0.0, 0.5, 0.8, 1.0001],\n",
    "    # --- item / IRT ---------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    \"irt_models\": [\"rasch\", \"1pl\", \"2pl\"],\n",
    "    \"irt_min_obs_per_item\": 5,\n",
    "    \"irt_2pl_min_obs_per_item\": 50,\n",
    "    \"irt_prior_theta_sd\": 1.0,\n",
    "    \"irt_prior_b_sd\": 2.0,\n",
    "    \"irt_prior_loga_sd\": 0.5,\n",
    "    \"irt_max_iter\": 500,\n",
    "    \"item_redundancy_min_coexposure\": 30,\n",
    "    \"item_rare_threshold\": 10,\n",
    "    # --- discovery ----------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    \"residual_group_quantiles\": [0.2, 0.8],\n",
    "    \"matching_calipers\": [0.1, 0.2, 0.5],\n",
    "    \"permutation_iterations\": 1000,\n",
    "    \"permutation_top_k\": 50,\n",
    "    \"discovery_split_repeats\": 20,\n",
    "    \"discovery_top_k\": 50,\n",
    "    \"min_n_correlation\": 20,\n",
    "    \"cluster_k_range\": [2, 8],\n",
    "    \"cluster_bootstrap\": 50,\n",
    "    \"cluster_max_pca_components\": 20,\n",
    "    \"umap_enabled\": True,\n",
    "    \"tsne_enabled\": True,\n",
    "    \"hdbscan_min_cluster_size\": 10,\n",
    "    \"spectral_clustering_max_n\": 3000,\n",
    "    \"interaction_candidates\": [\n",
    "        [\"SCREENING\", \"TEMPORAL\"], [\"SCREENING\", \"SPECTRAL\"], [\"SCREENING\", \"PHONETIC\"],\n",
    "        [\"SCREENING\", \"FLUENCY\"], [\"DIFFICULTY\", \"DURATION\"], [\"DIFFICULTY\", \"PHONETIC_CONFIDENCE\"],\n",
    "        [\"DIFFICULTY\", \"SPECTRAL_ENTROPY\"], [\"CORRECTNESS\", \"ACOUSTIC_CONSISTENCY\"],\n",
    "        [\"TASK\", \"ACOUSTIC\"], [\"INSTRUMENT\", \"SCREENING\"], [\"TASK\", \"COMPLEXITY\"],\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"interaction_h_statistic_max_n\": 600,\n",
    "    \"index_min_components\": 2,\n",
    "    \"ablation_models\": [\"RIDGE\", \"ELASTIC_NET\", \"CATBOOST\", \"XGBOOST\", \"LIGHTGBM\", \"PLS\"],\n",
    "    \"ablation_primary_model\": \"RIDGE\",\n",
    "    \"ablation_max_features\": 300,\n",
    "    \"ablation_pairwise_families\": True,\n",
    "    \"ablation_forward_max_steps\": 6,\n",
    "    \"residual_fusion_alphas\": [0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0],\n",
    "    \"feature_registry_cv_top_k\": 100,\n",
    "    \"feature_registry_bootstrap_top_k\": 200,\n",
    "    \"redundancy_threshold\": 0.9,\n",
    "    \"sensitivity_artifact_corr\": 0.5,\n",
    "    \"sensitivity_item_icc\": 0.1,\n",
    "    \"sensitivity_correctness_r\": 0.1,\n",
    "    # --- linguistic / phonetic / foundation models --------------------------\n",
    "    \"enable_linguistic_features\": True,\n",
    "    \"g2p_backend\": \"auto\",            # auto | g2p_en | pronouncing | rules\n",
    "    \"asr_models\": [],                 # list of dicts, see phonetic_features.ASR_MODEL_SPEC\n",
    "    \"embedding_models\": [],           # list of dicts, see foundation_models.EMBEDDING_MODEL_SPEC\n",
    "    \"hf_local_files_only\": True,\n",
    "    \"embedding_max_seconds\": 30.0,\n",
    "    \"embedding_pca_components\": 32,\n",
    "    # --- submission ---------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    \"submission_model\": \"M01_RIDGE\",\n",
    "    \"submission_feature_set\": \"A01_THETA_ONLY\",\n",
    "    \"submission_filename\": \"WILDSPEECH_P01_SCREENING_BASELINE_submission.csv\",\n",
    "    # --- orchestration ------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    \"stage_selection\": None,\n",
    "    \"profile_exempt_keys\": [],\n",
    "    \"last_run_config_name\": \"last_run_config.json\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "PROFILES: dict = {\n",
    "    \"SMOKE\": {\n",
    "        \"debug_max_students\": 10,\n",
    "        \"debug_max_clips\": 60,\n",
    "        \"cv_repeats\": 1,\n",
    "        \"bootstrap_iterations\": 50,\n",
    "        \"permutation_iterations\": 50,\n",
    "        \"cluster_bootstrap\": 5,\n",
    "        \"discovery_split_repeats\": 3,\n",
    "        \"enable_prosody\": False,\n",
    "        \"enable_wavelets\": False,\n",
    "        \"enable_cwt\": False,\n",
    "        \"atlas_max_examples\": 2,\n",
    "        \"ablation_models\": [\"RIDGE\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"DEBUG\": {\n",
    "        \"cv_repeats\": 1,\n",
    "        \"bootstrap_iterations\": 100,\n",
    "        \"permutation_iterations\": 100,\n",
    "        \"cluster_bootstrap\": 10,\n",
    "        \"discovery_split_repeats\": 5,\n",
    "        \"wavelet_families_dwt\": [\"db4\"],\n",
    "        \"atlas_max_examples\": 6,\n",
    "        \"ablation_models\": [\"RIDGE\", \"CATBOOST\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"FAST\": {\n",
    "        \"enable_prosody\": False,\n",
    "        \"enable_cwt\": False,\n",
    "        \"enable_hpss\": False,\n",
    "        \"enable_chroma\": False,\n",
    "        \"wavelet_families_dwt\": [\"db4\"],\n",
    "        \"bootstrap_iterations\": 300,\n",
    "        \"permutation_iterations\": 300,\n",
    "        \"cluster_bootstrap\": 20,\n",
    "        \"ablation_models\": [\"RIDGE\", \"CATBOOST\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"FULL\": {},\n",
    "    \"RESEARCH\": {\n",
    "        \"enable_phonetic_analysis\": True,\n",
    "        \"enable_hpss\": True,\n",
    "        \"enable_chroma\": True,\n",
    "        \"enable_cwt\": True,\n",
    "        \"cwt_wavelets\": [\"morl\", \"mexh\", \"cmor1.5-1.0\"],\n",
    "        \"wavelet_families_dwt\": [\"haar\", \"db2\", \"db4\", \"db6\", \"db8\", \"sym4\", \"sym8\", \"coif3\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"RESUME\": {\"resume\": True, \"overwrite_cache\": False},\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "PROFILE_DEFAULT_STAGES: dict = {\n",
    "    \"SMOKE\": [\"00\", \"01\", \"02\", \"03\", \"06\"],\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "VALID_ENVIRONMENTS = {\"COLAB\", \"LOCAL_WINDOWS\", \"LOCAL_LINUX\", \"PRIVATE_CLOUD\"}\n",
    "VALID_RUN_MODES = set(PROFILES)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keys that never change scientific results and are excluded from config hashes.\n",
    "NON_SEMANTIC_KEYS = {\n",
    "    \"resume\", \"overwrite_cache\", \"n_jobs\", \"save_figures\", \"save_tables\",\n",
    "    \"save_html_report\", \"figure_dpi\", \"use_gpu\", \"audio_batch_size\",\n",
    "    \"stage_selection\", \"max_features_for_heatmap\", \"install_optional_dependencies\",\n",
    "    \"profile_exempt_keys\", \"last_run_config_name\", \"mount_drive\",\n",
    "    \"drive_mount_point\", \"data_search_roots\", \"data_search_max_depth\",\n",
    "    \"drive_root\", \"local_root\", \"output_root\", \"persist_root\",\n",
    "    \"cloud_storage_authorized\", \"environment\", \"drive_folder_url\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class ConfigError(ValueError):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Raised for invalid or unsafe configuration values.\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _load_yaml(path: Path) -> dict:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import yaml  # type: ignore\n",
    "    except ImportError as exc:  # pragma: no cover - depends on env\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"PyYAML is required to read YAML configuration files\") from exc\n",
    "    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n",
    "        data = yaml.safe_load(fh) or {}\n",
    "    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(f\"YAML config {path} must contain a mapping\")\n",
    "    return data\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_config(\n",
    "    user_config: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None,\n",
    "    profile: str | None = None,\n",
    "    yaml_path: str | Path | None = None,\n",
    "    last_run_path: str | Path | None = None,\n",
    ") -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Assemble the effective configuration for a run.\"\"\"\n",
    "    cfg: dict = copy.deepcopy(BASE_CONFIG)\n",
    "    cfg.update(copy.deepcopy(EXTENDED_DEFAULTS))\n",
    "    if yaml_path is not None and Path(yaml_path).exists():\n",
    "        cfg.update(_load_yaml(Path(yaml_path)))\n",
    "    if user_config:\n",
    "        cfg.update(copy.deepcopy(dict(user_config)))\n",
    "    profile = (profile or cfg.get(\"run_mode\") or \"FULL\").upper()\n",
    "    if profile not in PROFILES:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(f\"Unknown profile {profile!r}; expected one of {sorted(PROFILES)}\")\n",
    "    if profile == \"RESUME\":\n",
    "        if last_run_path is None or not Path(last_run_path).exists():\n",
    "            raise ConfigError(\n",
    "                \"RESUME profile requires the configuration of a previous run \"\n",
    "                f\"(looked for {last_run_path}). Run another profile first.\"\n",
    "            )\n",
    "        with open(last_run_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n",
    "            previous = json.load(fh)\n",
    "        keep = {k: cfg[k] for k in NON_SEMANTIC_KEYS if k in cfg}\n",
    "        cfg.update(previous)\n",
    "        cfg.update(keep)\n",
    "        cfg[\"resume\"] = True\n",
    "        cfg[\"overwrite_cache\"] = False\n",
    "        cfg[\"resumed_profile\"] = previous.get(\"run_mode\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        exempt = set(cfg.get(\"profile_exempt_keys\") or [])\n",
    "        for key, value in PROFILES[profile].items():\n",
    "            if key not in exempt:\n",
    "                cfg[key] = copy.deepcopy(value)\n",
    "        cfg[\"run_mode\"] = profile\n",
    "    validate_config(cfg)\n",
    "    return cfg\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def validate_config(cfg: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Validate configuration types and safety constraints.\"\"\"\n",
    "    env = str(cfg.get(\"environment\", \"\")).upper()\n",
    "    if env not in VALID_ENVIRONMENTS:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(f\"environment must be one of {sorted(VALID_ENVIRONMENTS)}, got {env!r}\")\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"run_mode\") not in VALID_RUN_MODES:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(f\"run_mode must be one of {sorted(VALID_RUN_MODES)}\")\n",
    "    if bool(cfg.get(\"allow_external_apis\")):\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\n",
    "            \"allow_external_apis=True is not supported: P01 never transmits competition \"\n",
    "            \"data to external APIs, LLM providers or remote speech services.\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    if int(cfg.get(\"cv_folds\", 0)) < 2:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"cv_folds must be >= 2\")\n",
    "    if int(cfg.get(\"cv_repeats\", 0)) < 1:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"cv_repeats must be >= 1\")\n",
    "    if not 0.0 < float(cfg.get(\"fdr_alpha\", 0.05)) < 1.0:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"fdr_alpha must be in (0, 1)\")\n",
    "    if int(cfg.get(\"bootstrap_iterations\", 0)) < 10:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"bootstrap_iterations must be >= 10\")\n",
    "    if int(cfg.get(\"sample_rate\", 0)) not in {8000, 16000, 22050, 24000, 32000, 44100, 48000}:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"sample_rate must be a standard audio rate\")\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"hop_length\", 1) <= 0 or cfg.get(\"n_fft\", 1) <= 0:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"n_fft and hop_length must be positive\")\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"win_length\", 0) > cfg.get(\"n_fft\", 0):\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"win_length must be <= n_fft\")\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"vad_backend\") not in {\"energy\", \"webrtc\", \"silero_local\"}:\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"vad_backend must be energy, webrtc or silero_local\")\n",
    "    if cfg.get(\"enable_submission\") and not cfg.get(\"allow_test_inference\"):\n",
    "        raise ConfigError(\"enable_submission=True requires allow_test_inference=True\")\n",
    "    for spec in cfg.get(\"asr_models\") or []:\n",
    "        if not isinstance(spec, dict) or \"checkpoint\" not in spec:\n",
    "            raise ConfigError(\"each asr_models entry must be a dict with a 'checkpoint'\")\n",
    "    for spec in cfg.get(\"embedding_models\") or []:\n",
    "        if not isinstance(spec, dict) or \"checkpoint\" not in spec:\n",
    "            raise ConfigError(\"each embedding_models entry must be a dict with a 'checkpoint'\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def semantic_config(cfg: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict:\n",
    "    return {k: v for k, v in cfg.items() if k not in NON_SEMANTIC_KEYS}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stable_hash(obj: Any, length: int = 16) -> str:\n",
    "    payload = json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n",
    "    return hashlib.sha256(payload.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()[:length]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def config_hash(cfg: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Hash of all scientifically relevant configuration values.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return stable_hash(semantic_config(cfg))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def subset_hash(cfg: Mapping[str, Any], keys: list[str] | tuple[str, ...]) -> str:\n",
    "    return stable_hash({k: cfg.get(k) for k in keys})\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "EXTRACTION_KEYS = (\n",
    "    \"sample_rate\", \"n_fft\", \"hop_length\", \"win_length\", \"n_mels\", \"n_mfcc\",\n",
    "    \"clip_level_threshold\", \"enable_vad\", \"vad_backend\", \"vad_model_path\",\n",
    "    \"vad_webrtc_aggressiveness\", \"vad_energy_offset_db\", \"vad_max_below_peak_db\",\n",
    "    \"vad_min_dynamic_range_db\", \"vad_min_speech_s\", \"vad_min_silence_s\",\n",
    "    \"short_pause_s\", \"long_pause_s\", \"spectral_robust_stats\", \"spectral_min_frames\",\n",
    "    \"enable_hpss\", \"enable_chroma\", \"enable_wavelets\", \"wavelet_families_dwt\",\n",
    "    \"wavelet_primary_family\", \"wavelet_max_level\", \"wavelet_packet_family\",\n",
    "    \"wavelet_packet_level\", \"enable_cwt\", \"cwt_wavelets\", \"cwt_sr\", \"cwt_n_scales\",\n",
    "    \"cwt_max_seconds\", \"enable_prosody\", \"prosody_f0_method\", \"f0_min_hz\",\n",
    "    \"f0_max_hz\", \"formant_max_frames\", \"extraction_version\", \"min_audio_duration_s\",\n",
    "    \"max_audio_duration_s\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def extraction_config(cfg: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Small, picklable configuration subset for worker processes.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return {k: copy.deepcopy(cfg.get(k)) for k in EXTRACTION_KEYS}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def save_config(cfg: Mapping[str, Any], directory: Path, name: str = \"p01_effective_config.json\") -> Path:\n",
    "    directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    from .io_utils import atomic_write_json\n",
    "\n",
    "    path = directory / name\n",
    "    atomic_write_json(path, dict(cfg))\n",
    "    last = directory / str(cfg.get(\"last_run_config_name\", \"last_run_config.json\"))\n",
    "    atomic_write_json(last, semantic_config(cfg))\n",
    "    return path\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def update_in_place(cfg: MutableMapping[str, Any], **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n",
    "    cfg.update(kwargs)\n",
    "    validate_config(cfg)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-011",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/confound_analysis.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 17 - confounding, artifact detection and robustness.\n",
    "\n",
    "Scientific question: are discovered acoustic signals genuine speech-related\n",
    "predictive information or technical shortcuts?\n",
    "\n",
    "Negative controls preserve grouping structure: student-level shuffles are\n",
    "performed within school, clip-level shuffles within item. Speech-active\n",
    "frames are never assumed to contain only the child; the multi-speaker\n",
    "indicator below is a crude proxy, not speaker identification.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "from .ablation import ColumnSetBuilder, cv_evaluate\n",
    "from .families import columns_by_family, feature_family, modeling_columns\n",
    "from .stats_utils import permute_within_groups, safe_corr\n",
    "from .validation import available_schemes, group_performance, paired_bootstrap_delta, pooled_predictions\n",
    "\n",
    "SPEECH_FAMILIES = [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _cols(S: pd.DataFrame, families) -> list:\n",
    "    return [c for c in modeling_columns(S.columns, families) if pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(S[c])]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def shuffled_within_groups(S: pd.DataFrame, cols: list, groups: pd.Series | None, seed: int) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "    perm = permute_within_groups(len(S), groups.reindex(S.index).fillna(\"NA\").to_numpy() if groups is not None else None, rng)\n",
    "    out = S.copy()\n",
    "    out[cols] = S[cols].to_numpy()[perm]\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def shuffled_within_item_aggregates(ctx, seed: int) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    from .student_aggregation import core_features, numeric_clip_features\n",
    "\n",
    "    clips = da.clip_table(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    feats = core_features(numeric_clip_features(clips), ctx.config)\n",
    "    feats = [f for f in feats if f.startswith((\"t_\", \"s_\", \"m_\", \"w_\", \"p_\"))]\n",
    "    if not feats or \"item_key\" not in clips.columns:\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "    shuffled = clips[[\"student_id\", \"item_key\"] + feats].copy()\n",
    "    for item, idx in shuffled.groupby(\"item_key\").groups.items():\n",
    "        idx = np.asarray(idx)\n",
    "        shuffled.loc[idx, feats] = shuffled.loc[rng.permutation(idx), feats].to_numpy()\n",
    "    out = shuffled.groupby(\"student_id\")[feats].agg([\"mean\", \"std\"])\n",
    "    out.columns = [f\"{a}__{b}\" for a, b in out.columns]\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def school_separability(S: pd.DataFrame, families: dict, schools: pd.Series, cfg: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "    from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "    from sklearn.metrics import balanced_accuracy_score\n",
    "    from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold, cross_val_predict\n",
    "    from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n",
    "    from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "    sch = schools.reindex(S.index)\n",
    "    counts = sch.value_counts()\n",
    "    keep = counts[counts >= int(cfg[\"min_group_size\"])].index\n",
    "    mask = sch.isin(keep)\n",
    "    if len(keep) < 2:\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame([{\"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT_SCHOOLS\"}])\n",
    "    yv = sch[mask].astype(str).to_numpy()\n",
    "    cv = StratifiedKFold(min(5, int(counts[keep].min())), shuffle=True, random_state=int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for fam, cols in families.items():\n",
    "        if not cols:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        X = S.loc[mask, cols[:400]]\n",
    "        model = make_pipeline(SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\"), StandardScaler(), LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, C=0.1))\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            pred = cross_val_predict(model, X, yv, cv=cv)\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:\n",
    "            rows.append({\"family\": fam, \"status\": f\"FAILED: {exc}\"})\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        rows.append({\"family\": fam, \"status\": \"OK\", \"n_students\": int(mask.sum()), \"n_schools\": int(len(keep)),\n",
    "                     \"balanced_accuracy\": float(balanced_accuracy_score(yv, pred)), \"chance\": 1.0 / len(keep),\n",
    "                     \"n_features\": len(cols[:400])})\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def confound_matrix(S: pd.DataFrame, meta: pd.DataFrame, families: dict, cfg: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    confounders = {}\n",
    "    for c in (\"q_snr_db_approx__mean\", \"q_duration_s__mean\", \"meta_n_clips\", \"meta_orig_sr_mode\", \"q_noise_floor_db__mean\",\n",
    "              \"q_eff_bandwidth_hz__mean\", \"meta_frac_quality_flagged\"):\n",
    "        if c in S.columns:\n",
    "            confounders[c] = S[c]\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for fam, cols in families.items():\n",
    "        sub = cols[:300]\n",
    "        row = {\"family\": fam, \"n_features\": len(cols)}\n",
    "        for name, conf in confounders.items():\n",
    "            rs = [abs(safe_corr(S[c], conf, \"spearman\", 20)[0]) for c in sub if c != name]\n",
    "            row[name] = float(np.nanmedian(rs)) if rs and np.isfinite(rs).any() else np.nan\n",
    "        for cat in (\"school_id\", \"instrument\"):\n",
    "            if cat in meta.columns and meta[cat].nunique() > 1:\n",
    "                g = meta[cat].reindex(S.index)\n",
    "                etas = []\n",
    "                for c in sub:\n",
    "                    x = S[c]\n",
    "                    m = x.notna() & g.notna()\n",
    "                    if m.sum() < 20:\n",
    "                        continue\n",
    "                    grand = x[m].mean()\n",
    "                    ss_t = ((x[m] - grand) ** 2).sum()\n",
    "                    ss_b = x[m].groupby(g[m]).apply(lambda v: len(v) * (v.mean() - grand) ** 2).sum()\n",
    "                    etas.append(np.sqrt(ss_b / ss_t) if ss_t > 0 else np.nan)\n",
    "                row[f\"eta_{cat}\"] = float(np.nanmedian(etas)) if etas else np.nan\n",
    "        rows.append(row)\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def sign_consistency(S: pd.DataFrame, residual: pd.Series, feats: list, assign: pd.DataFrame, meta: pd.DataFrame, cfg: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    from .validation import iter_folds\n",
    "\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    sch = meta[\"school_id\"].reindex(S.index)\n",
    "    for f in feats:\n",
    "        overall = safe_corr(S[f], residual, \"spearman\", 20)[0]\n",
    "        signs = []\n",
    "        for _, _, tr, _ in iter_folds(assign, \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\", repeats=[0]):\n",
    "            tr = [t for t in tr if t in S.index]\n",
    "            r = safe_corr(S.loc[tr, f], residual.reindex(tr), \"spearman\", 20)[0]\n",
    "            if np.isfinite(r) and np.isfinite(overall):\n",
    "                signs.append(np.sign(r) == np.sign(overall))\n",
    "        school_rs = {}\n",
    "        for s, idx in sch.dropna().groupby(sch.dropna()).groups.items():\n",
    "            if len(idx) >= int(cfg[\"min_group_size\"]):\n",
    "                school_rs[s] = safe_corr(S.loc[idx, f], residual.reindex(idx), \"spearman\", int(cfg[\"min_group_size\"]))[0]\n",
    "        vals = np.array([v for v in school_rs.values() if np.isfinite(v)])\n",
    "        rows.append({\"feature\": f, \"residual_rho\": overall, \"fold_sign_consistency\": float(np.mean(signs)) if signs else np.nan,\n",
    "                     \"school_sign_consistency\": float(np.mean(np.sign(vals) == np.sign(overall))) if len(vals) and np.isfinite(overall) else np.nan,\n",
    "                     \"n_schools\": len(vals), \"school_rho_sd\": float(vals.std(ddof=1)) if len(vals) > 1 else np.nan,\n",
    "                     **{f\"school_{k}\": v for k, v in school_rs.items()}})\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_confound_analysis(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    from .fold_features import FoldFeatureBuilder\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    S = da.student_features(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    meta = da.student_meta(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    y = meta[\"target\"].dropna().astype(float)\n",
    "    S = S.reindex(y.index)\n",
    "    assign = ctx.load_df(\"cv_assignments\")\n",
    "    residual = da.residuals(ctx).reindex(y.index)\n",
    "    schools = meta[\"school_id\"] if meta[\"school_id\"].notna().any() else None\n",
    "    scheme = \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\"\n",
    "    builder = FoldFeatureBuilder(ctx)\n",
    "    builder.base = builder.base.reindex(y.index)\n",
    "    screening_cols = builder.columns_for({\"SCREENING\"})\n",
    "    duration_cols = [c for c in S.columns if c.startswith((\"q_duration_s__\", \"t_total_dur__\", \"t_active_dur__\"))]\n",
    "    speech_cols = _cols(S, SPEECH_FAMILIES)\n",
    "    controls = {\n",
    "        \"NC01_BACKGROUND_ONLY\": _cols(S, [\"BACKGROUND\"]),\n",
    "        \"NC02_RECORDING_METADATA_ONLY\": _cols(S, [\"RECORDING_METADATA\"]),\n",
    "        \"NC03_AUDIO_QUALITY_ONLY\": _cols(S, [\"QUALITY\"]),\n",
    "        \"NC04_DURATION_ONLY\": duration_cols,\n",
    "        \"NC07_TECHNICAL_FEATURES_ONLY\": _cols(S, [\"QUALITY\", \"BACKGROUND\", \"RECORDING_METADATA\"]),\n",
    "        \"SPEECH_FEATURES_REFERENCE\": speech_cols,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    rows, oofs = [], {}\n",
    "    ref = cv_evaluate(ColumnSetBuilder(builder.base, screening_cols), None, y, assign, scheme, cfg, repeats=[0], groups=schools)\n",
    "    oofs[\"SCREENING_REFERENCE\"] = pooled_predictions(ref.oof)\n",
    "    rows.append({\"control\": \"SCREENING_REFERENCE\", \"variant\": \"screening\", \"n_features\": len(screening_cols), **ref.summary})\n",
    "\n",
    "    def run(name, base, cols):\n",
    "        if not cols:\n",
    "            rows.append({\"control\": name, \"status\": \"UNAVAILABLE\"})\n",
    "            return\n",
    "        for variant, cset in ((\"alone\", cols), (\"with_screening\", screening_cols + cols)):\n",
    "            bd = ColumnSetBuilder(base.reindex(y.index), cset)\n",
    "            res = cv_evaluate(bd, None, y, assign, scheme, cfg, repeats=[0], groups=schools)\n",
    "            p = pooled_predictions(res.oof)\n",
    "            oofs[f\"{name}|{variant}\"] = p\n",
    "            row = {\"control\": name, \"variant\": variant, \"n_features\": len(cset), **res.summary}\n",
    "            if variant == \"with_screening\":\n",
    "                d = paired_bootstrap_delta(p[\"y\"], p[\"pred\"], oofs[\"SCREENING_REFERENCE\"].reindex(p.index)[\"pred\"], cfg, \"r2\")\n",
    "                row.update({\"delta_r2_vs_screening\": d[\"delta\"], \"delta_ci_lower\": d[\"ci_lower\"], \"delta_ci_upper\": d[\"ci_upper\"]})\n",
    "            rows.append(row)\n",
    "\n",
    "    base_full = builder.base.join(S[[c for c in S.columns if c not in builder.base.columns]])\n",
    "    for name, cols in controls.items():\n",
    "        run(name, base_full, cols)\n",
    "    run(\"NC05_SHUFFLED_STUDENT_AUDIO\", shuffled_within_groups(base_full, speech_cols, schools, int(cfg[\"seed\"])), speech_cols)\n",
    "    nc06 = shuffled_within_item_aggregates(ctx, int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "    if not nc06.empty:\n",
    "        nc06_base = base_full[screening_cols].join(nc06.add_prefix(\"nc06_\"))\n",
    "        nc06_cols = [c for c in nc06_base.columns if c.startswith(\"nc06_\")]\n",
    "        run(\"NC06_SHUFFLED_AUDIO_WITHIN_ITEM\", nc06_base, nc06_cols)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        rows.append({\"control\": \"NC06_SHUFFLED_AUDIO_WITHIN_ITEM\", \"status\": \"UNAVAILABLE\"})\n",
    "    regions = {\n",
    "        \"full_recording_features\": [c for c in speech_cols if c.startswith((\"s_full_\", \"m_full_\"))],\n",
    "        \"speech_active_features\": [c for c in speech_cols if c.startswith((\"s_sp_\", \"m_sp_\"))],\n",
    "        \"background_region_features\": _cols(S, [\"BACKGROUND\"]),\n",
    "        \"content_conditioned_features\": [c for c in speech_cols if \"__task=\" in c or \"__corr=\" in c or \"__cplx=\" in c],\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    for name, cols in regions.items():\n",
    "        run(f\"REGION_{name}\", base_full, cols)\n",
    "    ia = cv_evaluate(builder, [\"SCREENING\", \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\"], y, assign, scheme, cfg, repeats=[0], groups=schools)\n",
    "    rows.append({\"control\": \"REGION_item_adjusted_features\", \"variant\": \"with_screening\", **ia.summary})\n",
    "    nc = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(nc, \"negative_controls\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    fams = {f: c for f, c in columns_by_family([c for c in S.columns if pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(S[c])]).items()\n",
    "            if f not in {\"OTHER\"}}\n",
    "    sep = school_separability(S, fams, schools, cfg) if schools is not None else pd.DataFrame([{\"status\": \"NO_SCHOOL_INFO\"}])\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(sep, \"school_separability\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    cmat = confound_matrix(S, meta, fams, cfg)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(cmat, \"confound_matrix\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    rank = pd.Series({c: abs(safe_corr(S[c], residual, \"spearman\", 20)[0]) for c in speech_cols}).dropna().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    sc = sign_consistency(S, residual, rank.index[:50].tolist(), assign, meta, cfg)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(sc, \"sign_consistency\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    multi = {}\n",
    "    for c in (\"p_f0_jump_frac__mean\", \"t_n_segments__mean\", \"t_active_ratio__mean\"):\n",
    "        if c in S.columns:\n",
    "            multi[c] = {\"target_rho\": safe_corr(S[c], y, \"spearman\", 20)[0], \"residual_rho\": safe_corr(S[c], residual, \"spearman\", 20)[0]}\n",
    "    sr = {}\n",
    "    if \"meta_orig_sr_mode\" in S.columns and S[\"meta_orig_sr_mode\"].nunique() > 1:\n",
    "        sr = S.groupby(\"meta_orig_sr_mode\").apply(lambda g: pd.Series({\"n\": len(g), \"target_mean\": y.reindex(g.index).mean(),\n",
    "                                                                       \"residual_mean\": residual.reindex(g.index).mean()})).reset_index().to_dict(\"records\")\n",
    "    miss = {c: safe_corr(S[c], residual, \"spearman\", 20)[0] for c in S.columns if c.startswith(\"meta_missing_\") and S[c].nunique() > 1}\n",
    "    ctx.save_json({\"multi_speaker_proxy\": multi, \"sampling_rate_groups\": sr, \"missingness_residual_rho\": miss,\n",
    "                   \"caveat\": \"Proxies only: child-only analysis requires a validated speaker-role identification method.\"},\n",
    "                  \"confound_diagnostics\")\n",
    "    subgroup = []\n",
    "    multi_res = cv_evaluate(builder, [\"SCREENING\"] + SPEECH_FAMILIES, y, assign, scheme, cfg, repeats=[0], groups=schools)\n",
    "    pm = pooled_predictions(multi_res.oof)\n",
    "    for col in (\"school_id\", \"instrument\"):\n",
    "        if col in meta.columns and meta[col].notna().any():\n",
    "            for label, p in ((\"screening\", oofs[\"SCREENING_REFERENCE\"]), (\"screening_plus_speech\", pm)):\n",
    "                gp = group_performance(p, meta[col], int(cfg[\"min_group_size\"]))\n",
    "                subgroup.append(gp.assign(by=col, model=label))\n",
    "    if subgroup:\n",
    "        ctx.save_df(pd.concat(subgroup, ignore_index=True), \"subgroup_performance\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    gap_rows = []\n",
    "    if \"CV_B_SCHOOL_GROUP_KFOLD\" in available_schemes(assign):\n",
    "        for label, fams_ in ((\"screening\", [\"SCREENING\"]), (\"screening_plus_speech\", [\"SCREENING\"] + SPEECH_FAMILIES)):\n",
    "            a = cv_evaluate(builder, fams_, y, assign, scheme, cfg, repeats=[0]).summary.get(\"pooled_r2\")\n",
    "            b = cv_evaluate(builder, fams_, y, assign, \"CV_B_SCHOOL_GROUP_KFOLD\", cfg).summary.get(\"pooled_r2\")\n",
    "            gap_rows.append({\"model\": label, \"r2_student_cv\": a, \"r2_school_grouped_cv\": b, \"generalization_gap\": a - b if a is not None and b is not None else np.nan})\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.DataFrame(gap_rows), \"domain_generalization_gap\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    _confound_figures(ctx, nc, sep, cmat, sc, meta, S, y)\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": [\"negative_controls\", \"school_separability\", \"confound_matrix\", \"sign_consistency\",\n",
    "                        \"confound_diagnostics\", \"domain_generalization_gap\"] + ([\"subgroup_performance\"] if subgroup else []),\n",
    "            \"summary\": {\"negative_controls\": nc[[\"control\", \"variant\", \"pooled_r2\"]].dropna().to_dict(\"records\") if \"pooled_r2\" in nc else []}}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _confound_figures(ctx, nc, sep, cmat, sc, meta, S, y) -> None:\n",
    "    if \"pooled_r2\" in nc.columns:\n",
    "        d = nc.dropna(subset=[\"pooled_r2\"]).copy()\n",
    "        d[\"label\"] = d[\"control\"] + \" | \" + d[\"variant\"].fillna(\"\")\n",
    "        d = d.sort_values(\"pooled_r2\")\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (8, 0.3 * len(d) + 2))\n",
    "        axes[0, 0].barh(d[\"label\"], d[\"pooled_r2\"])\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], \"Negative controls vs reference models (pooled OOF R²)\", \"R²\", \"\", int(len(y)))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"negative_controls\", \"Negative-control comparison\", \"Do technical features predict literacy as well as speech features?\",\n",
    "                   \"negative_controls\", int(len(y)), \"Shuffles preserve school (NC05) and item (NC06) grouping.\")\n",
    "    if \"balanced_accuracy\" in sep.columns:\n",
    "        s = sep.dropna(subset=[\"balanced_accuracy\"]).sort_values(\"balanced_accuracy\")\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (7, 0.3 * len(s) + 2))\n",
    "        axes[0, 0].barh(s[\"family\"], s[\"balanced_accuracy\"])\n",
    "        axes[0, 0].axvline(s[\"chance\"].iloc[0], color=\"red\", ls=\"--\", label=\"chance\")\n",
    "        axes[0, 0].legend(fontsize=7)\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], \"School separability by feature family\", \"balanced accuracy (CV)\", \"\", int(s[\"n_students\"].max()))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"school_separability\", \"School-prediction diagnostic\", \"Do features encode recording environment?\",\n",
    "                   \"school_separability\", int(s[\"n_students\"].max()), \"Logistic regression; well above chance suggests environment encoding.\")\n",
    "    if len(cmat) and cmat.shape[1] > 2:\n",
    "        M = cmat.set_index(\"family\").drop(columns=[\"n_features\"]).astype(float)\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (8, 0.35 * len(M) + 2))\n",
    "        viz.heatmap(axes[0, 0], M, \"Feature-family confounding (median |rho| or eta)\", cmap=\"viridis\", vmin=0, vmax=1, annotate=True)\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"confound_matrix\", \"Feature-family confounding matrix\", \"Which families track technical confounders?\",\n",
    "                   \"confound_matrix\", int(len(S)), \"Median association between family features and each potential confounder.\")\n",
    "    school_cols = [c for c in sc.columns if c.startswith(\"school_\") and c not in (\"school_sign_consistency\", \"school_rho_sd\")]\n",
    "    if school_cols:\n",
    "        M = sc.set_index(\"feature\")[school_cols].head(30)\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (max(6, len(school_cols) * 0.3 + 3), 0.25 * len(M) + 2))\n",
    "        viz.heatmap(axes[0, 0], M, \"Per-school residual correlation of top speech features\", vmin=-1, vmax=1, cbar_label=\"rho\")\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"school_stability_heatmap\", \"School-level feature stability\", \"Do associations generalise across schools?\",\n",
    "                   \"sign_consistency\", int(len(S)), f\"Median school sign consistency {sc['school_sign_consistency'].median():.2f}.\")\n",
    "    if \"meta_orig_sr_mode\" in S.columns and S[\"meta_orig_sr_mode\"].nunique() > 1:\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1)\n",
    "        viz.grouped_box(axes[0, 0], pd.DataFrame({\"sr\": S[\"meta_orig_sr_mode\"].astype(str), \"target\": y}), \"target\", \"sr\", \"outcome\")\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"sampling_rate_comparison\", \"Outcome by original sampling rate\", \"Could sampling rate act as a shortcut?\",\n",
    "                   \"student_features\", int(len(S)), \"Modal original sampling rate per student.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-012",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/data_access.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Convenience loaders shared by stages (training-only by default).\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def students(ctx, split: str = \"train\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    sm = ctx.load_df(\"student_master\")\n",
    "    return sm[sm[\"split\"] == split].reset_index(drop=True) if split != \"all\" else sm\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def target(ctx) -> pd.Series:\n",
    "    sm = students(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    y = pd.to_numeric(sm.set_index(\"student_id\")[\"target\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "    return y[np.isfinite(y)]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def clips(ctx, split: str = \"train\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    cm = ctx.load_df(\"clip_master\")\n",
    "    return cm[cm[\"split\"] == split].reset_index(drop=True) if split != \"all\" else cm\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def screening(ctx, split: str = \"train\") -> pd.DataFrame | None:\n",
    "    name = \"screening_features\" if split == \"train\" else \"screening_features_test\"\n",
    "    df = ctx.load_df(name, required=False)\n",
    "    return None if df is None else df.set_index(\"student_id\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def theta_columns(df: pd.DataFrame) -> list:\n",
    "    return [c for c in df.columns if c.startswith(\"theta_\") and not c.startswith(\"theta_se_\")]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def raw_theta_columns(df: pd.DataFrame) -> list:\n",
    "    return [c for c in (\"theta_blending\", \"theta_deletion\", \"theta_repetition\") if c in df.columns] + \\\n",
    "        sorted(c for c in df.columns if c.startswith(\"theta_other_\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def clip_features(ctx, split: str = \"train\", required: bool = False) -> pd.DataFrame | None:\n",
    "    name = \"clip_features\" if split == \"train\" else \"clip_features_test\"\n",
    "    return ctx.load_df(name, required=required)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def item_difficulty(ctx) -> pd.DataFrame | None:\n",
    "    \"\"\"All-training IRT item parameters (EDA only; prediction refits within folds).\"\"\"\n",
    "    if not ctx.stage_available(\"04\"):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    items = ctx.load_df(\"irt_item_params\", required=False)\n",
    "    if items is None or items.empty:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    prim = items[items[\"model\"] == items[\"selected_model\"]] if \"selected_model\" in items.columns else items\n",
    "    return prim[[\"item_key\", \"b\", \"a\"]].drop_duplicates(\"item_key\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def item_linguistics(ctx) -> pd.DataFrame | None:\n",
    "    if not ctx.stage_available(\"11\"):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    return ctx.load_df(\"item_linguistic_features\", required=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def clip_phonetics(ctx, split: str = \"train\") -> pd.DataFrame | None:\n",
    "    if not ctx.stage_available(\"11\"):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    name = \"clip_phonetic_features\" if split == \"train\" else \"clip_phonetic_features_test\"\n",
    "    return ctx.load_df(name, required=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def clip_table(ctx, split: str = \"train\", with_audio: bool = True) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Clip master joined with audio, item difficulty, linguistic and phonetic features.\"\"\"\n",
    "    cm = clips(ctx, split)\n",
    "    if with_audio:\n",
    "        cf = clip_features(ctx, split)\n",
    "        if cf is not None:\n",
    "            cm = cm.merge(cf, on=\"clip_id\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "    diff = item_difficulty(ctx)\n",
    "    if diff is not None:\n",
    "        cm = cm.merge(diff.rename(columns={\"b\": \"item_b\", \"a\": \"item_a\"}), on=\"item_key\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "    ling = item_linguistics(ctx)\n",
    "    if ling is not None:\n",
    "        cm = cm.merge(ling, on=\"item_key\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "    ph = clip_phonetics(ctx, split)\n",
    "    if ph is not None:\n",
    "        cm = cm.merge(ph, on=\"clip_id\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "    return cm\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def residuals(ctx) -> pd.Series | None:\n",
    "    if not ctx.stage_available(\"14\"):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    res = ctx.load_df(\"baseline_residuals\", required=False)\n",
    "    if res is None:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    return res.set_index(\"student_id\")[\"residual\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def oof_baseline(ctx) -> pd.Series | None:\n",
    "    if not ctx.stage_available(\"14\"):\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    res = ctx.load_df(\"baseline_residuals\", required=False)\n",
    "    return None if res is None else res.set_index(\"student_id\")[\"oof_prediction\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def student_features(ctx, split: str = \"train\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    name = \"student_features\" if split == \"train\" else \"student_features_test\"\n",
    "    return ctx.load_df(name).set_index(\"student_id\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def student_meta(ctx, split: str = \"train\") -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    sm = students(ctx, split).set_index(\"student_id\")\n",
    "    cols = [c for c in (\"school_id\", \"instrument\", \"target\") if c in sm.columns]\n",
    "    return sm[cols]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def numeric_frame(df: pd.DataFrame, cols: list) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    out = df[cols].apply(pd.to_numeric, errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "    return out.replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def task_families(ctx) -> list:\n",
    "    cm = clips(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    return sorted(cm[\"task_family\"].dropna().unique().tolist()) if \"task_family\" in cm.columns else []\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-013",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/data_audit.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 01 - data integrity and hierarchical data reconstruction.\n",
    "\n",
    "Scientific question: can the dataset be represented reliably at the student,\n",
    "task, item, clip and acoustic-frame levels?\n",
    "\n",
    "All schemas are discovered at runtime. A schema-resolution layer maps actual\n",
    "columns to canonical names; ambiguous mappings are never guessed silently -\n",
    "they must be resolved through ``CONFIG['schema_overrides']``.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import re\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import audio_manifest as am\n",
    "from .families import sanitize_token\n",
    "\n",
    "FILE_ROLES = {\n",
    "    \"train_student_metadata.csv\": \"student_train\",\n",
    "    \"test_student_metadata.csv\": \"student_test\",\n",
    "    \"train_clip_metadata.csv\": \"clip_train\",\n",
    "    \"test_clip_metadata.csv\": \"clip_test\",\n",
    "    \"train_labels.csv\": \"labels\",\n",
    "    \"submission_format.csv\": \"submission\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "ROLE_GROUP = {\"student_train\": \"student\", \"student_test\": \"student\", \"clip_train\": \"clip\",\n",
    "              \"clip_test\": \"clip\", \"labels\": \"labels\", \"submission\": \"submission\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "READ_CSV_PARAMS = {\n",
    "    \"sep\", \"delimiter\", \"header\", \"names\", \"index_col\", \"usecols\", \"dtype\", \"engine\", \"converters\",\n",
    "    \"true_values\", \"false_values\", \"skipinitialspace\", \"skiprows\", \"skipfooter\", \"nrows\", \"na_values\",\n",
    "    \"keep_default_na\", \"na_filter\", \"parse_dates\", \"date_format\", \"dayfirst\", \"thousands\", \"decimal\",\n",
    "    \"lineterminator\", \"quotechar\", \"quoting\", \"doublequote\", \"escapechar\", \"comment\", \"encoding\",\n",
    "    \"encoding_errors\", \"dialect\", \"on_bad_lines\", \"low_memory\", \"memory_map\", \"float_precision\",\n",
    "    \"dtype_backend\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "FIELD_SPECS: dict = {\n",
    "    \"student\": {\n",
    "        \"student_id\": [r\"^(student|child|participant|subject|learner|pupil|kid)(_?(id|key|uid|identifier|code))?$\", r\"^s_?id$\"],\n",
    "        \"school_id\": [r\"^(school|site|campus)(_?(id|code|name|key))?$\"],\n",
    "        \"instrument\": [r\"(instrument|assessment_?name|assessment_?type|measure|test_?name|test_?type|outcome_?test|eoy_?test|outcome_?measure|score_?type|metric_?name)\"],\n",
    "        \"grade\": [r\"^grade(_?level)?$\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"clip\": {\n",
    "        \"student_id\": [r\"^(student|child|participant|subject|learner|pupil|kid)(_?(id|key|uid|identifier|code))?$\", r\"^s_?id$\"],\n",
    "        \"clip_id\": [r\"^(clip|recording|audio|utterance|response|trial)_?(id|key|uid|identifier)$\", r\"^clip$\", r\"^(file|filename|file_name)_?id$\"],\n",
    "        \"audio_file\": [r\"^(file|filename|file_name|filepath|file_path|path|audio|audio_?file|audio_?path|audio_?filename|wav|wav_?file|wav_?path|recording|recording_?file|clip_?file|clip_?path|clip_?filename)$\"],\n",
    "        \"school_id\": [r\"^(school|site|campus)(_?(id|code|name|key))?$\"],\n",
    "        \"task\": [r\"^(task|task_?name|task_?type|subtest|sub_?test|activity|task_?id|assessment_?task|skill)$\"],\n",
    "        \"item_id\": [r\"^(item|item_?id|item_?name|item_?code|prompt_?id|question_?id|stimulus_?id|word_?id|item_?number)$\"],\n",
    "        \"expected_text\": [r\"^(expected|expected_?text|expected_?response|expected_?answer|prompt|prompt_?text|target_?text|stimulus|stimulus_?text|text|word|target_?word|answer|correct_?answer|correct_?response|sentence|transcript)$\"],\n",
    "        \"correct\": [r\"^(correct|is_?correct|correctness|accuracy|response_?correct|item_?score|score|correct_?flag|accurate|result)$\"],\n",
    "        \"order\": [r\"^(order|item_?order|sequence|seq|seq_?num|sequence_?number|position|item_?position|trial|trial_?num|trial_?number|item_?index|presentation_?order|item_?seq)$\"],\n",
    "        \"timestamp\": [r\"(timestamp|start_?time|datetime|recorded_?at|created_?at|time_?stamp)$\"],\n",
    "        \"response_duration\": [r\"^(duration|response_?time|rt|response_?duration|latency|duration_?s|duration_?sec|length_?s)$\"],\n",
    "        \"orig_sample_rate\": [r\"^(sample_?rate|sampling_?rate|sr|orig_?sr|original_?sample_?rate|samplerate)$\"],\n",
    "        \"deletion_source_text\": [r\"^(source_?word|original_?word|base_?word|full_?word)$\"],\n",
    "        \"deletion_target_sound\": [r\"^(deleted_?sound|delete_?sound|target_?sound|removed_?sound|sound_?to_?delete|deleted_?phoneme)$\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"labels\": {\n",
    "        \"student_id\": [r\"^(student|child|participant|subject|learner|pupil|kid)(_?(id|key|uid|identifier|code))?$\", r\"^s_?id$\"],\n",
    "        \"instrument\": [r\"(instrument|assessment_?name|assessment_?type|measure|test_?name|test_?type|outcome_?test|eoy_?test|outcome_?measure|score_?type|metric_?name)\"],\n",
    "        \"school_id\": [r\"^(school|site|campus)(_?(id|code|name|key))?$\"],\n",
    "        \"target\": [r\"(score|target|label|outcome|eoy|reading|^y)$\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"submission\": {\n",
    "        \"student_id\": [r\"^(student|child|participant|subject|learner|pupil|kid)(_?(id|key|uid|identifier|code))?$\", r\"^s_?id$\"],\n",
    "        \"target\": [r\"(score|target|label|outcome|eoy|reading|prediction|^y)$\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "}\n",
    "REQUIRED_FIELDS = {\"student\": [\"student_id\"], \"clip\": [\"student_id\"], \"labels\": [\"student_id\", \"target\"],\n",
    "                   \"submission\": [\"student_id\"]}\n",
    "SKILL_PATTERNS = {\"blending\": r\"blend\", \"deletion\": r\"(delet|elision|elid)\", \"repetition\": r\"(repet|sentence|srep|imitat)\"}\n",
    "SE_PATTERN = r\"(^|_)(se|sem|stderr|std_?err|error|var|variance|sd)($|_)\"\n",
    "ABILITY_PATTERN = r\"(theta|ability|irt|est|score|boy|screen|eap|mle|level|rasch)\"\n",
    "TASK_PATTERNS = SKILL_PATTERNS\n",
    "TRUE_STRINGS = {\"true\", \"t\", \"correct\", \"yes\", \"y\", \"1\", \"1.0\", \"c\", \"right\"}\n",
    "FALSE_STRINGS = {\"false\", \"f\", \"incorrect\", \"no\", \"n\", \"0\", \"0.0\", \"i\", \"wrong\", \"x\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class SchemaResolutionError(RuntimeError):\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def normalize_name(name: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return re.sub(r\"[^0-9a-z]+\", \"_\", str(name).strip().lower()).strip(\"_\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- CSV\n",
    "def load_read_kwargs(path: Path, files: list) -> tuple[dict, dict]:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Interpret pandas_read_csv_kwargs.json and decide which files it applies to.\"\"\"\n",
    "    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n",
    "        raw = json.load(fh)\n",
    "    report: dict = {\"raw_keys\": list(raw) if isinstance(raw, dict) else str(type(raw)), \"mode\": None}\n",
    "    per_file: dict = {f: {} for f in files}\n",
    "    if not isinstance(raw, dict):\n",
    "        report[\"mode\"] = \"UNRECOGNISED_IGNORED\"\n",
    "        return per_file, report\n",
    "    file_keys = [k for k in raw if k in files or Path(k).name in files or f\"{k}.csv\" in files]\n",
    "    if file_keys and len(file_keys) == len(raw):\n",
    "        report[\"mode\"] = \"PER_FILE\"\n",
    "        for k, v in raw.items():\n",
    "            name = k if k in files else (Path(k).name if Path(k).name in files else f\"{k}.csv\")\n",
    "            per_file[name] = {p: val for p, val in (v or {}).items() if p in READ_CSV_PARAMS}\n",
    "        return per_file, report\n",
    "    params = {k: v for k, v in raw.items() if k in READ_CSV_PARAMS}\n",
    "    report[\"ignored_keys\"] = [k for k in raw if k not in READ_CSV_PARAMS]\n",
    "    report[\"mode\"] = \"GLOBAL\"\n",
    "    for f in files:\n",
    "        per_file[f] = dict(params)\n",
    "    return per_file, report\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _adapt_kwargs(path: Path, kwargs: dict) -> tuple[dict, dict]:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Restrict column-specific arguments to columns that exist in this file.\"\"\"\n",
    "    probe_kwargs = {k: v for k, v in kwargs.items() if k in {\"sep\", \"delimiter\", \"encoding\", \"header\", \"quotechar\", \"comment\"}}\n",
    "    header = pd.read_csv(path, nrows=0, **probe_kwargs).columns.tolist()\n",
    "    applied = dict(kwargs)\n",
    "    notes: dict = {}\n",
    "    if isinstance(applied.get(\"dtype\"), dict):\n",
    "        dtypes = {c: t for c, t in applied[\"dtype\"].items() if c in header}\n",
    "        notes[\"dtype_columns_applied\"] = sorted(dtypes)\n",
    "        notes[\"dtype_columns_not_present\"] = sorted(set(applied[\"dtype\"]) - set(dtypes))\n",
    "        applied[\"dtype\"] = dtypes\n",
    "    if isinstance(applied.get(\"parse_dates\"), list):\n",
    "        applied[\"parse_dates\"] = [c for c in applied[\"parse_dates\"] if c in header]\n",
    "    if isinstance(applied.get(\"usecols\"), list):\n",
    "        applied[\"usecols\"] = [c for c in applied[\"usecols\"] if c in header]\n",
    "    if isinstance(applied.get(\"converters\"), dict):\n",
    "        applied.pop(\"converters\")\n",
    "        notes[\"converters_ignored\"] = True\n",
    "    return applied, notes\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def read_tables(data_root: Path, logger) -> tuple[dict, dict]:\n",
    "    files = [f for f in FILE_ROLES]\n",
    "    per_file, kw_report = load_read_kwargs(data_root / \"pandas_read_csv_kwargs.json\", files)\n",
    "    tables: dict = {}\n",
    "    report: dict = {\"read_csv_kwargs\": kw_report, \"files\": {}}\n",
    "    for fname, role in FILE_ROLES.items():\n",
    "        path = data_root / fname\n",
    "        applied, notes = _adapt_kwargs(path, per_file.get(fname, {}))\n",
    "        df = pd.read_csv(path, low_memory=False, **applied)\n",
    "        tables[role] = df\n",
    "        report[\"files\"][fname] = {\"role\": role, \"shape\": list(df.shape), \"kwargs_applied\": applied, **notes}\n",
    "        logger.info(\"Read %s: %s rows x %s cols\", fname, df.shape[0], df.shape[1])\n",
    "    return tables, report\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def profile_table(df: pd.DataFrame, table: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    n = len(df)\n",
    "    for col in df.columns:\n",
    "        s = df[col]\n",
    "        num = pd.to_numeric(s, errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "        rows.append({\n",
    "            \"table\": table, \"column\": col, \"normalized\": normalize_name(col), \"dtype\": str(s.dtype),\n",
    "            \"n_rows\": n, \"n_missing\": int(s.isna().sum()), \"missing_rate\": float(s.isna().mean()) if n else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"n_unique\": int(s.nunique(dropna=True)), \"unique_ratio\": float(s.nunique(dropna=True) / max(n, 1)),\n",
    "            \"numeric_fraction\": float(num.notna().sum() / max(s.notna().sum(), 1)),\n",
    "            \"min\": float(num.min()) if num.notna().any() else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"max\": float(num.max()) if num.notna().any() else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"mean\": float(num.mean()) if num.notna().any() else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"examples\": \"; \".join(map(str, s.dropna().unique()[:3])),\n",
    "        })\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------ schema resolution\n",
    "def resolve_fields(df: pd.DataFrame, group: str, overrides: dict) -> dict:\n",
    "    specs = FIELD_SPECS[group]\n",
    "    norm = {c: normalize_name(c) for c in df.columns}\n",
    "    assigned: dict = {}\n",
    "    ambiguous: dict = {}\n",
    "    used: set = set()\n",
    "    over = overrides.get(group, {}) or {}\n",
    "    for field, col in over.items():\n",
    "        if col not in df.columns:\n",
    "            raise SchemaResolutionError(f\"schema_overrides[{group}][{field}]={col!r} not in columns {list(df.columns)}\")\n",
    "        assigned[field] = col\n",
    "        used.add(col)\n",
    "    for field, patterns in specs.items():\n",
    "        if field in assigned:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        matches = [c for c in df.columns if c not in used and any(re.search(p, norm[c]) for p in patterns)]\n",
    "        if field == \"target\":\n",
    "            matches = [c for c in matches if pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors=\"coerce\").notna().mean() > 0.95]\n",
    "        if len(matches) == 1:\n",
    "            assigned[field] = matches[0]\n",
    "            used.add(matches[0])\n",
    "        elif len(matches) > 1:\n",
    "            exact = [c for c in matches if norm[c] == field]\n",
    "            if len(exact) == 1:\n",
    "                assigned[field] = exact[0]\n",
    "                used.add(exact[0])\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                ambiguous[field] = matches\n",
    "    if group in {\"labels\", \"submission\"} and \"target\" not in assigned and \"target\" not in ambiguous:\n",
    "        numeric = [c for c in df.columns if c not in used and pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors=\"coerce\").notna().mean() > 0.95]\n",
    "        if len(numeric) == 1:\n",
    "            assigned[\"target\"] = numeric[0]\n",
    "            used.add(numeric[0])\n",
    "        elif len(numeric) > 1:\n",
    "            ambiguous[\"target\"] = numeric\n",
    "    missing = [f for f in REQUIRED_FIELDS.get(group, []) if f not in assigned]\n",
    "    return {\"assigned\": assigned, \"ambiguous\": ambiguous, \"missing_required\": missing,\n",
    "            \"unassigned_columns\": [c for c in df.columns if c not in used]}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def resolve_thetas(df: pd.DataFrame, exclude: set, overrides: dict) -> dict:\n",
    "    over = (overrides.get(\"student\", {}) or {})\n",
    "    result: dict = {\"theta\": {}, \"theta_se\": {}, \"ambiguous\": {}, \"other\": {}}\n",
    "    for skill in SKILL_PATTERNS:\n",
    "        key = f\"theta_{skill}\"\n",
    "        if key in over:\n",
    "            result[\"theta\"][skill] = over[key]\n",
    "    numeric_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c not in exclude\n",
    "                    and pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors=\"coerce\").notna().mean() > 0.5]\n",
    "    claimed = set(result[\"theta\"].values())\n",
    "    for skill, rx in SKILL_PATTERNS.items():\n",
    "        cands = [c for c in numeric_cols if c not in claimed and re.search(rx, normalize_name(c))]\n",
    "        se = [c for c in cands if re.search(SE_PATTERN, normalize_name(c))]\n",
    "        est = [c for c in cands if c not in se]\n",
    "        if se:\n",
    "            result[\"theta_se\"][skill] = se[0] if len(se) == 1 else se\n",
    "        if skill in result[\"theta\"]:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        if len(est) > 1:\n",
    "            preferred = [c for c in est if re.search(ABILITY_PATTERN, normalize_name(c))]\n",
    "            est = preferred if len(preferred) >= 1 else est\n",
    "        if len(est) == 1:\n",
    "            result[\"theta\"][skill] = est[0]\n",
    "            claimed.add(est[0])\n",
    "        elif len(est) > 1:\n",
    "            result[\"ambiguous\"][skill] = est\n",
    "    for c in numeric_cols:\n",
    "        if c in claimed or any(c == v or (isinstance(v, list) and c in v) for v in result[\"theta_se\"].values()):\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        if re.search(r\"(theta|ability|irt|rasch)\", normalize_name(c)):\n",
    "            result[\"other\"][c] = f\"theta_other_{sanitize_token(c)}\"\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def normalize_correct(series: pd.Series, threshold=None) -> tuple[pd.Series, pd.Series, dict]:\n",
    "    s = series.copy()\n",
    "    info: dict = {\"original_dtype\": str(series.dtype)}\n",
    "    if s.dtype == bool:\n",
    "        out = s.astype(float)\n",
    "        info[\"mode\"] = \"BOOLEAN\"\n",
    "        return out, out, info\n",
    "    num = pd.to_numeric(s, errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "    if num.notna().sum() >= 0.95 * s.notna().sum() and s.notna().any():\n",
    "        vals = set(np.unique(num.dropna()))\n",
    "        if vals <= {0.0, 1.0}:\n",
    "            info[\"mode\"] = \"BINARY_NUMERIC\"\n",
    "            return num, num, info\n",
    "        info[\"mode\"] = \"PARTIAL_SCORE\"\n",
    "        info[\"unique_values\"] = sorted(map(float, list(vals)[:20]))\n",
    "        if threshold is not None:\n",
    "            info[\"binarized_at\"] = float(threshold)\n",
    "            return (num >= threshold).astype(float).where(num.notna()), num, info\n",
    "        info[\"note\"] = \"Not binary; correct left missing. Set correct_binarize_threshold to binarise.\"\n",
    "        return pd.Series(np.nan, index=s.index), num, info\n",
    "    low = s.astype(str).str.strip().str.lower()\n",
    "    mapped = pd.Series(np.where(low.isin(TRUE_STRINGS), 1.0, np.where(low.isin(FALSE_STRINGS), 0.0, np.nan)), index=s.index)\n",
    "    mapped[s.isna()] = np.nan\n",
    "    info[\"mode\"] = \"STRING_MAPPED\"\n",
    "    info[\"unmapped_values\"] = sorted(set(low[mapped.isna() & s.notna()].unique()))[:20]\n",
    "    return mapped, mapped, info\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def task_family(value, overrides: dict) -> str:\n",
    "    if pd.isna(value):\n",
    "        return \"unknown\"\n",
    "    if str(value) in overrides:\n",
    "        return overrides[str(value)]\n",
    "    low = normalize_name(value)\n",
    "    matches = [fam for fam, rx in TASK_PATTERNS.items() if re.search(rx, low)]\n",
    "    return matches[0] if len(matches) == 1 else f\"other_{sanitize_token(value)}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def normalize_text(text) -> str:\n",
    "    if pd.isna(text):\n",
    "        return \"\"\n",
    "    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", str(text).strip().lower())\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------- join keys\n",
    "def candidate_join_keys(tables: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    names = list(tables)\n",
    "    for i, a in enumerate(names):\n",
    "        for b in names[i + 1:]:\n",
    "            na = {normalize_name(c): c for c in tables[a].columns}\n",
    "            nb = {normalize_name(c): c for c in tables[b].columns}\n",
    "            for key in sorted(set(na) & set(nb)):\n",
    "                va = set(tables[a][na[key]].dropna().astype(str))\n",
    "                vb = set(tables[b][nb[key]].dropna().astype(str))\n",
    "                if not va or not vb:\n",
    "                    continue\n",
    "                inter = len(va & vb)\n",
    "                rows.append({\"table_a\": a, \"table_b\": b, \"column_a\": na[key], \"column_b\": nb[key],\n",
    "                             \"unique_a\": len(va), \"unique_b\": len(vb), \"overlap\": inter,\n",
    "                             \"overlap_fraction_of_smaller\": inter / min(len(va), len(vb))})\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _canonical(df: pd.DataFrame, assigned: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    rename = {col: field for field, col in assigned.items()}\n",
    "    out = df.rename(columns=rename)\n",
    "    collisions = [c for c in out.columns[out.columns.duplicated()]]\n",
    "    if collisions:\n",
    "        raise SchemaResolutionError(f\"canonical name collision: {collisions}\")\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _id_str(s: pd.Series) -> pd.Series:\n",
    "    out = s.astype(\"string\").str.strip()\n",
    "    return out.astype(object).where(out.notna(), np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _dedupe_students(df: pd.DataFrame, report: dict, label: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    dup = df[\"student_id\"].duplicated(keep=False)\n",
    "    if not dup.any():\n",
    "        report[f\"{label}_duplicate_rows\"] = 0\n",
    "        return df\n",
    "    exact = df[dup].duplicated(keep=\"first\")\n",
    "    conflicting_ids = df[dup].drop_duplicates().groupby(\"student_id\").size()\n",
    "    conflicting_ids = conflicting_ids[conflicting_ids > 1].index.tolist()\n",
    "    report[f\"{label}_duplicate_rows\"] = int(dup.sum())\n",
    "    report[f\"{label}_exact_duplicates_removed\"] = int(exact.sum())\n",
    "    report[f\"{label}_conflicting_student_ids\"] = conflicting_ids[:50]\n",
    "    report[f\"{label}_n_conflicting_student_ids\"] = len(conflicting_ids)\n",
    "    out = df.drop_duplicates().drop_duplicates(\"student_id\", keep=\"first\").copy()\n",
    "    out[\"student_record_conflict\"] = out[\"student_id\"].isin(conflicting_ids)\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def sample_students(student_ids: pd.Series, clip_counts: pd.Series, cfg: dict) -> list:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Student-level sampling for SMOKE/DEBUG profiles (never samples clips independently).\"\"\"\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "    ids = np.array(sorted(student_ids.unique()))\n",
    "    rng.shuffle(ids)\n",
    "    chosen, total = [], 0\n",
    "    for sid in ids:\n",
    "        c = int(clip_counts.get(sid, 0))\n",
    "        if len(chosen) >= int(cfg[\"debug_max_students\"]):\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        if chosen and total + c > int(cfg[\"debug_max_clips\"]):\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        chosen.append(sid)\n",
    "        total += c\n",
    "    return chosen\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------------ stage\n",
    "def stage_data_audit(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    logger = ctx.logger\n",
    "    data_root = ctx.data_root()\n",
    "    tables, read_report = read_tables(data_root, logger)\n",
    "    overrides = cfg.get(\"schema_overrides\") or {}\n",
    "    profiles = pd.concat([profile_table(df, role) for role, df in tables.items()], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(profiles, \"column_profiles\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    schema: dict = {\"read_report\": read_report, \"groups\": {}, \"warnings\": []}\n",
    "    for group, roles in {\"student\": [\"student_train\", \"student_test\"], \"clip\": [\"clip_train\", \"clip_test\"],\n",
    "                         \"labels\": [\"labels\"], \"submission\": [\"submission\"]}.items():\n",
    "        primary = tables[roles[0]]\n",
    "        res = resolve_fields(primary, group, overrides)\n",
    "        if len(roles) > 1:\n",
    "            other = tables[roles[1]]\n",
    "            res[\"columns_only_in_train\"] = sorted(set(primary.columns) - set(other.columns))\n",
    "            res[\"columns_only_in_test\"] = sorted(set(other.columns) - set(primary.columns))\n",
    "            res[\"test_missing_assigned\"] = [c for c in res[\"assigned\"].values() if c not in other.columns]\n",
    "        schema[\"groups\"][group] = res\n",
    "    st = schema[\"groups\"][\"student\"]\n",
    "    thetas = resolve_thetas(tables[\"student_train\"], set(st[\"assigned\"].values()), overrides)\n",
    "    schema[\"thetas\"] = thetas\n",
    "    problems = {g: {\"missing_required\": r[\"missing_required\"], \"ambiguous\": r[\"ambiguous\"]}\n",
    "                for g, r in schema[\"groups\"].items() if r[\"missing_required\"] or (\n",
    "                    r[\"ambiguous\"] and set(r[\"ambiguous\"]) & set(REQUIRED_FIELDS.get(g, []) + [\"clip_id\", \"audio_file\", \"task\", \"correct\"]))}\n",
    "    if thetas[\"ambiguous\"]:\n",
    "        problems[\"thetas\"] = thetas[\"ambiguous\"]\n",
    "    ctx.save_json(schema, \"schema_registry\")\n",
    "    if problems:\n",
    "        raise SchemaResolutionError(\n",
    "            \"Schema could not be resolved unambiguously. Inspect schema_registry.json and set \"\n",
    "            f\"CONFIG['schema_overrides']. Problems: {json.dumps(problems, default=str)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    quality: dict = {\"tables\": read_report[\"files\"]}\n",
    "    # ---- students -------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    sa = st[\"assigned\"]\n",
    "    theta_map = {col: f\"theta_{skill}\" for skill, col in thetas[\"theta\"].items()}\n",
    "    for skill, col in thetas[\"theta_se\"].items():\n",
    "        if isinstance(col, str):\n",
    "            theta_map[col] = f\"theta_se_{skill}\"\n",
    "    theta_map.update(thetas[\"other\"])\n",
    "    stud = []\n",
    "    for role, split in ((\"student_train\", \"train\"), (\"student_test\", \"test\")):\n",
    "        df = _canonical(tables[role], {k: v for k, v in sa.items() if v in tables[role].columns}).rename(columns=theta_map)\n",
    "        df[\"student_id\"] = _id_str(df[\"student_id\"])\n",
    "        df[\"split\"] = split\n",
    "        for c in theta_map.values():\n",
    "            if c in df.columns:\n",
    "                df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "        stud.append(_dedupe_students(df, quality, f\"students_{split}\"))\n",
    "    students = pd.concat(stud, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    overlap_students = set(stud[0][\"student_id\"]) & set(stud[1][\"student_id\"])\n",
    "    quality[\"train_test_student_overlap\"] = len(overlap_students)\n",
    "    # ---- labels -----------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    la = schema[\"groups\"][\"labels\"][\"assigned\"]\n",
    "    labels = _canonical(tables[\"labels\"], la)\n",
    "    labels[\"student_id\"] = _id_str(labels[\"student_id\"])\n",
    "    labels[\"target\"] = pd.to_numeric(labels[\"target\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "    quality[\"labels_duplicate_students\"] = int(labels[\"student_id\"].duplicated().sum())\n",
    "    if quality[\"labels_duplicate_students\"]:\n",
    "        conflict = labels.groupby(\"student_id\")[\"target\"].nunique()\n",
    "        quality[\"labels_conflicting_students\"] = int((conflict > 1).sum())\n",
    "        labels = labels.drop_duplicates(\"student_id\", keep=\"first\")\n",
    "    label_cols = [\"student_id\", \"target\"] + [c for c in (\"instrument\", \"school_id\") if c in labels.columns]\n",
    "    train_ids = set(stud[0][\"student_id\"])\n",
    "    quality[\"labels_not_in_train_students\"] = int((~labels[\"student_id\"].isin(train_ids)).sum())\n",
    "    quality[\"train_students_without_label\"] = int(len(train_ids - set(labels[\"student_id\"])))\n",
    "    quality[\"labels_in_test_students\"] = int(labels[\"student_id\"].isin(set(stud[1][\"student_id\"])).sum())\n",
    "    lab = labels[label_cols].rename(columns={\"instrument\": \"instrument_label\", \"school_id\": \"school_label\"})\n",
    "    students = students.merge(lab, on=\"student_id\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "    students.loc[students[\"split\"] != \"train\", \"target\"] = np.nan\n",
    "    for base, extra in ((\"instrument\", \"instrument_label\"), (\"school_id\", \"school_label\")):\n",
    "        if extra in students.columns:\n",
    "            if base in students.columns:\n",
    "                both = students[base].notna() & students[extra].notna()\n",
    "                quality[f\"{base}_label_conflicts\"] = int((students.loc[both, base].astype(str) != students.loc[both, extra].astype(str)).sum())\n",
    "                students[base] = students[base].where(students[base].notna(), students[extra])\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                students[base] = students[extra]\n",
    "            students = students.drop(columns=[extra])\n",
    "    for col in (\"school_id\", \"instrument\"):\n",
    "        if col not in students.columns:\n",
    "            students[col] = np.nan\n",
    "            schema[\"warnings\"].append(f\"{col} unavailable: grouped analyses will report fallbacks\")\n",
    "    students[\"school_id\"] = students[\"school_id\"].astype(object).where(students[\"school_id\"].notna(), np.nan)\n",
    "    if students[\"student_id\"].duplicated().any():\n",
    "        raise SchemaResolutionError(\"student_master would contain duplicate student ids\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ---- clips --------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    ca = schema[\"groups\"][\"clip\"][\"assigned\"]\n",
    "    clip_parts = []\n",
    "    correct_info = {}\n",
    "    for role, split in ((\"clip_train\", \"train\"), (\"clip_test\", \"test\")):\n",
    "        df = _canonical(tables[role], {k: v for k, v in ca.items() if v in tables[role].columns})\n",
    "        df[\"student_id\"] = _id_str(df[\"student_id\"])\n",
    "        if \"clip_id\" not in df.columns:\n",
    "            if \"audio_file\" in df.columns:\n",
    "                df[\"clip_id\"] = df[\"audio_file\"].astype(str).map(lambda s: Path(s.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")).stem)\n",
    "                schema[\"warnings\"].append(f\"{role}: clip_id derived from audio_file stem\")\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                raise SchemaResolutionError(f\"{role}: neither clip_id nor audio_file could be resolved\")\n",
    "        df[\"clip_id\"] = _id_str(df[\"clip_id\"])\n",
    "        df[\"split\"] = split\n",
    "        if \"correct\" in df.columns:\n",
    "            df[\"correct\"], df[\"correct_score\"], correct_info[split] = normalize_correct(\n",
    "                df[\"correct\"], cfg.get(\"correct_binarize_threshold\"))\n",
    "        for col in (\"order\", \"response_duration\", \"orig_sample_rate\"):\n",
    "            if col in df.columns:\n",
    "                df[col] = pd.to_numeric(df[col], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "        if \"timestamp\" in df.columns:\n",
    "            df[\"timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"timestamp\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "        clip_parts.append(df)\n",
    "    clips = pd.concat(clip_parts, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    quality[\"correctness_normalization\"] = correct_info\n",
    "    dup_clip = clips.duplicated([\"split\", \"clip_id\"], keep=False)\n",
    "    quality[\"duplicate_clip_ids\"] = int(dup_clip.sum())\n",
    "    if dup_clip.any():\n",
    "        clips[\"clip_id_original\"] = clips[\"clip_id\"]\n",
    "        clips.loc[dup_clip, \"clip_id\"] = clips.loc[dup_clip, \"clip_id\"] + \"__dup\" + clips[dup_clip].groupby([\"split\", \"clip_id\"]).cumcount().astype(str)\n",
    "    quality[\"train_test_clip_id_overlap\"] = int(len(set(clips.loc[clips.split == \"train\", \"clip_id\"]) & set(clips.loc[clips.split == \"test\", \"clip_id\"])))\n",
    "    known = set(students[\"student_id\"])\n",
    "    quality[\"clips_with_unknown_student\"] = int((~clips[\"student_id\"].isin(known)).sum())\n",
    "    split_check = clips.merge(students[[\"student_id\", \"split\"]].rename(columns={\"split\": \"student_split\"}), on=\"student_id\", how=\"left\")\n",
    "    quality[\"clips_split_mismatch\"] = int((split_check[\"student_split\"].notna() & (split_check[\"student_split\"] != split_check[\"split\"])).sum())\n",
    "    if \"task\" not in clips.columns:\n",
    "        clips[\"task\"] = \"unknown_task\"\n",
    "        schema[\"warnings\"].append(\"task unavailable: all clips treated as one task\")\n",
    "    tf_over = cfg.get(\"task_family_overrides\") or {}\n",
    "    clips[\"task_family\"] = clips[\"task\"].map(lambda v: task_family(v, tf_over))\n",
    "    if \"item_id\" in clips.columns:\n",
    "        clips[\"item_key\"] = clips[\"task_family\"] + \"||\" + clips[\"item_id\"].astype(str)\n",
    "        item_source = \"item_id\"\n",
    "    elif \"expected_text\" in clips.columns:\n",
    "        clips[\"item_key\"] = clips[\"task_family\"] + \"||\" + clips[\"expected_text\"].map(normalize_text)\n",
    "        item_source = \"task_family+expected_text\"\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        clips[\"item_key\"] = np.nan\n",
    "        item_source = \"UNAVAILABLE\"\n",
    "    schema[\"item_key_source\"] = item_source\n",
    "    if \"school_id\" in clips.columns:\n",
    "        clips = clips.rename(columns={\"school_id\": \"clip_school_id\"})\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ---- audio inventory -----------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    manifests, match_reports = [], {}\n",
    "    clips[\"audio_archive\"] = np.where(clips[\"split\"] == \"train\", \"train_audio.tar\", \"test_audio.tar\")\n",
    "    for split, archive in ((\"train\", \"train_audio.tar\"), (\"test\", \"test_audio.tar\")):\n",
    "        tar_path = data_root / archive\n",
    "        members = am.inspect_archive(tar_path)\n",
    "        quality[f\"{split}_archive_members\"] = int(len(members))\n",
    "        quality[f\"{split}_unsafe_members\"] = members.loc[~members[\"safe\"], [\"member\", \"safety_reason\"]].head(50).to_dict(\"records\") if len(members) else []\n",
    "        quality[f\"{split}_non_audio_members\"] = int((~members[\"is_audio_ext\"]).sum()) if len(members) else 0\n",
    "        sub = clips[clips[\"split\"] == split]\n",
    "        matched, rep = am.match_clips_to_members(sub, members, split)\n",
    "        match_reports[split] = rep\n",
    "        clips.loc[matched.index, \"audio_member\"] = matched[\"audio_member\"]\n",
    "        clips.loc[matched.index, \"audio_match_key\"] = matched[\"audio_match_key\"]\n",
    "        decode = bool(cfg.get(\"audio_inventory_decode\")) and (split == \"train\" or cfg.get(\"allow_test_inference\") or cfg.get(\"extract_test_audio\"))\n",
    "        inv = am.audio_inventory(tar_path, members, decode=decode, hash_bytes=bool(cfg.get(\"audio_inventory_hash\")), logger=logger)\n",
    "        inv[\"split\"] = split\n",
    "        manifests.append(inv)\n",
    "    manifest = pd.concat(manifests, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    clip_links = (clips.dropna(subset=[\"audio_member\"]).groupby([\"audio_archive\", \"audio_member\"])[\"clip_id\"]\n",
    "                  .agg(lambda s: \";\".join(map(str, s))).reset_index()\n",
    "                  .rename(columns={\"audio_archive\": \"archive\", \"audio_member\": \"member\", \"clip_id\": \"linked_clip_ids\"}))\n",
    "    manifest = manifest.merge(clip_links, on=[\"archive\", \"member\"], how=\"left\")\n",
    "    if \"sha1\" in manifest.columns:\n",
    "        hashed = manifest.dropna(subset=[\"sha1\"])\n",
    "        quality[\"duplicate_audio_within_split\"] = {s: int(g[\"sha1\"].duplicated(keep=False).sum()) for s, g in hashed.groupby(\"split\")}\n",
    "        tr = set(hashed.loc[hashed.split == \"train\", \"sha1\"])\n",
    "        te = set(hashed.loc[hashed.split == \"test\", \"sha1\"])\n",
    "        quality[\"identical_audio_train_test\"] = len(tr & te)\n",
    "    quality[\"audio_matching\"] = match_reports\n",
    "    quality[\"decode_status_counts\"] = manifest.groupby([\"split\", \"decode_status\"]).size().reset_index(name=\"n\").to_dict(\"records\")\n",
    "    if \"sample_rate\" in manifest.columns:\n",
    "        quality[\"sample_rate_counts\"] = manifest.groupby([\"split\", \"sample_rate\"]).size().reset_index(name=\"n\").to_dict(\"records\")\n",
    "        quality[\"channel_counts\"] = manifest.groupby([\"split\", \"channels\"]).size().reset_index(name=\"n\").to_dict(\"records\")\n",
    "        meta_cols = manifest[[\"archive\", \"member\", \"sample_rate\", \"channels\", \"duration_s\", \"size_bytes\", \"decode_status\"]]\n",
    "        meta_cols = meta_cols.drop_duplicates([\"archive\", \"member\"]).rename(\n",
    "            columns={\"archive\": \"audio_archive\", \"member\": \"audio_member\", \"sample_rate\": \"audio_sample_rate\",\n",
    "                     \"channels\": \"audio_channels\", \"duration_s\": \"audio_duration_s\", \"size_bytes\": \"audio_size_bytes\",\n",
    "                     \"decode_status\": \"audio_decode_status\"})\n",
    "        clips = clips.merge(meta_cols, on=[\"audio_archive\", \"audio_member\"], how=\"left\")\n",
    "        if \"response_duration\" in clips.columns:\n",
    "            both = clips[[\"response_duration\", \"audio_duration_s\"]].dropna()\n",
    "            if len(both) > 10:\n",
    "                quality[\"metadata_vs_audio_duration_spearman\"] = float(both.corr(method=\"spearman\").iloc[0, 1])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ---- sampling (student level) ----------------------------------------------\n",
    "    if cfg[\"run_mode\"] in {\"SMOKE\", \"DEBUG\"} or cfg.get(\"resumed_profile\") in {\"SMOKE\", \"DEBUG\"}:\n",
    "        tr_students = students[(students.split == \"train\") & students[\"target\"].notna()][\"student_id\"]\n",
    "        counts = clips[clips.split == \"train\"].groupby(\"student_id\").size()\n",
    "        keep = set(sample_students(tr_students, counts, cfg))\n",
    "        test_keep = set(students[students.split == \"test\"][\"student_id\"].head(int(cfg[\"debug_max_students\"])))\n",
    "        students = students[students[\"student_id\"].isin(keep | test_keep)].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "        clips = clips[clips[\"student_id\"].isin(keep | test_keep)].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "        quality[\"sampling\"] = {\"mode\": \"STUDENT_LEVEL\", \"train_students\": len(keep), \"test_students\": len(test_keep)}\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ---- hierarchical tables --------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    train_clips = clips[clips.split == \"train\"]\n",
    "    n_clips = clips.groupby(\"student_id\").size()\n",
    "    students[\"n_clips\"] = students[\"student_id\"].map(n_clips).fillna(0).astype(int)\n",
    "    agg = {\"n_clips_train\": (\"clip_id\", lambda s: int((clips.loc[s.index, \"split\"] == \"train\").sum())),\n",
    "           \"n_clips_test\": (\"clip_id\", lambda s: int((clips.loc[s.index, \"split\"] == \"test\").sum())),\n",
    "           \"n_students\": (\"student_id\", \"nunique\")}\n",
    "    task_master = clips.groupby([\"task\", \"task_family\"], dropna=False).agg(**agg).reset_index()\n",
    "    if item_source != \"UNAVAILABLE\":\n",
    "        item_cols = {\"n_exposures\": (\"clip_id\", \"size\"), \"n_students\": (\"student_id\", \"nunique\")}\n",
    "        if \"correct\" in train_clips.columns:\n",
    "            item_cols.update(n_scored=(\"correct\", \"count\"), p_correct=(\"correct\", \"mean\"))\n",
    "        item_master = train_clips.groupby(\"item_key\").agg(**item_cols).reset_index()\n",
    "        firsts = train_clips.drop_duplicates(\"item_key\").set_index(\"item_key\")\n",
    "        for c in (\"task\", \"task_family\", \"item_id\", \"expected_text\", \"deletion_source_text\", \"deletion_target_sound\"):\n",
    "            if c in firsts.columns:\n",
    "                item_master[c] = item_master[\"item_key\"].map(firsts[c])\n",
    "        test_items = set(clips.loc[clips.split == \"test\", \"item_key\"].dropna())\n",
    "        item_master[\"seen_in_test\"] = item_master[\"item_key\"].isin(test_items)\n",
    "        quality[\"test_items_unseen_in_train\"] = int(len(test_items - set(item_master[\"item_key\"])))\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        item_master = pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"item_key\"])\n",
    "    inventory = pd.DataFrame([{\"file\": f, \"role\": FILE_ROLES.get(f, \"archive\" if f.endswith(\".tar\") else \"config\"),\n",
    "                               \"size_bytes\": (data_root / f).stat().st_size,\n",
    "                               \"rows\": read_report[\"files\"].get(f, {}).get(\"shape\", [np.nan, np.nan])[0],\n",
    "                               \"cols\": read_report[\"files\"].get(f, {}).get(\"shape\", [np.nan, np.nan])[1]}\n",
    "                              for f in cfg[\"required_files\"]])\n",
    "    joins = candidate_join_keys(tables)\n",
    "    quality.update({\n",
    "        \"n_students\": {s: int((students.split == s).sum()) for s in (\"train\", \"test\")},\n",
    "        \"n_clips\": {s: int((clips.split == s).sum()) for s in (\"train\", \"test\")},\n",
    "        \"n_tasks\": int(clips[\"task\"].nunique()), \"task_families\": sorted(clips[\"task_family\"].unique().tolist()),\n",
    "        \"n_items\": int(len(item_master)), \"item_key_source\": item_source,\n",
    "        \"n_schools\": int(students[\"school_id\"].nunique()), \"n_instruments\": int(students[\"instrument\"].nunique()),\n",
    "        \"train_target_missing\": int(students.loc[students.split == \"train\", \"target\"].isna().sum()),\n",
    "        \"clips_missing_audio\": int(clips[\"audio_member\"].isna().sum()),\n",
    "        \"warnings\": schema[\"warnings\"],\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(students, \"student_master\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(clips, \"clip_master\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(task_master, \"task_master\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(item_master, \"item_master\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(manifest, \"audio_manifest\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(inventory, \"dataset_inventory\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(joins, \"candidate_join_keys\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_json(schema, \"schema_registry\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_json(quality, \"data_quality_report\")\n",
    "    _audit_figures(ctx, students, clips, manifest)\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": [\"student_master\", \"clip_master\", \"task_master\", \"item_master\", \"audio_manifest\",\n",
    "                        \"dataset_inventory\", \"schema_registry\", \"data_quality_report\", \"column_profiles\",\n",
    "                        \"candidate_join_keys\"],\n",
    "            \"summary\": {\"n_students\": quality[\"n_students\"], \"n_clips\": quality[\"n_clips\"],\n",
    "                        \"item_key_source\": item_source, \"warnings\": len(schema[\"warnings\"])}}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _audit_figures(ctx, students: pd.DataFrame, clips: pd.DataFrame, manifest: pd.DataFrame) -> None:\n",
    "    from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "\n",
    "    viz.missingness_matrix(ctx, clips[clips.split == \"train\"], \"clip_missingness\", \"Training clip metadata missingness\", \"clip_master\")\n",
    "    per_student = clips[clips.split == \"train\"].groupby(\"student_id\").size()\n",
    "    fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 2)\n",
    "    viz.hist_kde(axes[0, 0], per_student.to_numpy(), \"clips per training student\", \"clips\")\n",
    "    if \"duration_s\" in manifest.columns:\n",
    "        viz.hist_kde(axes[0, 1], manifest.loc[manifest.split == \"train\", \"duration_s\"], \"training recording duration\", \"s\")\n",
    "    ctx.figure(fig, \"clips_and_durations\", \"Clips per student and recording durations\",\n",
    "               \"How many observations does each student contribute?\", \"clip_master/audio_manifest\", int(len(per_student)),\n",
    "               f\"Median clips per student {per_student.median():.1f} (IQR {per_student.quantile(.25):.1f}-{per_student.quantile(.75):.1f}).\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-014",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/environment.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 00 - environment detection, diagnostics, Drive mounting and seeds.\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import importlib\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import platform\n",
    "import random\n",
    "import shutil\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from .paths import discover_data_root\n",
    "\n",
    "MIN_PYTHON = (3, 9)\n",
    "\n",
    "CORE_PACKAGES = [\n",
    "    \"numpy\", \"pandas\", \"scipy\", \"sklearn\", \"pyarrow\", \"matplotlib\", \"joblib\",\n",
    "    \"tqdm\", \"psutil\", \"yaml\", \"soundfile\", \"librosa\", \"pywt\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "OPTIONAL_PACKAGES = [\n",
    "    \"catboost\", \"xgboost\", \"lightgbm\", \"umap\", \"hdbscan\", \"shap\", \"torch\",\n",
    "    \"torchaudio\", \"transformers\", \"webrtcvad\", \"g2p_en\", \"pronouncing\", \"nltk\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "PACKAGE_DIST_NAMES = {\"sklearn\": \"scikit-learn\", \"yaml\": \"PyYAML\", \"pywt\": \"PyWavelets\", \"umap\": \"umap-learn\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def detect_environment() -> str:\n",
    "    if \"google.colab\" in sys.modules or os.environ.get(\"COLAB_RELEASE_TAG\") or os.environ.get(\"COLAB_GPU\") is not None:\n",
    "        return \"COLAB\"\n",
    "    if platform.system() == \"Windows\":\n",
    "        return \"LOCAL_WINDOWS\"\n",
    "    return \"LOCAL_LINUX\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def check_python() -> dict:\n",
    "    ok = sys.version_info[:2] >= MIN_PYTHON\n",
    "    return {\"python_version\": platform.python_version(), \"minimum\": \".\".join(map(str, MIN_PYTHON)), \"ok\": ok}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def package_versions(names: list[str]) -> dict:\n",
    "    from importlib import metadata\n",
    "\n",
    "    out = {}\n",
    "    for name in names:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            module = importlib.import_module(name)\n",
    "            version = getattr(module, \"__version__\", None)\n",
    "            if version is None:\n",
    "                version = metadata.version(PACKAGE_DIST_NAMES.get(name, name))\n",
    "            out[name] = {\"available\": True, \"version\": str(version)}\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:  # pragma: no cover - environment dependent\n",
    "            out[name] = {\"available\": False, \"error\": type(exc).__name__}\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def is_available(name: str) -> bool:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        importlib.import_module(name)\n",
    "        return True\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        return False\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def gpu_report(use_gpu: bool) -> dict:\n",
    "    report: dict = {\"requested\": bool(use_gpu), \"torch_cuda\": False, \"devices\": []}\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import torch  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "        report[\"torch_cuda\"] = bool(torch.cuda.is_available())\n",
    "        if report[\"torch_cuda\"]:\n",
    "            for i in range(torch.cuda.device_count()):\n",
    "                props = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(i)\n",
    "                report[\"devices\"].append({\"index\": i, \"name\": props.name, \"total_memory_gb\": props.total_memory / 1e9})\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "    if not report[\"devices\"] and shutil.which(\"nvidia-smi\"):\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            res = subprocess.run([\"nvidia-smi\", \"--query-gpu=name,memory.total\", \"--format=csv,noheader\"],\n",
    "                                 capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)\n",
    "            report[\"nvidia_smi\"] = res.stdout.strip()\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            pass\n",
    "    report[\"will_use_gpu\"] = bool(use_gpu and report[\"torch_cuda\"])\n",
    "    return report\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def hardware_report(paths_to_check: list[Path]) -> dict:\n",
    "    info: dict = {\"platform\": platform.platform(), \"machine\": platform.machine(), \"cpu_count\": os.cpu_count()}\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import psutil  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "        vm = psutil.virtual_memory()\n",
    "        info[\"ram_total_gb\"] = vm.total / 1e9\n",
    "        info[\"ram_available_gb\"] = vm.available / 1e9\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        info[\"ram_total_gb\"] = float(\"nan\")\n",
    "    disks = {}\n",
    "    for p in paths_to_check:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            p.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "            usage = shutil.disk_usage(p)\n",
    "            disks[str(p)] = {\"total_gb\": usage.total / 1e9, \"free_gb\": usage.free / 1e9}\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:\n",
    "            disks[str(p)] = {\"error\": str(exc)}\n",
    "    info[\"disks\"] = disks\n",
    "    return info\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def disk_free_bytes(path: Path) -> int:\n",
    "    path = Path(path)\n",
    "    probe = path if path.exists() else next((p for p in path.parents if p.exists()), Path(\"/\"))\n",
    "    return int(shutil.disk_usage(probe).free)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def set_seeds(seed: int) -> None:\n",
    "    os.environ[\"PYTHONHASHSEED\"] = str(seed)\n",
    "    random.seed(seed)\n",
    "    np.random.seed(seed)\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import torch  # type: ignore\n",
    "\n",
    "        torch.manual_seed(seed)\n",
    "        if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "            torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(seed)\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def resolve_n_jobs(n_jobs: int) -> int:\n",
    "    cpus = os.cpu_count() or 1\n",
    "    if n_jobs is None or n_jobs == 0:\n",
    "        return 1\n",
    "    if n_jobs < 0:\n",
    "        return max(1, cpus + 1 + n_jobs)\n",
    "    return min(int(n_jobs), cpus)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def mount_drive(cfg: dict, logger) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Mount Google Drive in Colab when configured and authorised.\"\"\"\n",
    "    mount_point = cfg.get(\"drive_mount_point\", \"/content/drive\")\n",
    "    if Path(mount_point, \"MyDrive\").exists():\n",
    "        return {\"mounted\": True, \"mount_point\": mount_point, \"note\": \"already mounted\"}\n",
    "    if not cfg.get(\"mount_drive\", True):\n",
    "        return {\"mounted\": False, \"note\": \"mount_drive disabled\"}\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        from google.colab import drive  # type: ignore\n",
    "    except Exception as exc:\n",
    "        return {\"mounted\": False, \"error\": f\"google.colab unavailable: {exc}\"}\n",
    "    logger.info(\"Mounting Google Drive at %s (interactive authorisation)\", mount_point)\n",
    "    drive.mount(mount_point)\n",
    "    return {\"mounted\": Path(mount_point, \"MyDrive\").exists(), \"mount_point\": mount_point}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def check_environment_authorisation(cfg: dict, detected: str) -> None:\n",
    "    configured = str(cfg.get(\"environment\", \"\")).upper()\n",
    "    cloud = configured in {\"COLAB\", \"PRIVATE_CLOUD\"} or detected == \"COLAB\"\n",
    "    if cloud and not cfg.get(\"cloud_storage_authorized\", False):\n",
    "        raise PermissionError(\n",
    "            \"Cloud storage/processing is disabled. Confirm that your environment complies with the \"\n",
    "            \"competition data-use agreement, then set CONFIG['cloud_storage_authorized'] = True.\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    if configured == \"COLAB\" and detected != \"COLAB\":\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(\"CONFIG['environment'] is COLAB but the runtime is not Google Colab\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_environment(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    logger = ctx.logger\n",
    "    detected = detect_environment()\n",
    "    check_environment_authorisation(cfg, detected)\n",
    "    py = check_python()\n",
    "    if not py[\"ok\"]:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(f\"Python >= {py['minimum']} required, found {py['python_version']}\")\n",
    "    mount = {\"mounted\": False, \"note\": \"not Colab\"}\n",
    "    if detected == \"COLAB\":\n",
    "        mount = mount_drive(cfg, logger)\n",
    "    set_seeds(int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "    discovery = discover_data_root(cfg, cfg[\"environment\"] if detected != \"COLAB\" else \"COLAB\")\n",
    "    if discovery[\"chosen\"] is None:\n",
    "        ctx.save_json(discovery, \"data_discovery_report\")\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(discovery[\"message\"])\n",
    "    data_root = Path(discovery[\"chosen\"])\n",
    "    ctx.set_data_root(data_root)\n",
    "    file_info = []\n",
    "    for name in cfg[\"required_files\"]:\n",
    "        p = data_root / name\n",
    "        st = p.stat()\n",
    "        file_info.append({\"file\": name, \"size_bytes\": int(st.st_size), \"mtime_ns\": int(st.st_mtime_ns)})\n",
    "    hw = hardware_report([ctx.paths.root, ctx.paths.local_root])\n",
    "    gpu = gpu_report(bool(cfg.get(\"use_gpu\")))\n",
    "    versions = {\"core\": package_versions(CORE_PACKAGES), \"optional\": package_versions(OPTIONAL_PACKAGES)}\n",
    "    missing_core = [k for k, v in versions[\"core\"].items() if not v[\"available\"]]\n",
    "    report = {\n",
    "        \"detected_environment\": detected,\n",
    "        \"configured_environment\": cfg[\"environment\"],\n",
    "        \"python\": py,\n",
    "        \"drive\": mount,\n",
    "        \"data_discovery\": discovery,\n",
    "        \"data_root\": str(data_root),\n",
    "        \"required_files\": file_info,\n",
    "        \"hardware\": hw,\n",
    "        \"gpu\": gpu,\n",
    "        \"packages\": versions,\n",
    "        \"missing_core_packages\": missing_core,\n",
    "        \"n_jobs_effective\": resolve_n_jobs(int(cfg.get(\"n_jobs\", -1))),\n",
    "        \"seed\": int(cfg[\"seed\"]),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    ctx.save_json(report, \"environment_report\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.DataFrame(file_info), \"required_file_inventory\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    source = {\"data_root\": str(data_root), \"note\": \"Original files are read in place and never modified.\"}\n",
    "    from .io_utils import atomic_write_json\n",
    "\n",
    "    atomic_write_json(ctx.paths.data_raw / \"SOURCE.json\", source)\n",
    "    if missing_core:\n",
    "        logger.warning(\"Missing core packages: %s - dependent stages will fail clearly.\", missing_core)\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"outputs\": [\"environment_report\", \"required_file_inventory\"],\n",
    "        \"summary\": {\"environment\": detected, \"data_root\": str(data_root), \"missing_core\": missing_core,\n",
    "                    \"gpu\": gpu[\"will_use_gpu\"]},\n",
    "        \"fingerprint_extra\": file_info,\n",
    "    }\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-015",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/failure_atlas.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 22 - failure phenotype atlas.\n",
    "\n",
    "Scientific question: which student profiles are systematically difficult to\n",
    "predict, and why? Outcome-based failure categories describe prediction\n",
    "errors; they are not diagnoses.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "\n",
    "PHENOTYPES = [\"F01_UNEXPECTED_HIGH_OUTCOME\", \"F02_UNEXPECTED_LOW_OUTCOME\", \"F03_SKILL_IMBALANCE\", \"F04_RESPONSE_INCONSISTENCY\",\n",
    "              \"F05_SPARSE_OBSERVATIONS\", \"F06_RECORDING_QUALITY\", \"F07_SCHOOL_DOMAIN_SHIFT\", \"F08_EXTREME_TARGET\",\n",
    "              \"F09_COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\", \"F10_PHONETIC_DIFFICULTY\", \"F11_MODEL_DISAGREEMENT\", \"F12_MISSING_MODALITIES\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _multimodal_oof(ctx) -> tuple[pd.Series | None, str]:\n",
    "    if ctx.stage_available(\"21\"):\n",
    "        r = ctx.load_df(\"residual_learning_oof\", required=False)\n",
    "        if r is not None and len(r):\n",
    "            g = r[(r[\"approach\"] == \"TWO_STAGE_RESIDUAL\") & (r[\"scheme\"] == \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\")]\n",
    "            if len(g):\n",
    "                return g.groupby(\"student_id\")[\"pred\"].mean(), \"TWO_STAGE_RESIDUAL\"\n",
    "    if ctx.stage_available(\"20\"):\n",
    "        o = ctx.load_df(\"ablation_oof_predictions\", required=False)\n",
    "        if o is not None and len(o):\n",
    "            for exp in (\"A22_ALL_VALIDATED_FEATURES\", \"A13_TABULAR_MULTIMODAL\", \"A05_COMPLETE_TABULAR\"):\n",
    "                g = o[(o[\"experiment\"] == exp) & (o[\"scheme\"] == \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\") & (o[\"model\"] == ctx.config[\"ablation_primary_model\"])]\n",
    "                if len(g):\n",
    "                    return g.groupby(\"student_id\")[\"pred\"].mean(), exp\n",
    "    return None, \"UNAVAILABLE\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_failure_atlas(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    from sklearn.mixture import GaussianMixture\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    base = ctx.load_df(\"baseline_residuals\").set_index(\"student_id\")\n",
    "    multi, multi_name = _multimodal_oof(ctx)\n",
    "    S = da.student_features(ctx, \"train\") if ctx.stage_available(\"13\") else pd.DataFrame(index=base.index)\n",
    "    meta = da.student_meta(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    D = base[[\"y\", \"oof_prediction\"]].rename(columns={\"y\": \"observed_outcome\", \"oof_prediction\": \"baseline_prediction\"})\n",
    "    D[\"multimodal_prediction\"] = multi.reindex(D.index) if multi is not None else np.nan\n",
    "    D[\"baseline_error\"] = D[\"baseline_prediction\"] - D[\"observed_outcome\"]\n",
    "    D[\"multimodal_error\"] = D[\"multimodal_prediction\"] - D[\"observed_outcome\"]\n",
    "    D[\"error_reduction\"] = D[\"baseline_error\"].abs() - D[\"multimodal_error\"].abs()\n",
    "    oof_all = ctx.load_df(\"baseline_oof_predictions\")\n",
    "    prim = oof_all[(oof_all[\"model_id\"] == cfg[\"primary_baseline\"]) & (oof_all[\"scheme\"] == cfg[\"primary_cv_scheme\"])]\n",
    "    persist = prim.assign(abs_err=(prim[\"pred\"] - prim[\"y\"]).abs())\n",
    "    thr = persist[\"abs_err\"].quantile(0.8)\n",
    "    D[\"error_persistence\"] = persist.groupby(\"student_id\")[\"abs_err\"].apply(lambda s: float((s >= thr).mean())).reindex(D.index)\n",
    "    preds = prim.pivot_table(index=\"student_id\", columns=\"repeat\", values=\"pred\")\n",
    "    models = oof_all[oof_all[\"scheme\"] == cfg[\"primary_cv_scheme\"]].groupby([\"student_id\", \"model_id\"])[\"pred\"].mean().unstack()\n",
    "    D[\"model_disagreement\"] = models.drop(columns=[\"M00_MEAN\"], errors=\"ignore\").std(axis=1).reindex(D.index)\n",
    "    D[\"repeat_prediction_sd\"] = preds.std(axis=1).reindex(D.index)\n",
    "    J = D.join(S, how=\"left\").join(meta, rsuffix=\"_meta\")\n",
    "    err = D[\"baseline_error\"]\n",
    "    q_hi, q_lo = err.quantile(0.9), err.quantile(0.1)\n",
    "    flags = pd.DataFrame(index=D.index)\n",
    "    flags[\"F01_UNEXPECTED_HIGH_OUTCOME\"] = err <= q_lo\n",
    "    flags[\"F02_UNEXPECTED_LOW_OUTCOME\"] = err >= q_hi\n",
    "    flags[\"F03_SKILL_IMBALANCE\"] = J.get(\"theta_skill_imbalance\", pd.Series(np.nan, index=D.index)) >= J.get(\"theta_skill_imbalance\", pd.Series(np.nan, index=D.index)).quantile(0.9)\n",
    "    inc = J[[c for c in J.columns if c.startswith(\"ia_item_adjusted_acoustic_variability\")]].mean(axis=1) if any(c.startswith(\"ia_item_adjusted_acoustic_variability\") for c in J.columns) else pd.Series(np.nan, index=D.index)\n",
    "    flags[\"F04_RESPONSE_INCONSISTENCY\"] = inc >= inc.quantile(0.9)\n",
    "    flags[\"F05_SPARSE_OBSERVATIONS\"] = J.get(\"meta_n_clips\", pd.Series(np.nan, index=D.index)) <= J.get(\"meta_n_clips\", pd.Series(np.nan, index=D.index)).quantile(0.1)\n",
    "    flags[\"F06_RECORDING_QUALITY\"] = J.get(\"meta_frac_quality_flagged\", pd.Series(np.nan, index=D.index)) >= 0.5\n",
    "    if \"school_id\" in J.columns and J[\"school_id\"].notna().any():\n",
    "        school_err = D[\"baseline_error\"].abs().groupby(J[\"school_id\"]).mean()\n",
    "        flags[\"F07_SCHOOL_DOMAIN_SHIFT\"] = J[\"school_id\"].map(school_err) >= school_err.quantile(0.9)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        flags[\"F07_SCHOOL_DOMAIN_SHIFT\"] = False\n",
    "    flags[\"F08_EXTREME_TARGET\"] = (D[\"observed_outcome\"] <= D[\"observed_outcome\"].quantile(0.05)) | (D[\"observed_outcome\"] >= D[\"observed_outcome\"].quantile(0.95))\n",
    "    cx = J[[c for c in J.columns if c.startswith(\"cx_t_active_dur__vs_\") and c.endswith(\"__all\")]]\n",
    "    flags[\"F09_COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\"] = (cx.iloc[:, 0] >= cx.iloc[:, 0].quantile(0.9)) if cx.shape[1] else False\n",
    "    ph = J[[c for c in J.columns if c.startswith(\"ph_\") and c.endswith(\"_phone_er__mean\")]]\n",
    "    flags[\"F10_PHONETIC_DIFFICULTY\"] = (ph.iloc[:, 0] >= ph.iloc[:, 0].quantile(0.9)) if ph.shape[1] else False\n",
    "    flags[\"F11_MODEL_DISAGREEMENT\"] = D[\"model_disagreement\"] >= D[\"model_disagreement\"].quantile(0.9)\n",
    "    miss_cols = [c for c in J.columns if c.startswith(\"meta_missing_\")]\n",
    "    flags[\"F12_MISSING_MODALITIES\"] = J[miss_cols].sum(axis=1) >= 2 if miss_cols else False\n",
    "    flags = flags.fillna(False).astype(bool)\n",
    "    hard = D[\"baseline_error\"].abs() >= D[\"baseline_error\"].abs().quantile(0.8)\n",
    "    feats = [\"baseline_error\", \"error_persistence\", \"model_disagreement\"] + [c for c in (\"theta_mean\", \"theta_skill_imbalance\", \"acc_all\",\n",
    "                                                                                     \"meta_n_clips\", \"q_snr_db_approx__mean\", \"t_active_dur__mean\") if c in J.columns]\n",
    "    X = J.loc[hard, feats].apply(lambda s: (s - s.mean()) / s.std() if s.std() > 0 else s * 0).fillna(0)\n",
    "    D[\"failure_cluster\"] = \"NOT_HARD\"\n",
    "    cluster_info = {}\n",
    "    if len(X) >= 30:\n",
    "        best, best_bic = None, np.inf\n",
    "        for k in range(2, min(6, len(X) // 10) + 1):\n",
    "            g = GaussianMixture(k, random_state=int(cfg[\"seed\"]), n_init=3).fit(X)\n",
    "            if g.bic(X) < best_bic:\n",
    "                best, best_bic = g, g.bic(X)\n",
    "        if best is not None:\n",
    "            D.loc[X.index, \"failure_cluster\"] = [f\"FC{l}\" for l in best.predict(X)]\n",
    "            cluster_info = {\"k\": int(best.n_components), \"bic\": float(best_bic), \"features\": feats}\n",
    "    def mech(row):\n",
    "        f = [p for p in PHENOTYPES if flags.loc[row.name, p]]\n",
    "        return \";\".join(f) if f else \"NO_PREDEFINED_PATTERN\"\n",
    "    D[\"candidate_mechanism\"] = D.apply(mech, axis=1)\n",
    "    D[\"available_evidence\"] = D.apply(lambda r: \";\".join(c for c in (\"baseline\", \"multimodal\" if np.isfinite(r[\"multimodal_prediction\"]) else None,\n",
    "                                                                   \"audio\" if \"t_active_dur__mean\" in J.columns and np.isfinite(J.loc[r.name].get(\"t_active_dur__mean\", np.nan)) else None,\n",
    "                                                                   \"phonetic\" if ph.shape[1] and np.isfinite(ph.iloc[:, 0].get(r.name, np.nan)) else None) if c), axis=1)\n",
    "    reg = D.reset_index().rename(columns={\"index\": \"student_id\"})\n",
    "    reg.insert(0, \"failure_id\", [f\"FAIL_{i:05d}\" for i in range(len(reg))])\n",
    "    cols = [\"failure_id\", \"student_id\", \"baseline_prediction\", \"multimodal_prediction\", \"observed_outcome\", \"baseline_error\",\n",
    "            \"multimodal_error\", \"error_reduction\", \"failure_cluster\", \"candidate_mechanism\", \"available_evidence\",\n",
    "            \"error_persistence\", \"model_disagreement\", \"repeat_prediction_sd\"]\n",
    "    reg = reg[cols]\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(reg, \"failure_registry\")\n",
    "    summary = []\n",
    "    for p in PHENOTYPES:\n",
    "        m = flags[p]\n",
    "        summary.append({\"phenotype\": p, \"n\": int(m.sum()), \"mean_abs_baseline_error\": float(D.loc[m, \"baseline_error\"].abs().mean()) if m.any() else np.nan,\n",
    "                        \"mean_error_reduction\": float(D.loc[m, \"error_reduction\"].mean()) if m.any() else np.nan,\n",
    "                        \"overall_mean_abs_baseline_error\": float(D[\"baseline_error\"].abs().mean())})\n",
    "    summary = pd.DataFrame(summary)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(summary, \"failure_summary\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    overlap = flags.T.astype(int) @ flags.astype(int)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(overlap.reset_index().rename(columns={\"index\": \"phenotype\"}), \"failure_overlap\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    ctx.save_json({\"multimodal_source\": multi_name, \"clusters\": cluster_info,\n",
    "                   \"note\": \"Outcome-based failure categories are descriptive, not diagnoses.\"}, \"failure_info\")\n",
    "    _failure_figures(ctx, D, summary, X, flags)\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": [\"failure_registry\", \"failure_summary\", \"failure_overlap\", \"failure_info\"],\n",
    "            \"summary\": {\"multimodal_source\": multi_name, \"n_hard\": int(hard.sum()),\n",
    "                        \"mean_error_reduction\": float(D[\"error_reduction\"].mean()) if D[\"error_reduction\"].notna().any() else None}}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _failure_figures(ctx, D, summary, X, flags) -> None:\n",
    "    n = int(len(D))\n",
    "    e = D[\"baseline_error\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 3, (5, 4))\n",
    "    share = (e ** 2).cumsum() / (e ** 2).sum()\n",
    "    axes[0, 0].plot(np.arange(1, len(e) + 1) / len(e), share.to_numpy())\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], \"Error concentration curve\", \"fraction of students (sorted by |error|)\", \"share of squared error\", n)\n",
    "    if D[\"multimodal_error\"].notna().any():\n",
    "        axes[0, 1].scatter(D[\"baseline_error\"].abs(), D[\"multimodal_error\"].abs(), s=6, alpha=0.5)\n",
    "        lim = float(np.nanmax(D[[\"baseline_error\", \"multimodal_error\"]].abs().to_numpy()))\n",
    "        axes[0, 1].plot([0, lim], [0, lim], \"--\", color=\"grey\")\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 1], \"Baseline vs multimodal |error|\", \"baseline |error|\", \"multimodal |error|\", n)\n",
    "    axes[0, 2].scatter(D[\"model_disagreement\"], D[\"baseline_error\"].abs(), s=6, alpha=0.5)\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 2], \"Model disagreement vs error\", \"SD across baseline models\", \"|baseline error|\", n)\n",
    "    ctx.figure(fig, \"failure_overview\", \"Failure atlas overview\", \"Which students are hard to predict?\", \"failure_registry\", n,\n",
    "               f\"Top 10% of students account for {share.iloc[max(0, int(0.1 * len(share)) - 1)]:.1%} of squared error.\")\n",
    "    if len(summary):\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (8, 5))\n",
    "        s = summary.set_index(\"phenotype\")[[\"mean_abs_baseline_error\", \"mean_error_reduction\"]]\n",
    "        s.plot(kind=\"barh\", ax=axes[0, 0])\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], \"Failure phenotypes: error and multimodal recovery\", \"outcome units\", \"\", n)\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"failure_recovery\", \"Model recovery by failure phenotype\", \"Which modalities recover baseline failures?\",\n",
    "                   \"failure_summary\", n, \"Positive error reduction means the multimodal model reduced |error|.\")\n",
    "        M = flags.groupby(D[\"failure_cluster\"]).mean().T\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (6, 6))\n",
    "        viz.heatmap(axes[0, 0], M, \"Phenotype prevalence by empirical failure cluster\", cmap=\"viridis\", vmin=0, vmax=1)\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"failure_heatmap\", \"Error heatmap by failure cluster\", \"Do empirical failure clusters match predefined phenotypes?\",\n",
    "                   \"failure_registry\", n, \"Empirical clusters fitted on hard-to-predict students (top 20% |error|).\")\n",
    "    if len(X) >= 10:\n",
    "        _, _, vt = np.linalg.svd(X.to_numpy() - X.to_numpy().mean(0), full_matrices=False)\n",
    "        P = (X.to_numpy() - X.to_numpy().mean(0)) @ vt[:2].T\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1)\n",
    "        labs = D.loc[X.index, \"failure_cluster\"].astype(\"category\")\n",
    "        axes[0, 0].scatter(P[:, 0], P[:, 1], c=labs.cat.codes, cmap=\"tab10\", s=8)\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], \"Failure embedding map (PCA of hard students)\", \"PC1\", \"PC2\", len(X))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"failure_embedding\", \"Failure embedding map\", \"How do hard-to-predict students group?\", \"failure_registry\",\n",
    "                   len(X), \"Colours: empirical failure clusters.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-016",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/families.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Feature naming conventions and feature-family assignment.\n",
    "\n",
    "Clip-level prefixes: q_ quality, t_ temporal, s_full_/s_sp_ spectral,\n",
    "s_bg_ background spectral, m_ MFCC/cepstral, w_ wavelet, p_ prosody,\n",
    "l_ linguistic item complexity, ph_ phonetic/ASR, e_ embeddings.\n",
    "\n",
    "Student-level prefixes: theta_ screening, acc_ correctness, irt_ item\n",
    "difficulty (fold-fitted for prediction), traj_ adaptive behaviour,\n",
    "meta_ recording metadata/missingness, ia_ item-adjusted audio (fold-fitted),\n",
    "cx_ complexity sensitivity, cc_ correctness contrasts, xt_ cross-task,\n",
    "idx_ literacy indices, clu_ cluster features. Aggregated clip features keep\n",
    "their clip prefix: ``<clip_feature>__<condition>__<stat>``.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "FAMILY_RULES = [\n",
    "    (\"SCREENING\", r\"^theta_\"),\n",
    "    (\"CORRECTNESS\", r\"^acc_\"),\n",
    "    (\"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\", r\"^irt_\"),\n",
    "    (\"ADAPTIVE\", r\"^traj_\"),\n",
    "    (\"RECORDING_METADATA\", r\"^meta_\"),\n",
    "    (\"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\", r\"^ia_\"),\n",
    "    (\"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\", r\"^cx_\"),\n",
    "    (\"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\", r\"^cc_\"),\n",
    "    (\"CROSS_TASK\", r\"^xt_\"),\n",
    "    (\"LITERACY_INDICES\", r\"^idx_\"),\n",
    "    (\"CLUSTER\", r\"^clu_\"),\n",
    "    (\"QUALITY\", r\"^q_\"),\n",
    "    (\"BACKGROUND\", r\"^s_bg_\"),\n",
    "    (\"TEMPORAL\", r\"^t_\"),\n",
    "    (\"MFCC\", r\"^m_\"),\n",
    "    (\"SPECTRAL\", r\"^s_\"),\n",
    "    (\"WAVELETS\", r\"^w_\"),\n",
    "    (\"PROSODY\", r\"^p_\"),\n",
    "    (\"LINGUISTIC\", r\"^l_\"),\n",
    "    (\"PHONETIC\", r\"^ph_\"),\n",
    "    (\"EMBEDDINGS\", r\"^e_\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "_COMPILED = [(fam, re.compile(rx)) for fam, rx in FAMILY_RULES]\n",
    "\n",
    "ID_COLUMNS = {\"student_id\", \"clip_id\", \"school_id\", \"instrument\", \"split\", \"target\", \"item_key\", \"task\",\n",
    "              \"task_family\", \"item_id\", \"expected_text\", \"correct\", \"order\", \"audio_member\", \"audio_archive\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "TABULAR_FAMILIES = [\"SCREENING\", \"CORRECTNESS\", \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\", \"ADAPTIVE\", \"LINGUISTIC\"]\n",
    "AUDIO_FAMILIES = [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\", \"WAVELETS\", \"PROSODY\", \"PHONETIC\", \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\",\n",
    "                  \"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\", \"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\", \"CROSS_TASK\", \"EMBEDDINGS\"]\n",
    "TECHNICAL_FAMILIES = [\"QUALITY\", \"BACKGROUND\", \"RECORDING_METADATA\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Families that must be computed inside training folds before predictive use.\n",
    "FOLD_FITTED_FAMILIES = {\"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\", \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\", \"LITERACY_INDICES\", \"CLUSTER\"}\n",
    "FOLD_FITTED_COLUMNS = {\"theta_common_factor\"}\n",
    "# Conditional aggregates that rely on all-training item statistics (EDA only).\n",
    "EDA_ONLY_PATTERNS = [re.compile(r\"__diff=\")]\n",
    "\n",
    "VOICE_PRIOR_PATTERNS = [re.compile(p) for p in (\n",
    "    r\"^p_f0\", r\"^p_f[123]_\", r\"^p_f2_f1\", r\"^p_jitter\", r\"^p_shimmer\", r\"^p_hnr\", r\"^p_voiced\",\n",
    ")]\n",
    "\n",
    "COMPUTATION_COST = {\n",
    "    \"SCREENING\": \"LOW\", \"CORRECTNESS\": \"LOW\", \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\": \"MEDIUM\", \"ADAPTIVE\": \"LOW\",\n",
    "    \"RECORDING_METADATA\": \"LOW\", \"QUALITY\": \"LOW\", \"BACKGROUND\": \"MEDIUM\", \"TEMPORAL\": \"LOW\",\n",
    "    \"SPECTRAL\": \"MEDIUM\", \"MFCC\": \"MEDIUM\", \"WAVELETS\": \"HIGH\", \"PROSODY\": \"HIGH\",\n",
    "    \"LINGUISTIC\": \"LOW\", \"PHONETIC\": \"VERY_HIGH\", \"EMBEDDINGS\": \"VERY_HIGH\",\n",
    "    \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\": \"MEDIUM\", \"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\": \"MEDIUM\", \"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\": \"LOW\",\n",
    "    \"CROSS_TASK\": \"LOW\", \"LITERACY_INDICES\": \"MEDIUM\", \"CLUSTER\": \"MEDIUM\", \"OTHER\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "INTERPRETABILITY = {\n",
    "    \"SCREENING\": \"HIGH\", \"CORRECTNESS\": \"HIGH\", \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\": \"HIGH\", \"ADAPTIVE\": \"HIGH\",\n",
    "    \"RECORDING_METADATA\": \"HIGH\", \"QUALITY\": \"HIGH\", \"BACKGROUND\": \"MEDIUM\", \"TEMPORAL\": \"HIGH\",\n",
    "    \"SPECTRAL\": \"MEDIUM\", \"MFCC\": \"LOW\", \"WAVELETS\": \"LOW\", \"PROSODY\": \"MEDIUM\", \"LINGUISTIC\": \"HIGH\",\n",
    "    \"PHONETIC\": \"HIGH\", \"EMBEDDINGS\": \"LOW\", \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\": \"MEDIUM\",\n",
    "    \"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\": \"HIGH\", \"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\": \"HIGH\", \"CROSS_TASK\": \"MEDIUM\",\n",
    "    \"LITERACY_INDICES\": \"HIGH\", \"CLUSTER\": \"MEDIUM\", \"OTHER\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "FAMILY_HYPOTHESIS = {\n",
    "    \"SCREENING\": \"Initial literacy ability predicts end-of-year reading.\",\n",
    "    \"CORRECTNESS\": \"Item-level accuracy adds detail beyond summary ability estimates.\",\n",
    "    \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\": \"Difficulty-aware performance captures information beyond raw accuracy (H03, H18).\",\n",
    "    \"ADAPTIVE\": \"Response trajectories carry complementary information (H18).\",\n",
    "    \"TEMPORAL\": \"Response organisation and fluency predict later reading (H01, H14).\",\n",
    "    \"SPECTRAL\": \"Frequency-domain articulation properties carry literacy signal (H01).\",\n",
    "    \"MFCC\": \"Cepstral dynamics reflect articulation precision (H01, H04).\",\n",
    "    \"WAVELETS\": \"Multiscale transients add signal beyond spectral features (H08).\",\n",
    "    \"PROSODY\": \"Prosodic organisation is informative after anonymisation (H01).\",\n",
    "    \"LINGUISTIC\": \"Complexity of attempted items reflects adaptive progression (H03).\",\n",
    "    \"PHONETIC\": \"Expected-versus-recognised speech deviations are informative (H02, H06).\",\n",
    "    \"EMBEDDINGS\": \"Pretrained representations capture complementary information (H09).\",\n",
    "    \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\": \"Item-conditioned acoustics beat unadjusted acoustics (H16).\",\n",
    "    \"COMPLEXITY_SENSITIVITY\": \"Sensitivity to item complexity predicts outcomes (H03).\",\n",
    "    \"CORRECTNESS_CONTRAST\": \"Correct responses carry heterogeneous information (H02).\",\n",
    "    \"CROSS_TASK\": \"Tasks provide complementary information (H05).\",\n",
    "    \"QUALITY\": \"Negative control: technical quality should not predict literacy (H12).\",\n",
    "    \"BACKGROUND\": \"Negative control: background regions should not predict literacy (H12).\",\n",
    "    \"RECORDING_METADATA\": \"Negative control: recording metadata should not predict literacy (H12).\",\n",
    "    \"LITERACY_INDICES\": \"Composite indices improve interpretability or prediction (H17).\",\n",
    "    \"CLUSTER\": \"Distinct profiles exist among similar screening scores (H07).\",\n",
    "    \"OTHER\": \"Unclassified feature.\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def feature_family(column: str) -> str:\n",
    "    for fam, rx in _COMPILED:\n",
    "        if rx.search(column):\n",
    "            return fam\n",
    "    return \"OTHER\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def feature_subfamily(column: str) -> str:\n",
    "    base = column.split(\"__\", 1)[0]\n",
    "    parts = base.split(\"_\")\n",
    "    if base.startswith((\"s_\", \"m_\")) and len(parts) > 2:\n",
    "        return \"_\".join(parts[1:3])\n",
    "    return parts[1] if len(parts) > 1 else base\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def is_feature_column(column: str) -> bool:\n",
    "    return column not in ID_COLUMNS and feature_family(column) != \"OTHER\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def columns_by_family(columns) -> dict:\n",
    "    out: dict = {}\n",
    "    for c in columns:\n",
    "        if c in ID_COLUMNS:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        out.setdefault(feature_family(c), []).append(c)\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def select_family_columns(columns, families, exclude_eda_only: bool = True) -> list:\n",
    "    families = set(families)\n",
    "    out = []\n",
    "    for c in columns:\n",
    "        if c in ID_COLUMNS:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        if feature_family(c) not in families:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        if exclude_eda_only and any(p.search(c) for p in EDA_ONLY_PATTERNS):\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        out.append(c)\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def modeling_columns(columns, families) -> list:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Columns usable directly for prediction (fold-fitted ones are rebuilt in folds).\"\"\"\n",
    "    return [c for c in select_family_columns(columns, families)\n",
    "            if feature_family(c) not in FOLD_FITTED_FAMILIES and c not in FOLD_FITTED_COLUMNS]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def is_voice_prior(column: str) -> bool:\n",
    "    base = column.split(\"__\", 1)[0]\n",
    "    return any(p.search(base) for p in VOICE_PRIOR_PATTERNS)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def sanitize_token(value) -> str:\n",
    "    return re.sub(r\"[^0-9a-zA-Z]+\", \"_\", str(value)).strip(\"_\").lower() or \"na\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-017",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/family_analysis.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Shared analysis engine for acoustic feature families (Sections 07-10).\n",
    "\n",
    "For every feature of a family it reports distributions, clip-level\n",
    "associations with correctness (within item), item and student ICCs,\n",
    "relationships with expected-text complexity and item difficulty, and\n",
    "student-level associations with the target and (when available) the\n",
    "out-of-fold screening residual, including partial correlations controlling for\n",
    "screening ability and recording quality, and item-adjusted variants.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "from .stats_utils import bh_fdr, bootstrap_ci, hedges_g, icc1, partial_corr, safe_corr\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _family_features(clips: pd.DataFrame, prefixes: tuple) -> list:\n",
    "    feats = []\n",
    "    for c in clips.columns:\n",
    "        if not c.startswith(prefixes) or not pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(clips[c]):\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        s = clips[c]\n",
    "        if s.notna().mean() < 0.05 or s.nunique(dropna=True) < 3:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        feats.append(c)\n",
    "    return feats\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _complexity_column(clips: pd.DataFrame) -> str | None:\n",
    "    for c in (\"l_n_phonemes\", \"l_n_chars\", \"l_n_words\"):\n",
    "        if c in clips.columns and clips[c].notna().mean() > 0.5:\n",
    "            return c\n",
    "    return None\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _student_context(ctx) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    y = da.target(ctx).rename(\"target\")\n",
    "    out = y.to_frame()\n",
    "    scr = da.screening(ctx)\n",
    "    if scr is not None:\n",
    "        for c in [\"theta_mean\"] + da.raw_theta_columns(scr):\n",
    "            if c in scr.columns:\n",
    "                out[c] = scr[c]\n",
    "    res = da.residuals(ctx)\n",
    "    if res is not None:\n",
    "        out[\"residual\"] = res\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def analyze_family(ctx, family: str, prefixes: tuple, split_by_correctness: bool = False,\n",
    "                   control_quality: bool = False) -> dict:\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    min_n = int(cfg[\"min_n_correlation\"])\n",
    "    clips = da.clip_table(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    feats = _family_features(clips, prefixes)\n",
    "    tag = family.lower()\n",
    "    if not feats:\n",
    "        ctx.save_json({\"status\": \"NO_FEATURES\", \"family\": family}, f\"{tag}_family_status\")\n",
    "        return {\"outputs\": [f\"{tag}_family_status\"], \"summary\": {\"status\": \"NO_FEATURES\"}}\n",
    "    has_correct = \"correct\" in clips.columns and clips[\"correct\"].notna().sum() >= min_n\n",
    "    has_item = \"item_key\" in clips.columns and clips[\"item_key\"].notna().any()\n",
    "    cplx = _complexity_column(clips)\n",
    "    stud_ctx = _student_context(ctx)\n",
    "    theta_cols = [c for c in stud_ctx.columns if c.startswith(\"theta_\") and c != \"theta_mean\"]\n",
    "    quality_cols = [c for c in (\"q_snr_db_approx\", \"q_duration_s\", \"q_noise_floor_db\") if c in clips.columns]\n",
    "    smeans = clips.groupby(\"student_id\")[feats + quality_cols].mean()\n",
    "    if has_item:\n",
    "        item_means = clips.groupby(\"item_key\")[feats].transform(\"mean\")\n",
    "        adj = clips[feats] - item_means\n",
    "        adj[\"student_id\"] = clips[\"student_id\"]\n",
    "        smeans_adj = adj.groupby(\"student_id\")[feats].mean()\n",
    "        if has_correct:\n",
    "            corr_dm = clips[\"correct\"] - clips.groupby(\"item_key\")[\"correct\"].transform(\"mean\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        smeans_adj = None\n",
    "    S = stud_ctx.join(smeans, how=\"inner\")\n",
    "    S_adj = stud_ctx.join(smeans_adj, how=\"inner\") if smeans_adj is not None else None\n",
    "    split_means = {}\n",
    "    if split_by_correctness and has_correct:\n",
    "        for label, val in ((\"correct\", 1.0), (\"incorrect\", 0.0)):\n",
    "            split_means[label] = stud_ctx.join(clips[clips[\"correct\"] == val].groupby(\"student_id\")[feats].mean(), how=\"inner\")\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for f in feats:\n",
    "        x = clips[f]\n",
    "        row = {\"feature\": f, \"family\": family, \"n_clips\": int(x.notna().sum()), \"missing_rate\": float(x.isna().mean()),\n",
    "               \"mean\": float(x.mean()), \"std\": float(x.std()), \"median\": float(x.median()),\n",
    "               \"p05\": float(x.quantile(0.05)), \"p95\": float(x.quantile(0.95)), \"skew\": float(x.skew())}\n",
    "        row[\"student_icc\"] = icc1(x, clips[\"student_id\"])\n",
    "        if has_item:\n",
    "            row[\"item_icc\"] = icc1(x, clips[\"item_key\"])\n",
    "            if has_correct:\n",
    "                xd = x - item_means[f]\n",
    "                row[\"within_item_correct_r\"], row[\"within_item_correct_p\"], _ = safe_corr(xd, corr_dm, \"pearson\", min_n)\n",
    "                row[\"within_item_correct_g\"] = hedges_g(xd[clips[\"correct\"] == 1], xd[clips[\"correct\"] == 0])\n",
    "        elif has_correct:\n",
    "            row[\"within_item_correct_r\"], row[\"within_item_correct_p\"], _ = safe_corr(x, clips[\"correct\"], \"pearson\", min_n)\n",
    "        if cplx:\n",
    "            row[f\"rho_{cplx}\"] = safe_corr(x, clips[cplx], \"spearman\", min_n)[0]\n",
    "        if \"item_b\" in clips.columns:\n",
    "            row[\"rho_item_difficulty\"] = safe_corr(x, clips[\"item_b\"], \"spearman\", min_n)[0]\n",
    "        for tf in sorted(clips[\"task_family\"].dropna().unique()):\n",
    "            m = clips[\"task_family\"] == tf\n",
    "            if has_correct and has_item and m.sum() >= min_n:\n",
    "                row[f\"within_item_correct_r__{tf}\"] = safe_corr((x - item_means[f])[m], corr_dm[m], \"pearson\", min_n)[0]\n",
    "        row[\"target_rho\"], row[\"target_p\"], row[\"n_students\"] = safe_corr(S[f], S[\"target\"], \"spearman\", min_n)\n",
    "        if theta_cols:\n",
    "            row[\"target_partial_r_theta\"], row[\"target_partial_p_theta\"], _ = partial_corr(S[f], S[\"target\"], S[theta_cols], \"spearman\", min_n)\n",
    "        if control_quality and quality_cols and theta_cols:\n",
    "            ctrl = [c for c in theta_cols] + [q for q in quality_cols if q != f]\n",
    "            row[\"target_partial_r_theta_quality\"], row[\"target_partial_p_theta_quality\"], _ = partial_corr(\n",
    "                S[f], S[\"target\"], S[ctrl], \"spearman\", min_n)\n",
    "        if \"theta_mean\" in S.columns:\n",
    "            row[\"theta_mean_rho\"] = safe_corr(S[f], S[\"theta_mean\"], \"spearman\", min_n)[0]\n",
    "        if \"residual\" in S.columns:\n",
    "            row[\"residual_rho\"], row[\"residual_p\"], _ = safe_corr(S[f], S[\"residual\"], \"spearman\", min_n)\n",
    "        if S_adj is not None:\n",
    "            row[\"item_adjusted_target_rho\"] = safe_corr(S_adj[f], S_adj[\"target\"], \"spearman\", min_n)[0]\n",
    "            if \"residual\" in S_adj.columns:\n",
    "                row[\"item_adjusted_residual_rho\"], row[\"item_adjusted_residual_p\"], _ = safe_corr(\n",
    "                    S_adj[f], S_adj[\"residual\"], \"spearman\", min_n)\n",
    "        for label, frame in split_means.items():\n",
    "            row[f\"target_rho_{label}_only\"] = safe_corr(frame[f], frame[\"target\"], \"spearman\", min_n)[0]\n",
    "        rows.append(row)\n",
    "    report = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    for pcol in [c for c in report.columns if c.endswith(\"_p\") or c.endswith(\"_p_theta\") or c.endswith(\"_p_theta_quality\")]:\n",
    "        report[pcol.replace(\"_p\", \"_q\", 1) if pcol.endswith(\"_p\") else pcol + \"_fdr\"] = bh_fdr(report[pcol])\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(report, f\"{tag}_family_report\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    _family_figures(ctx, family, report, clips, S, feats)\n",
    "    top = report.reindex(report[\"target_rho\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index).head(10)\n",
    "    summary = {\"n_features\": len(feats), \"top_target_features\": top[[\"feature\", \"target_rho\"]].to_dict(\"records\")}\n",
    "    if \"residual_rho\" in report.columns:\n",
    "        summary[\"n_residual_fdr_significant\"] = int((report.get(\"residual_q\", pd.Series(dtype=float)) < cfg[\"fdr_alpha\"]).sum())\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": [f\"{tag}_family_report\"], \"summary\": summary}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _family_figures(ctx, family: str, report: pd.DataFrame, clips: pd.DataFrame, S: pd.DataFrame, feats: list) -> None:\n",
    "    tag = family.lower()\n",
    "    k = 25\n",
    "    if \"within_item_correct_r\" in report.columns and report[\"within_item_correct_r\"].notna().any():\n",
    "        top = report.reindex(report[\"within_item_correct_r\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index).head(k)\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (8, 0.25 * len(top) + 2))\n",
    "        ax = axes[0, 0]\n",
    "        ax.barh(top[\"feature\"], top[\"within_item_correct_r\"])\n",
    "        ax.invert_yaxis()\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(ax, f\"{family}: within-item association with correctness\", \"Pearson r (item-demeaned)\", \"\", int(top[\"n_clips\"].max()))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, f\"{tag}_correctness_association\", f\"{family} features vs correctness (within item)\",\n",
    "                   \"Do acoustic properties differ between correct and incorrect responses to the same item?\",\n",
    "                   f\"{tag}_family_report\", int(report[\"n_clips\"].max()),\n",
    "                   f\"Largest |r|={top['within_item_correct_r'].abs().max():.3f} ({top.iloc[0]['feature']}).\")\n",
    "    top_t = report.reindex(report[\"target_rho\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index).head(k)\n",
    "    if top_t[\"target_rho\"].notna().any():\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (8, 0.25 * len(top_t) + 2))\n",
    "        ax = axes[0, 0]\n",
    "        ax.barh(top_t[\"feature\"], top_t[\"target_rho\"], label=\"raw\")\n",
    "        if \"residual_rho\" in top_t.columns:\n",
    "            ax.barh(top_t[\"feature\"], top_t[\"residual_rho\"], alpha=0.6, label=\"OOF screening residual\")\n",
    "        ax.legend(fontsize=7)\n",
    "        ax.invert_yaxis()\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(ax, f\"{family}: student-level association with outcome\", \"Spearman rho\", \"\", int(top_t[\"n_students\"].max()))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, f\"{tag}_target_association\", f\"{family} features vs end-of-year outcome\",\n",
    "                   \"Which features relate to the outcome and to the screening residual?\", f\"{tag}_family_report\",\n",
    "                   int(top_t[\"n_students\"].max()),\n",
    "                   f\"Top raw rho {top_t['target_rho'].abs().max():.3f}; residual associations shown when available.\")\n",
    "    show = top_t[\"feature\"].head(6).tolist()\n",
    "    if show:\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(2, 3, (4.5, 3.2))\n",
    "        for ax, f in zip(axes.ravel(), show):\n",
    "            viz.hist_kde(ax, clips[f], f)\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, f\"{tag}_distributions\", f\"{family}: clip-level distributions of top features\",\n",
    "                   \"What do the most outcome-related features look like?\", f\"{tag}_family_report\",\n",
    "                   int(len(clips)), \"Histograms with KDE; titles report missing values.\")\n",
    "    viz.top_correlation_heatmap(ctx, S, top_t[\"feature\"].tolist() + [\"target\"], f\"{tag}_top_correlations\",\n",
    "                                f\"{family}: redundancy among outcome-related features\",\n",
    "                                \"Are top features redundant?\", f\"{tag}_family_report\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def complexity_surface(ctx, feature: str, outputs: list) -> None:\n",
    "    from .student_aggregation import shrunk_slopes\n",
    "\n",
    "    clips = da.clip_table(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    cplx = _complexity_column(clips) or (\"item_b\" if \"item_b\" in clips.columns else None)\n",
    "    if cplx is None or feature not in clips.columns:\n",
    "        ctx.save_json({\"status\": \"UNAVAILABLE\", \"reason\": \"no expected-text complexity or difficulty\"}, \"complexity_surface_status\")\n",
    "        outputs.append(\"complexity_surface_status\")\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    scr = da.screening(ctx)\n",
    "    if scr is not None and \"theta_mean\" in scr.columns:\n",
    "        clips = clips.merge(scr[[\"theta_mean\"]], left_on=\"student_id\", right_index=True, how=\"left\")\n",
    "        surf = viz.binned_surface(clips, cplx, \"theta_mean\", feature, bins=6, min_count=int(ctx.config[\"min_group_size\"]))\n",
    "        if not surf.empty:\n",
    "            fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (7, 5))\n",
    "            viz.heatmap(axes[0, 0], surf, f\"mean {feature} by {cplx} (x) and screening theta_mean (y)\", cmap=\"viridis\",\n",
    "                        cbar_label=feature)\n",
    "            ctx.figure(fig, f\"surface_{feature}_{cplx}\", \"Complexity-duration response surface\",\n",
    "                       \"How does response duration depend on item complexity and initial ability?\", \"clip_table\",\n",
    "                       int(clips[[cplx, \"theta_mean\", feature]].dropna().shape[0]),\n",
    "                       f\"Cells with fewer than {ctx.config['min_group_size']} clips are masked.\")\n",
    "    slopes = shrunk_slopes(clips, \"student_id\", cplx, feature, k=float(ctx.config[\"slope_shrinkage_k\"]),\n",
    "                           min_obs=int(ctx.config[\"aggregation_min_obs\"]))\n",
    "    y = da.target(ctx)\n",
    "    slopes = slopes.join(y.rename(\"target\"), how=\"left\")\n",
    "    from .stats_utils import safe_corr\n",
    "\n",
    "    r, p, n = safe_corr(slopes[\"slope_shrunk\"], slopes[\"target\"], \"spearman\", int(ctx.config[\"min_n_correlation\"]))\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(slopes.reset_index(), \"complexity_sensitivity_estimates\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    outputs.append(\"complexity_sensitivity_estimates\")\n",
    "    fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 2)\n",
    "    viz.hist_kde(axes[0, 0], slopes[\"slope_shrunk\"], f\"shrunk slope of {feature} on {cplx}\")\n",
    "    viz.scatter_fit(axes[0, 1], slopes[\"slope_shrunk\"], slopes[\"target\"], \"complexity sensitivity\", \"target\",\n",
    "                    \"complexity sensitivity vs outcome\")\n",
    "    ctx.figure(fig, f\"complexity_sensitivity_{feature}\", \"Student-level complexity sensitivity\",\n",
    "               \"Does sensitivity to item complexity relate to later reading?\", \"complexity_sensitivity_estimates\", n,\n",
    "               f\"Empirical-Bayes shrunk slopes (k={ctx.config['slope_shrinkage_k']}); Spearman rho with target={r:.3f} (p={p:.3g}).\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def multiscale_comparisons(ctx, prefixes: tuple, outputs: list) -> None:\n",
    "    from scipy.stats import kruskal\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    clips = da.clip_table(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    feats = _family_features(clips, prefixes)\n",
    "    if not feats:\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    stud = _student_context(ctx)\n",
    "    means = stud.join(clips.groupby(\"student_id\")[feats].mean(), how=\"inner\")\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    has_correct = \"correct\" in clips.columns and clips[\"correct\"].notna().any() and \"item_key\" in clips.columns\n",
    "    for f in feats:\n",
    "        row = {\"feature\": f}\n",
    "        if has_correct:\n",
    "            xd = clips[f] - clips.groupby(\"item_key\")[f].transform(\"mean\")\n",
    "            row[\"correct_vs_incorrect_g_within_item\"] = hedges_g(xd[clips[\"correct\"] == 1], xd[clips[\"correct\"] == 0])\n",
    "        if \"item_key\" in clips.columns:\n",
    "            row[\"same_item_icc\"] = icc1(clips[f], clips[\"item_key\"])\n",
    "        if \"theta_mean\" in means.columns:\n",
    "            terc = pd.qcut(means[\"theta_mean\"], 3, labels=[\"low\", \"mid\", \"high\"], duplicates=\"drop\")\n",
    "            groups = [means.loc[terc == g, f].dropna() for g in terc.dropna().unique()]\n",
    "            groups = [g for g in groups if len(g) >= 5]\n",
    "            if len(groups) >= 2:\n",
    "                h, p = kruskal(*groups)\n",
    "                row[\"ability_tertile_kruskal_h\"], row[\"ability_tertile_p\"] = float(h), float(p)\n",
    "        row[\"outcome_rho\"] = safe_corr(means[f], means[\"target\"], \"spearman\", int(cfg[\"min_n_correlation\"]))[0]\n",
    "        if \"residual\" in means.columns and \"theta_mean\" in means.columns:\n",
    "            lo_q, hi_q = cfg[\"residual_group_quantiles\"]\n",
    "            lo, hi = means[\"residual\"].quantile(lo_q), means[\"residual\"].quantile(hi_q)\n",
    "            bins = pd.qcut(means[\"theta_mean\"], 5, duplicates=\"drop\")\n",
    "            diffs, weights = [], []\n",
    "            for _, g in means.groupby(bins, observed=True):\n",
    "                pos, neg = g.loc[g[\"residual\"] >= hi, f], g.loc[g[\"residual\"] <= lo, f]\n",
    "                gg = hedges_g(pos, neg)\n",
    "                if np.isfinite(gg):\n",
    "                    diffs.append(gg)\n",
    "                    weights.append(min(len(pos.dropna()), len(neg.dropna())))\n",
    "            row[\"similar_screening_pos_vs_neg_residual_g\"] = float(np.average(diffs, weights=weights)) if diffs else np.nan\n",
    "            sub = means[[\"residual\", f]].dropna()\n",
    "            ci = bootstrap_ci(lambda a, b_: safe_corr(a, b_, \"spearman\", 10)[0], sub[f].to_numpy(), sub[\"residual\"].to_numpy(),\n",
    "                              n_boot=min(int(cfg[\"bootstrap_iterations\"]), 300), seed=int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "            row[\"residual_rho_ci_lower\"], row[\"residual_rho_ci_upper\"] = ci[\"lower\"], ci[\"upper\"]\n",
    "        rows.append(row)\n",
    "    table = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(table, \"multiscale_comparisons\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    outputs.append(\"multiscale_comparisons\")\n",
    "    if \"correct_vs_incorrect_g_within_item\" in table.columns:\n",
    "        top = table.reindex(table[\"correct_vs_incorrect_g_within_item\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index).head(20)\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (8, 0.25 * len(top) + 2))\n",
    "        axes[0, 0].barh(top[\"feature\"], top[\"correct_vs_incorrect_g_within_item\"])\n",
    "        axes[0, 0].invert_yaxis()\n",
    "        viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], \"Wavelet features: correct vs incorrect (within item)\", \"Hedges g\", \"\", int(len(clips)))\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"wavelet_correct_vs_incorrect\", \"Multiscale differences between correct and incorrect responses\",\n",
    "                   \"Do multiscale transitions differ by correctness for the same item?\", \"multiscale_comparisons\",\n",
    "                   int(len(clips)), f\"Max |g|={top['correct_vs_incorrect_g_within_item'].abs().max():.3f}.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-018",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/feature_interactions.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 18 - feature interactions and conditional relevance.\n",
    "\n",
    "Only a predefined, research-driven candidate set of interactions is tested\n",
    "(no unrestricted all-pairs search). Representative variables are built inside\n",
    "each training fold (PC1 of a family, standardised on training students) and\n",
    "interaction gains are evaluated out of fold with paired bootstrap CIs.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "from .families import modeling_columns\n",
    "from .stats_utils import mutual_information, safe_corr\n",
    "from .validation import iter_folds, paired_bootstrap_delta, regression_metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "REPRESENTATIVES = {\n",
    "    \"SCREENING\": {\"columns\": [\"theta_mean\"]},\n",
    "    \"TEMPORAL\": {\"families\": [\"TEMPORAL\"]},\n",
    "    \"SPECTRAL\": {\"families\": [\"SPECTRAL\"]},\n",
    "    \"PHONETIC\": {\"families\": [\"PHONETIC\"]},\n",
    "    \"ACOUSTIC\": {\"families\": [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\"]},\n",
    "    \"FLUENCY\": {\"prefixes\": [\"t_pause_speech_ratio__\", \"t_n_pauses__\", \"t_internal_sil__\", \"t_rhythm_regularity__\"]},\n",
    "    \"DURATION\": {\"columns\": [\"t_active_dur__mean\", \"q_duration_s__mean\"]},\n",
    "    \"PHONETIC_CONFIDENCE\": {\"suffix\": \"seq_confidence__mean\"},\n",
    "    \"SPECTRAL_ENTROPY\": {\"columns\": [\"s_sp_entropy_mean__mean\"]},\n",
    "    \"CORRECTNESS\": {\"columns\": [\"acc_all\"]},\n",
    "    \"DIFFICULTY\": {\"columns\": [\"l_n_phonemes__mean\", \"l_n_chars__mean\", \"irt_all_theta\"]},\n",
    "    \"ACOUSTIC_CONSISTENCY\": {\"columns\": [\"ia_item_adjusted_acoustic_variability\", \"m_sp_cepstral_variability__std\"]},\n",
    "    \"COMPLEXITY\": {\"prefixes\": [\"cx_t_active_dur__\"]},\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def representative_columns(S: pd.DataFrame, name: str) -> list:\n",
    "    spec = REPRESENTATIVES[name]\n",
    "    if \"columns\" in spec:\n",
    "        cols = [c for c in spec[\"columns\"] if c in S.columns]\n",
    "        return cols[:1]\n",
    "    if \"families\" in spec:\n",
    "        return modeling_columns(S.columns, spec[\"families\"])\n",
    "    if \"prefixes\" in spec:\n",
    "        return [c for c in S.columns if c.startswith(tuple(spec[\"prefixes\"])) and not c.endswith((\"_reliable\", \"_n\"))]\n",
    "    if \"suffix\" in spec:\n",
    "        return [c for c in S.columns if c.endswith(spec[\"suffix\"])][:1]\n",
    "    return []\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fold_representative(S: pd.DataFrame, cols: list, train_ids) -> pd.Series:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Single column standardised on training rows, or PC1 of several columns fitted on training rows.\"\"\"\n",
    "    X = S[cols]\n",
    "    tr = X.loc[train_ids]\n",
    "    med = tr.median()\n",
    "    sd = tr.std().replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "    Z = ((X - med) / sd).loc[:, sd.notna()].fillna(0.0)\n",
    "    if Z.shape[1] == 0:\n",
    "        return pd.Series(np.nan, index=S.index)\n",
    "    if Z.shape[1] == 1:\n",
    "        return Z.iloc[:, 0]\n",
    "    Ztr = Z.loc[train_ids].to_numpy()\n",
    "    mu = Ztr.mean(0)\n",
    "    _, _, vt = np.linalg.svd(Ztr - mu, full_matrices=False)\n",
    "    pc = (Z.to_numpy() - mu) @ vt[0]\n",
    "    s = pd.Series(pc, index=S.index)\n",
    "    return (s - s.loc[train_ids].mean()) / (s.loc[train_ids].std() or 1.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _ridge(Xtr, ytr, Xva):\n",
    "    from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "    from sklearn.linear_model import RidgeCV\n",
    "    from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n",
    "    from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "    m = make_pipeline(SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\"), StandardScaler(), RidgeCV(alphas=np.logspace(-3, 4, 30)))\n",
    "    m.fit(Xtr, ytr)\n",
    "    return m.predict(Xva)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def h_statistic(model, X: pd.DataFrame, a: str, b: str, max_n: int, seed: int) -> float:\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "    pts = X.iloc[rng.choice(len(X), min(len(X), max_n // 3), replace=False)]\n",
    "    bg = X.iloc[rng.choice(len(X), min(len(X), 100), replace=False)]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def pd_val(vals: dict) -> float:\n",
    "        Xb = bg.copy()\n",
    "        for k, v in vals.items():\n",
    "            Xb[k] = v\n",
    "        return float(model.predict(Xb).mean())\n",
    "    fab, fa, fb = [], [], []\n",
    "    for _, r in pts.iterrows():\n",
    "        fab.append(pd_val({a: r[a], b: r[b]}))\n",
    "        fa.append(pd_val({a: r[a]}))\n",
    "        fb.append(pd_val({b: r[b]}))\n",
    "    fab, fa, fb = (np.asarray(v) - np.mean(v) for v in (fab, fa, fb))\n",
    "    denom = (fab ** 2).sum()\n",
    "    return float(np.sqrt(((fab - fa - fb) ** 2).sum() / denom)) if denom > 0 else np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_feature_interactions(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    from sklearn.ensemble import HistGradientBoostingRegressor\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    S = da.student_features(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    meta = da.student_meta(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    y = meta[\"target\"].dropna().astype(float)\n",
    "    S = S.reindex(y.index)\n",
    "    assign = ctx.load_df(\"cv_assignments\")\n",
    "    screening = [c for c in da.raw_theta_columns(S)]\n",
    "    rows, fold_rows, surfaces = [], [], []\n",
    "    for pair in cfg[\"interaction_candidates\"]:\n",
    "        a, b = pair\n",
    "        label = f\"{a} x {b}\"\n",
    "        if \"TASK\" in (a, b) or \"INSTRUMENT\" in (a, b):\n",
    "            rows.append(_special_interaction(ctx, S, y, meta, assign, a, b, screening))\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        ca, cb = representative_columns(S, a), representative_columns(S, b)\n",
    "        if not ca or not cb:\n",
    "            rows.append({\"interaction\": label, \"status\": \"UNAVAILABLE\", \"reason\": f\"no columns for {a if not ca else b}\"})\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        preds_main, preds_int, ids_all = [], [], []\n",
    "        for rep, fold, tr, va in iter_folds(assign, \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\", repeats=[0]):\n",
    "            tr = [t for t in tr if t in S.index]\n",
    "            va = [v for v in va if v in S.index]\n",
    "            ra, rb = fold_representative(S, ca, tr), fold_representative(S, cb, tr)\n",
    "            base = S[screening].copy()\n",
    "            base[\"rep_a\"], base[\"rep_b\"] = ra, rb\n",
    "            inter = base.copy()\n",
    "            inter[\"rep_axb\"] = ra * rb\n",
    "            pm = _ridge(base.loc[tr], y.loc[tr], base.loc[va])\n",
    "            pi = _ridge(inter.loc[tr], y.loc[tr], inter.loc[va])\n",
    "            preds_main.append(pd.Series(pm, index=va))\n",
    "            preds_int.append(pd.Series(pi, index=va))\n",
    "            fold_rows.append({\"interaction\": label, \"fold\": fold, \"delta_r2\": regression_metrics(y.loc[va], pi)[\"r2\"] - regression_metrics(y.loc[va], pm)[\"r2\"]})\n",
    "        pmain, pint = pd.concat(preds_main), pd.concat(preds_int)\n",
    "        d = paired_bootstrap_delta(y.loc[pint.index], pint, pmain.reindex(pint.index), cfg, \"r2\")\n",
    "        ra_all, rb_all = fold_representative(S, ca, list(S.index)), fold_representative(S, cb, list(S.index))\n",
    "        prod = (ra_all * rb_all).rename(\"prod\")\n",
    "        mi = mutual_information(prod.to_frame(), y.reindex(prod.index), int(cfg[\"seed\"]))[\"prod\"]\n",
    "        terc = pd.qcut(ra_all, 3, labels=[\"low\", \"mid\", \"high\"], duplicates=\"drop\")\n",
    "        cond = {f\"rho_b_given_a_{lvl}\": safe_corr(rb_all[terc == lvl], y.reindex(rb_all.index)[terc == lvl], \"spearman\", 15)[0]\n",
    "                for lvl in terc.dropna().unique()}\n",
    "        sub = pd.DataFrame({\"a\": ra_all, \"b\": rb_all, \"theta\": S[screening].mean(axis=1)}).dropna()\n",
    "        h = np.nan\n",
    "        if len(sub) >= 50:\n",
    "            gbm = HistGradientBoostingRegressor(max_depth=3, max_iter=200, learning_rate=0.05, random_state=int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "            gbm.fit(sub, y.loc[sub.index])\n",
    "            h = h_statistic(gbm, sub, \"a\", \"b\", int(cfg[\"interaction_h_statistic_max_n\"]), int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "            surfaces.append((label, gbm, sub))\n",
    "        fr = pd.DataFrame(fold_rows)\n",
    "        fr = fr[fr[\"interaction\"] == label]\n",
    "        rows.append({\"interaction\": label, \"status\": \"OK\", \"n_columns_a\": len(ca), \"n_columns_b\": len(cb),\n",
    "                     \"delta_r2_interaction\": d[\"delta\"], \"ci_lower\": d[\"ci_lower\"], \"ci_upper\": d[\"ci_upper\"],\n",
    "                     \"fold_sign_consistency\": float((fr[\"delta_r2\"] > 0).mean()) if len(fr) else np.nan,\n",
    "                     \"mutual_information_product\": mi, \"friedman_h\": h, **cond})\n",
    "    res = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(res, \"interaction_results\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(pd.DataFrame(fold_rows), \"interaction_fold_stability\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    shap_summary = _shap_interactions(ctx, surfaces)\n",
    "    ctx.save_json(shap_summary, \"interaction_shap_summary\")\n",
    "    _interaction_figures(ctx, res, surfaces, y)\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": [\"interaction_results\", \"interaction_fold_stability\", \"interaction_shap_summary\"],\n",
    "            \"summary\": res[[\"interaction\", \"status\"] + [c for c in (\"delta_r2_interaction\", \"friedman_h\") if c in res]].to_dict(\"records\")}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _special_interaction(ctx, S, y, meta, assign, a, b, screening) -> dict:\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    label = f\"{a} x {b}\"\n",
    "    if \"INSTRUMENT\" in (a, b):\n",
    "        if meta[\"instrument\"].nunique() < 2:\n",
    "            return {\"interaction\": label, \"status\": \"UNAVAILABLE\", \"reason\": \"single instrument\"}\n",
    "        dummies = pd.get_dummies(meta[\"instrument\"].reindex(S.index).astype(str), drop_first=True, dtype=float)\n",
    "        base = S[screening].join(dummies)\n",
    "        inter = base.copy()\n",
    "        for c in dummies.columns:\n",
    "            inter[f\"theta_mean_x_{c}\"] = S[\"theta_mean\"] * dummies[c] if \"theta_mean\" in S else S[screening].mean(axis=1) * dummies[c]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        other = b if a == \"TASK\" else a\n",
    "        if other == \"COMPLEXITY\":\n",
    "            glob = [c for c in S.columns if c.startswith(\"cx_\") and c.endswith(\"__all\") and \"_reliable\" not in c]\n",
    "            task = [c for c in S.columns if c.startswith(\"cx_\") and not c.endswith((\"__all\", \"_reliable\", \"_n\"))]\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            fam_cols = modeling_columns(S.columns, [\"TEMPORAL\", \"SPECTRAL\", \"MFCC\"])\n",
    "            glob = [c for c in fam_cols if \"__task=\" not in c and c.endswith(\"__mean\")][:200]\n",
    "            task = [c for c in fam_cols if \"__task=\" in c and c.endswith(\"__mean\")][:400]\n",
    "        if not glob or not task:\n",
    "            return {\"interaction\": label, \"status\": \"UNAVAILABLE\", \"reason\": \"no task-conditioned features\"}\n",
    "        base = S[screening + glob]\n",
    "        inter = S[screening + glob + task]\n",
    "    pm, pi = [], []\n",
    "    for rep, fold, tr, va in iter_folds(assign, \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\", repeats=[0]):\n",
    "        tr = [t for t in tr if t in S.index]\n",
    "        va = [v for v in va if v in S.index]\n",
    "        pm.append(pd.Series(_ridge(base.loc[tr], y.loc[tr], base.loc[va]), index=va))\n",
    "        pi.append(pd.Series(_ridge(inter.loc[tr], y.loc[tr], inter.loc[va]), index=va))\n",
    "    pm, pi = pd.concat(pm), pd.concat(pi)\n",
    "    d = paired_bootstrap_delta(y.loc[pi.index], pi, pm.reindex(pi.index), cfg, \"r2\")\n",
    "    return {\"interaction\": label, \"status\": \"OK\", \"delta_r2_interaction\": d[\"delta\"], \"ci_lower\": d[\"ci_lower\"],\n",
    "            \"ci_upper\": d[\"ci_upper\"], \"note\": \"task-specific vs pooled representation\" if \"TASK\" in (a, b) else \"instrument-specific screening slopes\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _shap_interactions(ctx, surfaces) -> dict:\n",
    "    if not surfaces:\n",
    "        return {\"status\": \"NO_MODELS\"}\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import shap  # type: ignore\n",
    "        from xgboost import XGBRegressor  # type: ignore\n",
    "    except ImportError:\n",
    "        return {\"status\": \"UNAVAILABLE\", \"reason\": \"shap and xgboost required\"}\n",
    "    out = {}\n",
    "    for label, _, sub in surfaces[:5]:\n",
    "        y = da.target(ctx).reindex(sub.index)\n",
    "        m = XGBRegressor(max_depth=3, n_estimators=200, learning_rate=0.05, random_state=int(ctx.config[\"seed\"])).fit(sub, y)\n",
    "        vals = shap.TreeExplainer(m).shap_interaction_values(sub)\n",
    "        out[label] = {\"mean_abs_interaction_a_b\": float(np.abs(vals[:, 0, 1]).mean()),\n",
    "                      \"mean_abs_main_a\": float(np.abs(vals[:, 0, 0]).mean()), \"mean_abs_main_b\": float(np.abs(vals[:, 1, 1]).mean())}\n",
    "    return {\"status\": \"OK\", \"results\": out}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _interaction_figures(ctx, res: pd.DataFrame, surfaces, y) -> None:\n",
    "    ok = res[res[\"status\"] == \"OK\"].dropna(subset=[\"delta_r2_interaction\"])\n",
    "    if len(ok):\n",
    "        ok = ok.sort_values(\"delta_r2_interaction\")\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (8, 0.35 * len(ok) + 2))\n",
    "        viz.forest(axes[0, 0], ok, \"interaction\", \"delta_r2_interaction\", \"ci_lower\", \"ci_upper\",\n",
    "                   \"Out-of-fold R² gain from adding the interaction\", \"delta R² (paired bootstrap 95% CI)\")\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, \"interaction_gains\", \"Interaction stability report\", \"Do features matter only for particular profiles?\",\n",
    "                   \"interaction_results\", int(len(y)), \"Predefined candidate set; representatives fitted within folds.\")\n",
    "    for label, gbm, sub in surfaces[:4]:\n",
    "        ga = np.quantile(sub[\"a\"], np.linspace(0.05, 0.95, 12))\n",
    "        gb = np.quantile(sub[\"b\"], np.linspace(0.05, 0.95, 12))\n",
    "        M = np.zeros((len(gb), len(ga)))\n",
    "        bg = sub.sample(min(len(sub), 200), random_state=0)\n",
    "        for i, vb in enumerate(gb):\n",
    "            for j, va in enumerate(ga):\n",
    "                X = bg.copy()\n",
    "                X[\"a\"], X[\"b\"] = va, vb\n",
    "                M[i, j] = gbm.predict(X).mean()\n",
    "        fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (6, 5))\n",
    "        viz.heatmap(axes[0, 0], pd.DataFrame(M, index=np.round(gb, 2), columns=np.round(ga, 2)),\n",
    "                    f\"2-D partial dependence: {label} (a=x, b=y)\", cmap=\"viridis\", cbar_label=\"predicted outcome\")\n",
    "        ctx.figure(fig, f\"interaction_surface_{label.replace(' ', '')}\", f\"Two-dimensional response surface: {label}\",\n",
    "                   \"How do the two factors combine?\", \"interaction_results\", int(len(sub)),\n",
    "                   \"Gradient-boosting partial dependence over representative variables (descriptive).\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-019",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/feature_registry.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Section 24 - feature discovery registry.\n",
    "\n",
    "Tracks every generated student-level feature with provenance, availability,\n",
    "association evidence (raw and residual, adjusted, FDR, bootstrap), CV\n",
    "incremental value (student-level and school-grouped), cross-school sign\n",
    "consistency, redundancy, confounding risk and voice-conversion sensitivity.\n",
    "Evidence is kept in separate rankings rather than collapsed into a single\n",
    "arbitrary importance score.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from .families import COMPUTATION_COST, FAMILY_HYPOTHESIS, INTERPRETABILITY, TECHNICAL_FAMILIES, feature_family, feature_subfamily\n",
    "\n",
    "STAT_WORDS = {\"mean\": \"mean\", \"std\": \"standard deviation\", \"median\": \"median\", \"mad\": \"median absolute deviation\",\n",
    "              \"min\": \"minimum\", \"max\": \"maximum\", \"iqr\": \"interquartile range\", \"cv\": \"coefficient of variation\",\n",
    "              \"count\": \"observation count\", \"p10\": \"10th percentile\", \"p25\": \"25th percentile\", \"p75\": \"75th percentile\",\n",
    "              \"p90\": \"90th percentile\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def describe(col: str) -> tuple[str, str, str]:\n",
    "    parts = col.split(\"__\")\n",
    "    base = parts[0]\n",
    "    stat = parts[-1] if len(parts) > 1 and parts[-1] in STAT_WORDS else \"\"\n",
    "    conds = [p for p in parts[1:] if \"=\" in p]\n",
    "    level = \"student\" if not stat and not conds else \"clip->student\"\n",
    "    desc = f\"{STAT_WORDS.get(stat, stat)} of {base}\" if stat else base\n",
    "    if conds:\n",
    "        desc += \" restricted to \" + \", \".join(conds)\n",
    "    return desc, (\"conditional:\" + \",\".join(conds) if conds else (stat or \"direct\")), level\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _source(col: str) -> str:\n",
    "    fam = feature_family(col)\n",
    "    return {\"SCREENING\": \"train/test_student_metadata.csv\", \"CORRECTNESS\": \"clip metadata (correctness)\",\n",
    "            \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\": \"IRT on clip correctness\", \"ADAPTIVE\": \"ordered clip correctness\",\n",
    "            \"LINGUISTIC\": \"expected text (local G2P)\", \"PHONETIC\": \"local ASR vs expected text\",\n",
    "            \"EMBEDDINGS\": \"frozen foundation model\"}.get(fam, \"anonymised audio (unified extraction)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _dependencies(fam: str) -> str:\n",
    "    return {\"WAVELETS\": \"PyWavelets\", \"PROSODY\": \"librosa.pyin\", \"PHONETIC\": \"transformers+torch (ASR), G2P\",\n",
    "            \"EMBEDDINGS\": \"transformers+torch\", \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\": \"scipy (IRT)\", \"LINGUISTIC\": \"G2P backend\"}.get(fam, \"numpy/scipy/librosa\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def redundancy_groups(S: pd.DataFrame, cols: list, threshold: float, max_cols: int = 1500) -> pd.Series:\n",
    "    from scipy.cluster.hierarchy import fcluster, linkage\n",
    "    from scipy.spatial.distance import squareform\n",
    "\n",
    "    cols = cols[:max_cols]\n",
    "    if len(cols) < 2:\n",
    "        return pd.Series(dtype=object)\n",
    "    R = S[cols].rank().corr(min_periods=20).abs().fillna(0.0).to_numpy()\n",
    "    np.fill_diagonal(R, 1.0)\n",
    "    D = np.clip(1 - R, 0, 1)\n",
    "    Z = linkage(squareform(D, checks=False), \"average\")\n",
    "    lab = fcluster(Z, t=1 - threshold, criterion=\"distance\")\n",
    "    return pd.Series([f\"RG{l:05d}\" for l in lab], index=cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def classify(r: pd.Series, alpha: float, min_n: int) -> tuple[str, str]:\n",
    "    if r.get(\"valid_observation_count\", 0) < min_n or not np.isfinite(r.get(\"variance\", np.nan)) or r.get(\"variance\", 0) == 0:\n",
    "        return \"UNAVAILABLE\", \"too few valid observations or constant\"\n",
    "    q = r.get(\"fdr_adjusted_pvalue\", np.nan)\n",
    "    if not np.isfinite(q):\n",
    "        return \"INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE\", \"residual association not testable\"\n",
    "    ci_excl = np.isfinite(r.get(\"bootstrap_ci_lower\", np.nan)) and (r[\"bootstrap_ci_lower\"] > 0 or r[\"bootstrap_ci_upper\"] < 0)\n",
    "    cons = r.get(\"cross_school_sign_consistency\", np.nan)\n",
    "    cons_ok = (not np.isfinite(cons)) or cons >= 0.75\n",
    "    sig = q < alpha\n",
    "    if (sig or ci_excl) and r.get(\"confound_risk\") == \"HIGH\":\n",
    "        return \"CONFOUNDED_SIGNAL\", \"residual association but high technical confounding risk\"\n",
    "    if sig and np.isfinite(cons) and cons < 0.6:\n",
    "        return \"UNSTABLE_SIGNAL\", f\"significant but school sign consistency {cons:.2f}\"\n",
    "    cv_ok = (not np.isfinite(r.get(\"cv_delta_r2\", np.nan))) or r[\"cv_delta_r2\"] > 0\n",
    "    sg_ok = (not np.isfinite(r.get(\"school_grouped_delta_r2\", np.nan))) or r[\"school_grouped_delta_r2\"] > 0\n",
    "    if sig and ci_excl and cons_ok and cv_ok and sg_ok:\n",
    "        if r.get(\"is_redundancy_leader\") is False:\n",
    "            return \"REDUNDANT_SIGNAL\", f\"robust but redundant with {r.get('redundancy_leader')}\"\n",
    "        return \"ROBUST_SIGNAL\", \"FDR-significant, bootstrap CI excludes 0, stable across schools, positive CV gain\"\n",
    "    if (q < 0.2 or ci_excl) and (not np.isfinite(cons) or cons >= 0.6):\n",
    "        if r.get(\"is_redundancy_leader\") is False:\n",
    "            return \"REDUNDANT_SIGNAL\", f\"promising but redundant with {r.get('redundancy_leader')}\"\n",
    "        return \"PROMISING_SIGNAL\", \"suggestive residual association; needs confirmation\"\n",
    "    return \"WEAK_SIGNAL\", \"no reliable residual association\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def stage_feature_registry(ctx) -> dict:\n",
    "    from .ablation import ColumnSetBuilder, cv_evaluate\n",
    "    from .residual_discovery import association_screen, candidate_features\n",
    "    from .stats_utils import bootstrap_ci, mutual_information, safe_corr, spearman_stat\n",
    "    from .validation import available_schemes, paired_bootstrap_delta, pooled_predictions\n",
    "\n",
    "    cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "    alpha = float(cfg[\"fdr_alpha\"])\n",
    "    min_n = int(cfg[\"min_n_correlation\"])\n",
    "    S = da.student_features(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    meta = da.student_meta(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "    y = meta[\"target\"].dropna().astype(float)\n",
    "    S = S.reindex(y.index)\n",
    "    resid = ctx.load_df(\"baseline_residuals\").set_index(\"student_id\")\n",
    "    D = S.join(meta, rsuffix=\"_meta\").join(resid[[\"residual\", \"residual_group\", \"oof_prediction\"]])\n",
    "    all_cols = [c for c in S.columns if pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(S[c]) and feature_family(c) != \"OTHER\"]\n",
    "    if ctx.stage_available(\"16\"):\n",
    "        assoc = ctx.load_df(\"residual_associations\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        assoc = association_screen(D, candidate_features(D), da.raw_theta_columns(D), cfg)\n",
    "    assoc = assoc.set_index(\"feature\")\n",
    "    sens = ctx.load_df(\"anonymization_sensitivity\").set_index(\"feature\")[\"sensitivity\"] if ctx.stage_available(\"10\") else pd.Series(dtype=object)\n",
    "    sep = ctx.load_df(\"school_separability\") if ctx.stage_available(\"17\") else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    sep_map = sep.set_index(\"family\")[\"balanced_accuracy\"] / sep.set_index(\"family\")[\"chance\"] if \"balanced_accuracy\" in sep else pd.Series(dtype=float)\n",
    "    abl = ctx.load_df(\"ablation_results\") if ctx.stage_available(\"20\") else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    artifacts = [c for c in (\"q_snr_db_approx__mean\", \"q_noise_floor_db__mean\", \"q_eff_bandwidth_hz__mean\", \"s_bg_level_db__mean\",\n",
    "                             \"meta_orig_sr_mode\") if c in S.columns]\n",
    "    schools = meta[\"school_id\"].reindex(S.index)\n",
    "    mi = mutual_information(S[all_cols[:3000]], y, int(cfg[\"seed\"]), min_n) if all_cols else pd.Series(dtype=float)\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for c in all_cols:\n",
    "        fam = feature_family(c)\n",
    "        x = S[c]\n",
    "        desc, agg, level = describe(c)\n",
    "        a = assoc.loc[c] if c in assoc.index else None\n",
    "        art = [abs(safe_corr(x, S[q], \"spearman\", min_n)[0]) for q in artifacts if q != c]\n",
    "        art_max = float(np.nanmax(art)) if art and np.isfinite(art).any() else np.nan\n",
    "        sep_ratio = float(sep_map.get(fam, np.nan)) if len(sep_map) else np.nan\n",
    "        risk = \"HIGH\" if fam in TECHNICAL_FAMILIES or (np.isfinite(art_max) and art_max >= 0.5) or \\\n",
    "            sens.get(c.split(\"__\")[0]) == \"RECORDING_ARTIFACT_SENSITIVE\" else (\n",
    "            \"MEDIUM\" if (np.isfinite(art_max) and art_max >= 0.3) or (np.isfinite(sep_ratio) and sep_ratio >= 2) else \"LOW\")\n",
    "        base_name = c.split(\"__\")[0].replace(\"ia_\", \"\", 1)\n",
    "        vc = \"POTENTIALLY_VOICE_CONVERSION_SENSITIVE\" if sens.get(base_name) == \"POTENTIALLY_VOICE_CONVERSION_SENSITIVE\" else (\n",
    "            str(sens.get(base_name)) if base_name in sens.index else (\"NOT_APPLICABLE\" if fam in {\"SCREENING\", \"CORRECTNESS\", \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\", \"ADAPTIVE\", \"LINGUISTIC\"} else \"UNDETERMINED\"))\n",
    "        signs = []\n",
    "        r_all = a[\"residual_spearman\"] if a is not None else safe_corr(x, D[\"residual\"], \"spearman\", min_n)[0]\n",
    "        for s, ids in schools.dropna().groupby(schools.dropna()).groups.items():\n",
    "            if len(ids) >= int(cfg[\"min_group_size\"]) and np.isfinite(r_all):\n",
    "                rs = safe_corr(x.loc[ids], D.loc[ids, \"residual\"], \"spearman\", int(cfg[\"min_group_size\"]))[0]\n",
    "                if np.isfinite(rs):\n",
    "                    signs.append(np.sign(rs) == np.sign(r_all))\n",
    "        row = {\n",
    "            \"feature_id\": f\"F{len(rows):06d}\", \"feature_name\": c, \"feature_family\": fam, \"feature_subfamily\": feature_subfamily(c),\n",
    "            \"description\": desc, \"scientific_hypothesis\": FAMILY_HYPOTHESIS.get(fam, \"\"), \"source\": _source(c),\n",
    "            \"source_columns\": c.split(\"__\")[0], \"extraction_version\": cfg[\"extraction_version\"], \"aggregation_method\": agg,\n",
    "            \"hierarchical_level\": level, \"task\": next((p.split(\"=\")[1] for p in c.split(\"__\") if p.startswith(\"task=\")), \"all\"),\n",
    "            \"required_dependencies\": _dependencies(fam), \"availability\": \"AVAILABLE\" if x.notna().any() else \"UNAVAILABLE\",\n",
    "            \"missing_rate\": float(x.isna().mean()), \"valid_observation_count\": int(x.notna().sum()),\n",
    "            \"variance\": float(x.var()) if x.notna().sum() > 1 else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"target_pearson\": a[\"target_pearson\"] if a is not None else safe_corr(x, y, \"pearson\", min_n)[0],\n",
    "            \"target_spearman\": a[\"target_spearman\"] if a is not None else safe_corr(x, y, \"spearman\", min_n)[0],\n",
    "            \"target_mutual_information\": float(mi.get(c, np.nan)),\n",
    "            \"residual_pearson\": a[\"residual_pearson\"] if a is not None else safe_corr(x, D[\"residual\"], \"pearson\", min_n)[0],\n",
    "            \"residual_spearman\": r_all,\n",
    "            \"adjusted_regression_coefficient\": a.get(\"screening_adjusted_coef\", np.nan) if a is not None else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"effect_size\": a.get(\"screening_adjusted_coef\", np.nan) / y.std() if a is not None else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"pvalue\": a[\"residual_p\"] if a is not None else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"fdr_adjusted_pvalue\": a[\"residual_q\"] if a is not None else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"bootstrap_ci_lower\": a.get(\"residual_rho_ci_lower\", np.nan) if a is not None else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"bootstrap_ci_upper\": a.get(\"residual_rho_ci_upper\", np.nan) if a is not None else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"cv_delta_r2\": np.nan, \"school_grouped_delta_r2\": np.nan,\n",
    "            \"cross_school_sign_consistency\": float(np.mean(signs)) if signs else np.nan,\n",
    "            \"confound_risk\": risk, \"artifact_max_abs_rho\": art_max, \"family_school_separability_ratio\": sep_ratio,\n",
    "            \"voice_conversion_sensitivity\": vc, \"computation_cost\": COMPUTATION_COST.get(fam, \"UNKNOWN\"),\n",
    "            \"interpretability\": INTERPRETABILITY.get(fam, \"UNKNOWN\"),\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        rows.append(row)\n",
    "    reg = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    # bootstrap CIs for top features not covered by Section 16\n",
    "    need = reg[reg[\"bootstrap_ci_lower\"].isna()].reindex(reg[\"residual_spearman\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index).dropna(subset=[\"residual_spearman\"])\n",
    "    need = need.head(int(cfg[\"feature_registry_bootstrap_top_k\"]))\n",
    "    for i, r in need.iterrows():\n",
    "        sub = D[[r[\"feature_name\"], \"residual\"]].dropna()\n",
    "        ci = bootstrap_ci(spearman_stat, sub.iloc[:, 0].to_numpy(), sub[\"residual\"].to_numpy(), n_boot=min(int(cfg[\"bootstrap_iterations\"]), 500),\n",
    "                          seed=int(cfg[\"seed\"]))\n",
    "        reg.loc[i, \"bootstrap_ci_lower\"], reg.loc[i, \"bootstrap_ci_upper\"] = ci[\"lower\"], ci[\"upper\"]\n",
    "    # per-feature CV incremental value (top-K by |residual rho|)\n",
    "    assign = ctx.load_df(\"cv_assignments\")\n",
    "    num = S[[c for c in S.columns if pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(S[c])]]\n",
    "    screening = da.raw_theta_columns(num)\n",
    "    top = reg.reindex(reg[\"residual_spearman\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index).dropna(subset=[\"residual_spearman\"])\n",
    "    top = top[~top[\"feature_family\"].isin([\"SCREENING\"])].head(int(cfg[\"feature_registry_cv_top_k\"]))\n",
    "    refs = {}\n",
    "    for scheme in [s for s in (\"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\", \"CV_B_SCHOOL_GROUP_KFOLD\") if s in available_schemes(assign)]:\n",
    "        rep = [0] if scheme.startswith(\"CV_A\") else None\n",
    "        refs[scheme] = pooled_predictions(cv_evaluate(ColumnSetBuilder(num, screening), None, y, assign, scheme, cfg, repeats=rep).oof)\n",
    "        col = \"cv_delta_r2\" if scheme.startswith(\"CV_A\") else \"school_grouped_delta_r2\"\n",
    "        for i, r in top.iterrows():\n",
    "            p = pooled_predictions(cv_evaluate(ColumnSetBuilder(num, screening + [r[\"feature_name\"]]), None, y, assign, scheme, cfg, repeats=rep).oof)\n",
    "            common = p.index.intersection(refs[scheme].index)\n",
    "            reg.loc[i, col] = paired_bootstrap_delta(p.loc[common, \"y\"], p.loc[common, \"pred\"], refs[scheme].loc[common, \"pred\"],\n",
    "                                                     {**cfg, \"bootstrap_iterations\": 50}, \"r2\")[\"delta\"]\n",
    "    groups = redundancy_groups(S, reg.reindex(reg[\"residual_spearman\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).index)[\"feature_name\"].tolist(),\n",
    "                               float(cfg[\"redundancy_threshold\"]))\n",
    "    reg[\"redundancy_group\"] = reg[\"feature_name\"].map(groups)\n",
    "    strength = reg.set_index(\"feature_name\")[\"residual_spearman\"].abs()\n",
    "    leaders = reg.dropna(subset=[\"redundancy_group\"]).assign(s=lambda d: d[\"feature_name\"].map(strength)).sort_values(\"s\", ascending=False) \\\n",
    "        .groupby(\"redundancy_group\")[\"feature_name\"].first()\n",
    "    reg[\"redundancy_leader\"] = reg[\"redundancy_group\"].map(leaders)\n",
    "    reg[\"is_redundancy_leader\"] = reg[\"redundancy_leader\"].isna() | (reg[\"redundancy_leader\"] == reg[\"feature_name\"])\n",
    "    cls = reg.apply(lambda r: classify(r, alpha, min_n), axis=1)\n",
    "    reg[\"selection_status\"] = [c[0] for c in cls]\n",
    "    reg[\"selection_reason\"] = [c[1] for c in cls]\n",
    "    if len(abl):\n",
    "        fam_gain = abl[(abl[\"scheme\"] == \"CV_A_REPEATED_STUDENT_KFOLD\")].groupby(\"families\")[\"delta_r2_vs_full_tabular\"].max()\n",
    "        reg[\"family_ablation_context\"] = reg[\"feature_family\"].map(\n",
    "            lambda f: float(fam_gain[[f in k.split(\"+\") for k in fam_gain.index]].max()) if any(f in k.split(\"+\") for k in fam_gain.index) else np.nan)\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(reg, \"feature_registry\", also_csv=True)\n",
    "    rankings = {\n",
    "        \"predictive\": reg.assign(score=reg[\"target_spearman\"].abs()).sort_values(\"score\", ascending=False),\n",
    "        \"incremental\": reg.dropna(subset=[\"cv_delta_r2\"]).sort_values(\"cv_delta_r2\", ascending=False),\n",
    "        \"interpretability\": reg.assign(i=reg[\"interpretability\"].map({\"HIGH\": 0, \"MEDIUM\": 1, \"LOW\": 2}).fillna(3),\n",
    "                                       s=-reg[\"residual_spearman\"].abs()).sort_values([\"i\", \"s\"]),\n",
    "        \"cross_school_robustness\": reg.dropna(subset=[\"cross_school_sign_consistency\"]).sort_values(\n",
    "            [\"cross_school_sign_consistency\", \"residual_spearman\"], ascending=False),\n",
    "        \"residual\": reg.assign(score=reg[\"residual_spearman\"].abs()).sort_values(\"score\", ascending=False),\n",
    "        \"computational_efficiency\": reg.assign(c=reg[\"computation_cost\"].map({\"LOW\": 0, \"MEDIUM\": 1, \"HIGH\": 2, \"VERY_HIGH\": 3}).fillna(4),\n",
    "                                               s=-reg[\"residual_spearman\"].abs()).sort_values([\"c\", \"s\"]),\n",
    "        \"confounding_risk\": reg.assign(c=reg[\"confound_risk\"].map({\"LOW\": 0, \"MEDIUM\": 1, \"HIGH\": 2})).sort_values([\"c\", \"artifact_max_abs_rho\"]),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    outputs = [\"feature_registry\"]\n",
    "    for name, df in rankings.items():\n",
    "        ctx.save_df(df[[\"feature_name\", \"feature_family\", \"selection_status\", \"target_spearman\", \"residual_spearman\", \"cv_delta_r2\",\n",
    "                        \"cross_school_sign_consistency\", \"confound_risk\", \"computation_cost\", \"interpretability\"]].head(500),\n",
    "                    f\"feature_ranking_{name}\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "        outputs.append(f\"feature_ranking_{name}\")\n",
    "    evidence = reg.set_index(\"feature_name\")[[\"selection_status\", \"selection_reason\", \"fdr_adjusted_pvalue\", \"bootstrap_ci_lower\",\n",
    "                                              \"bootstrap_ci_upper\", \"cross_school_sign_consistency\", \"cv_delta_r2\",\n",
    "                                              \"school_grouped_delta_r2\", \"confound_risk\", \"redundancy_group\", \"redundancy_leader\"]]\n",
    "    ctx.save_df(evidence.reset_index(), \"feature_retention_evidence\", fmt=\"csv\")\n",
    "    outputs.append(\"feature_retention_evidence\")\n",
    "    from . import visualization as viz\n",
    "\n",
    "    counts = reg.groupby([\"feature_family\", \"selection_status\"]).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
    "    fig, axes = viz.new_figure(1, 1, (9, 0.35 * len(counts) + 2))\n",
    "    counts.plot(kind=\"barh\", stacked=True, ax=axes[0, 0])\n",
    "    viz.finalize_axis(axes[0, 0], \"Feature registry: selection status by family\", \"features\", \"\", int(len(y)))\n",
    "    ctx.figure(fig, \"feature_registry_status\", \"Feature discovery registry\", \"Which features carry robust signal?\", \"feature_registry\",\n",
    "               int(len(y)), \"; \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in reg[\"selection_status\"].value_counts().items()))\n",
    "    return {\"outputs\": outputs, \"summary\": reg[\"selection_status\"].value_counts().to_dict()}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-020",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%writefile {CODE_ROOT}/src/wildspeech/fold_features.py\n",
    "\"\"\"Fold-aware feature construction for predictive evaluation.\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything fitted on data (common screening factor, IRT item parameters,\n",
    "item reference statistics, index scaling, clustering) is fitted on the\n",
    "training students of the fold only and then applied to validation (or test)\n",
    "students. Imputation, scaling, PCA and supervised selection happen inside\n",
    "scikit-learn pipelines and are therefore fold-aware as well.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from . import data_access as da\n",
    "from .families import FOLD_FITTED_FAMILIES, modeling_columns\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class FoldFeatureBuilder:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, ctx, base: pd.DataFrame | None = None, include_test: bool = False):\n",
    "        self.ctx = ctx\n",
    "        self.cfg = ctx.config\n",
    "        if base is None:\n",
    "            base = da.student_features(ctx, \"train\")\n",
    "            if include_test and ctx.has(\"student_features_test\"):\n",
    "                base = pd.concat([base, da.student_features(ctx, \"test\")])\n",
    "        numeric = [c for c in base.columns if pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(base[c])]\n",
    "        self.base = base[numeric].replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n",
    "        self.include_test = include_test\n",
    "        self._clips = None\n",
    "        self._cache: dict = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "    def clips(self) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        if self._clips is None:\n",
    "            parts = [da.clip_table(self.ctx, \"train\", with_audio=self.ctx.stage_available(\"06\"))]\n",
    "            if self.include_test:\n",
    "                try:\n",
    "                    parts.append(da.clip_table(self.ctx, \"test\", with_audio=self.ctx.has(\"clip_features_test\")))\n",
    "                except Exception:\n",
    "                    pass\n",
    "            self._clips = pd.concat(parts, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "        return self._clips\n",
    "\n",
    "    def columns_for(self, families) -> list:\n",
    "        return modeling_columns(self.base.columns, families)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _cached(self, name: str, key, fn):\n",
    "        k = (name, key)\n",
    "        if key is not None and k in self._cache:\n",
    "            return self._cache[k]\n",
    "        value = fn()\n",
    "        if key is not None:\n",
    "            self._cache[k] = value\n",
    "        return value\n",
    "\n",
    "    def build(self, train_ids, val_ids, families, key=None) -> tuple[pd.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame]:\n",
    "        families = set(families)\n",
    "        train_ids = list(train_ids)\n",
    "        ids = train_ids + [v for v in val_ids if v not in set(train_ids)]\n",
    "        X = self.base.reindex(ids)[self.columns_for(families)].copy()\n",
    "        if \"SCREENING\" in families:\n",
    "            X = X.join(self._cached(\"theta_cf\", key, lambda: self._theta_factor(train_ids)).reindex(ids))\n",
    "        if \"ITEM_DIFFICULTY\" in families:\n",
    "            irt = self._irt(key, train_ids)\n",
    "            if not irt.empty:\n",
    "                X = X.join(irt.reindex(ids))\n",
    "        if \"ITEM_ADJUSTED_AUDIO\" in families:\n",
    "            ia = self._ia(key, train_ids)\n",
    "            if not ia.empty:\n",
    "                X = X.join(ia.reindex(ids), rsuffix=\"_fold\")\n",
    "        if \"LITERACY_INDICES\" in families:\n",
    "            from .literacy_indices import compute_indices\n",
    "\n",
    "            def _idx():\n",
    "                extra = pd.concat([self._irt(key, train_ids), self._ia(key, train_ids)], axis=1)\n",
    "                return compute_indices(self.base.reindex(ids), train_ids, self.cfg,\n",
    "                                       extra=extra.reindex(ids) if not extra.empty else None)[0]\n",
    "            idx = self._cached(\"idx\", key, _idx)\n",
    "            X = X.join(idx.reindex(ids), rsuffix=\"_fold\")\n",
    "        if \"CLUSTER\" in families:\n",
    "            from .clustering import fold_cluster_features\n",
    "\n",
    "            clu = self._cached(\"clu\", key, lambda: fold_cluster_features(self.base.reindex(ids), train_ids, self.cfg))\n",
    "            X = X.join(clu.reindex(ids), rsuffix=\"_fold\")\n",
    "        X = X.loc[:, ~X.columns.duplicated()]\n",
    "        X = X.loc[:, X.loc[train_ids].notna().any()]\n",
    "        return X.loc[train_ids], X.loc[list(val_ids)]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _irt(self, key, train_ids) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        if not self.cfg.get(\"enable_irt\"):\n",
    "            return pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "        from .irt import fold_irt_features\n",
    "\n",
    "        clips = self.clips()\n",
    "        if \"correct\" not in clips.columns or clips[\"correct\"].notna().sum() == 0:\n",
    "            return pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "        return self._cached(\"irt\", key, lambda: fold_irt_features(clips, set(train_ids), self.cfg))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _ia(self, key, train_ids) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        from .student_aggregation import core_features, item_adjusted_features, numeric_clip_features\n",
    "\n",
    "        def _compute():\n",
    "            c = self.clips()\n",
    "            return item_adjusted_features(c, core_features(numeric_clip_features(c), self.cfg), train_ids,\n",
    "                                          float(self.cfg[\"item_shrinkage_k\"]))\n",
    "        return self._cached(\"ia\", key, _compute)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _theta_factor(self, train_ids) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "        from .screening_eda import derive_screening_features\n",
    "\n",
    "        raw = da.raw_theta_columns(self.base)\n",
    "        if len(raw) < 2:\n",
    "            return pd.DataFrame(index=self.base.index)\n",
    "        _, params = derive_screening_features(self.base.loc[train_ids, raw])\n",
    "        feats, _ = derive_screening_features(self.base[raw], params)\n",
    "        return feats[[\"theta_common_factor\"]]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def requires_fold_fitting(families) -> bool:\n",
    "    return bool(set(families) & (FOLD_FITTED_FAMILIES | {\"SCREENING\"}))\n"
   ]
  },
