   "source": [
    "## Section 00 — Environment initialization\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research question.** Is the runtime authorised, correctly configured and able to locate the data?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Motivation.** Reproducibility and data-use compliance.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs.** CONFIG, Drive folder\n",
    "\n",
    "**Methodology.** Environment detection, Drive mount (Colab, authorised only), recursive data discovery with duplicate detection, hardware/GPU/package diagnostics, seeds.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Configuration.** `environment, cloud_storage_authorized, data_root, use_gpu, n_jobs, seed`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs.** environment_report.json, required_file_inventory.csv\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation.** Confirms where data was found and which optional modules can run.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations.** Package availability ≠ functional correctness."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-069",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "section_00_report = run_section(\"00\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-070",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 01 — Data integrity and hierarchical reconstruction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research question.** Can the dataset be represented reliably at student, task, item, clip and frame level?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Motivation.** Every later analysis depends on correct joins.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs.** All CSVs, read kwargs JSON, TAR archives (inspected, not extracted)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Methodology.** Runtime schema resolution with ambiguity detection, ID uniqueness, join-key inference, duplicates/conflicts, train-test overlap, archive safety, clip-audio matching, audio metadata, student-level sampling.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Configuration.** `schema_overrides, task_family_overrides, audio_inventory_decode`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs.** student_master, clip_master, task_master, item_master, audio_manifest, schema_registry, data_quality_report\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation.** Review warnings and ambiguity before proceeding.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations.** Test audio headers decoded only when test inference is allowed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-071",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "section_01_report = run_section(\"01\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-072",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 02 — Target variable intelligence\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research question.** What determines the distribution and predictability of the outcome?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Motivation.** Instrument and school effects can masquerade as signal.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs.** student_master\n",
    "\n",
    "**Methodology.** Robust summaries, outliers, floor/ceiling, GMM modality, instrument/school comparisons, variance decomposition, heteroscedasticity.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Configuration.** `min_group_size`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs.** target_summary.json, target_* tables, figures\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation.** Instruments are compared, never assumed interchangeable.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations.** Descriptive only."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-073",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "section_02_report = run_section(\"02\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-074",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 03 — Screening intelligence\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research question.** How much of the outcome does conventional screening explain?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Motivation.** Defines the baseline every new signal must beat.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs.** student_master\n",
    "\n",
    "**Methodology.** Linear/rank/MI/distance correlations, spline vs linear CV R², partial correlations, conditional distributions, group-conditioned (shrunk) correlations, PCA, missingness, derived features.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Configuration.** `min_n_correlation`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs.** screening_features, screening_associations, figures\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation.** theta_common_factor is refitted inside folds for prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations.** Profiles are descriptive."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-075",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
