   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-080",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 06 — Acoustic quality atlas and unified extraction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research question.** How reliable is the acoustic information, and what does it contain?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Motivation.** Quality defines which signals can be trusted.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs.** TAR archives\n",
    "\n",
    "**Methodology.** Safe extraction (or streaming), single decode per clip, shared STFT/mel/MFCC/VAD bundle, quality/temporal/spectral/wavelet/prosody features, chunked resumable parallel extraction, stratified atlas.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Configuration.** `sample_rate, n_fft, hop_length, vad_*, extraction_chunk_size, atlas_*`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs.** clip_features, vad_segments, audio_quality_*\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation.** VAD marks speech-like regions, not the child.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations.** SNR and noise floor are approximations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-081",
   "metadata": {},
