   "source": [
    "## Section 11 — Linguistic and phonetic intelligence\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research question.** Do expected-vs-produced speech deviations matter?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Motivation.** Phonological processing is central to literacy.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inputs.** item_master, audio (ASR optional)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Methodology.** Local G2P complexity features; optional licensed local ASR with word/char/phone alignment, confidences, CTC expected likelihood, confusions.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Configuration.** `enable_linguistic_features, enable_phonetic_analysis, enable_asr, asr_models`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs.** item_linguistic_features, clip_phonetic_features\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation.** ASR disagreement is an uncertain proxy.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations.** Child-speech ASR error rates are high."
